{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"DEV='Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701'; rg -n 'AIHub|connect\\\\(|onStart|onMessage|send|report|ready|onState|onSession|onClose' \\\"\"'$DEV/hub/session.js\" | head -100; sed -n '\"'1,180p' \\\"\"'$DEV/hub/session.js\"; rg -n '\"'AIHub|onStart|onMessage|send|report|ready' \\\"\"'$DEV/hub/harness.html\" | head -100; rg -n '\"'canvas|window.gameGlue|loadGame|id=\\\"msg\\\"|</body>' \\\"\"'$DEV/engine/web/index.html\"; sed -n '\"'1,200p' \\\"\"'$DEV/engine/scripts/build-web.sh\"; sed -n '\"'55,190p' PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"4:  if (root.AIHub) return;\n36:    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n150:   * empty storage stays: the game has read it already, and what it writes\n165:  var reported = false;\n180:    if (root.console) root.console.warn('[AIHub] ' + text);\n227:  function onMessage(event) {\n235:      // Every field the hub sends is kept, so a newer hub can add one without a newer client.\n303:    root.addEventListener('message', onMessage);\n320:  /** Everything is loaded: at once when info.splash, otherwise from the player's ready gesture. */\n321:  hub.ready = function () {\n324:    post('ready', {});\n327:  /** On the game's own card (connect({ card: true })): this player is 'ready', or asks for 'more' time (again takes it back). */\n330:    if (what !== 'ready' && what !== 'more') return warn('answer is ready or more');\n352:  hub.send = function (data, opts) {\n359:      warn('send: data is not JSON');\n364:      warn('send: message over ' + limits.maxBytes + ' bytes dropped');\n371:      warn('send: over ' + limits.ratePerS + ' messages a second, dropped');\n377:    post('send', fields);\n422:  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\n424:    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\n433:    reported = true;\n438:  /** Versus and co-op: the host reports the standings once, best first, ties grouped: [[2], [0, 3], [1]]. */\n440:    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\n445:    reported = true;\n449:  function sendProgress() {\n451:    if (!nextProgress || ended || reported) return;\n459:    if (!welcomed || ended || reported || !p || !finite(p.score)) return;\n463:    if (wait <= 0) sendProgress();\n464:    else if (!progressTimer) progressTimer = setTimeout(sendProgress, wait);\n487:  root.AIHub = hub;\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\n      },\n    };\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\n    return new Proxy(api, {\n      get: function (t, k) {\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\n      },\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\n        return true;\n      },\n      has: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data || k in t;\n      },\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\n        delete data[k];\n        return true;\n      },\n      ownKeys: function () {\n        return Object.keys(data);\n      },\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\n  function generator(a) {\n    return function () {\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n      var t = a;\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n    };\n  }\n\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\n  if (hub.active) {\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\n      try {\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\n      } catch (e) {\n        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\n  var seededRandom = null;\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\n    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\n    hub.seeded = true;\n  }\n\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\n    var asks = function (on) {\n      return function () {\n        post('fullscreen', { on: on });\n        return Promise.resolve();\n      };\n    };\n    var proto = root.Element.prototype;\n    proto.requestFullscreen = proto.webkitRequestFullscreen = asks(true);\n    root.document.exitFullscreen = root.document.webkitExitFullscreen = asks(false);\n    var shown = function () {\n      return fullscreenOn ? root.document.documentElement || null : null;\n    };\n    try {\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'fullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'webkitFullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n    } catch (e) {}\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * No hub after all: play on, with Math.random the page's own again. The\n   * empty storage stays: the game has read it already, and what it writes\n   * must never land on the player's real saves.\n   */\n  function standAlone() {\n    hub.active = false;\n    if (seededRandom && Math.random === seededRandom) Math.random = realRandom;\n    hub.seeded = false;\n  }\n\n  var origin = '*';\n  var welcomed = false;\n  var ended = false;\n  var connecting = null;\n  var goAt = null;\n  var sentReady = false;\n  var reported = false;\n  var handlers = {};\n  var pending = {};\n  var tokens = limits.burst;\n  var refilled = now();\n  var probeFn = null;\n  var lastProgress = -Infinity;\n  var nextProgress = null;\n  var progressTimer = null;\n\n  function now() {\n    return root.performance && root.performance.now ? root.performance.now() : Date.now();\n  }\n\n  function warn(text) {\n    if (root.console) root.console.warn('[AIHub] ' + text);\n181:  const state = { round, n, metas, mode, limitMs, seed, players, cells: [], hubEnd, status: null, record: null, hidden: false, splashUntil: performance.now() + SPLASH_MS, answers: { ready: new Set(), more: new Set() } };\n194:    deliver: (key, m) => hubEnd.send(key, { k: 'h', r: round, m }),\n202:  hubEnd.onMessage((from, env) => {\n239:      onProgress: (id, report) => {\n241:        cell.progress.push({ at: performance.now(), ...report });\n242:        state.coordinator.progress(id, report.score);\n246:    endpoint.onMessage((from, env) => cell.bridge.fromNet(from, env));\n272:/** A game's own card, as the hub drives it: the countdown and who is ready, to every copy that shows one. */\n275:  const ready = state.cells.filter((c) => state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => c.bridge.me);\n278:    const card = { left, paused: false, starting: left === null, ready, asking: state.answers.more.size, asked: state.answers.more.has(cell.key) };\n289:  const { ready, more } = state.answers;\n290:  if (what === 'ready') {\n291:    ready.add(cell.key);\n297:    ready.delete(cell.key);\n302:  if (!auto && players.every((c) => ready.has(c.key))) return releaseRound(state);\n340:    else if (p.ready) bits.push('ready');\n411:  const report = { done: false, pass: false, game: $('game').value, players: Number($('players').value), scenario, checks, log: logLines };\n412:  window.__hubCheck = report;\n440:    // The card collects ready: every game readies up by itself once loaded, with no prompt and no key.\n441:    const loaded = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.ready), 20_000);\n442:    check('ready without a key press (the card asks the players)', loaded, copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\n448:      const answered = await until(() => players.every((c) => state.answers.ready.has(c.key)), 3000);\n449:      check('its own card: Enter answers Ready', sent && answered, players.filter((c) => !state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => `${c.key}${c.cardSent ? '' : ' (no card yet)'}`).join(', '));\n453:    check('the round starts when the card ends', started && copies().every((p) => p.ready), copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', ') || state.status?.phase);\n473:      const seeded = state.cells.every((c) => c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.seeded === true);\n474:      check(`${mode}: Math.random is seeded, the same on every copy`, seeded, state.cells.map((c) => `${c.key}: client ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.version ?? '?'} seeded ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.seeded}`).join('; '));\n486:        check('ghost: every copy sends its player', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0) || n === 1,\n489:      if (!legacyRace) check(`${mode}: every copy reports its progress`, remaining.every((c) => c.progress.length > 0 || state.status?.players.find((p) => p.key === c.key)?.result),\n490:        remaining.map((c) => `${c.key}: ${c.progress.length} report${c.progress.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}`).join(', '));\n525:    report.pass = checks.length > 0 && checks.every((c) => c.pass);\n526:    report.done = true;\n528:    log(`conformance: ${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}`);\n19:  /* winit appends the game canvas to <body>; it fills the page and the game follows its size.\n21:  canvas { display: block; width: 100vw !important; height: 100vh !important; height: 100dvh !important;\n34:<div id=\"msg\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">Loading Shardfall…</div>\n45:    // The game hides this message once its canvas exists, and takes keyboard focus.\n47:      const c = document.querySelector('canvas');\n64:      // (scripts/pack_single_html.py) carries both inside the page and sets window.loadGame.\n65:      if (window.loadGame) await window.loadGame();\n74:</body>\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Builds the browser version (WebAssembly + WebGPU). Output: target/web/{index.html,manifest.webmanifest,shardfall.js,shardfall_bg.wasm}\n# Serve that folder over HTTP (e.g. `python3 -m http.server -d target/web`) and open it in Chrome or Edge.\n# --single-file writes only target/web/<title>.html (shardfall.html): one page with the glue and gzipped wasm inside\n#   that runs from file:// or any host (scripts/pack_single_html.py; also --title, --description, --theme-color,\n#   --scene NAME for the start scene when the address names none, --out PATH).\n# Needs: rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown\n#        cargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version <the wasm-bindgen version in Cargo.lock>\nset -euo pipefail\ncaller=$PWD\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\"\nsingle=false\npack=()\nwhile (($#)); do\n\tcase $1 in\n\t--single-file) single=true ;;\n\t--title | --description | --theme-color | --scene | --out)\n\t\t(($# > 1)) || { echo \"build-web.sh: $1 needs a value\" >&2; exit 2; }\n\t\tvalue=$2\n\t\t[[ $1 == --out && $value != /* ]] && value=$caller/$value\n\t\tpack+=(\"$1\" \"$value\")\n\t\tshift\n\t\t;;\n\t*) echo \"build-web.sh: unknown option $1 (options are listed at the top of $0)\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n\tesac\n\tshift\ndone\nif ((${#pack[@]})) && ! $single; then\n\techo \"build-web.sh: ${pack[0]} needs --single-file\" >&2\n\texit 2\nfi\ncargo build --locked --profile dist --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p pav_app\nwasm=${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/wasm32-unknown-unknown/dist/shardfall.wasm\nout=target/web\nif $single; then\n\tbindgen=$(mktemp -d)\n\ttrap 'rm -rf \"$bindgen\"' EXIT\n\twasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \"$bindgen\" --out-name shardfall \"$wasm\"\n\tpython3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py \"$bindgen\" \"${pack[@]}\"\n\texit\nfi\nrm -rf \"$out\"\nmkdir -p \"$out\"\nwasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \"$out\" --out-name shardfall \"$wasm\"\ncp web/index.html web/manifest.webmanifest \"$out/\"\nls -la \"$out\"\n1. Wake on the cabana deck. Pip greets you, with an absence comment if real days have passed.\n2. Morning Wobble Check (about 70 seconds), Balance Age reveal, Pip's comment.\n3. Free time on the island: walk, talk to guests, find lost flip-flops, step on an event mat. The Schedule (Triangle or Tab) lists everything and fast-travels.\n4. When the day's minute goal is met, Pip says so. Sleep at your cabana (or choose End Day in the Schedule). A big stamp lands on the Calendar. Next day.\n\n| Day | Opens | Minute goal | Story beat |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Stillness Studio: Breath Bloom, Pose Parade | 3 | Arrival. The checkout rule. \"Nobody has asked to leave yet\" |\n| 2 | Iron Gazebo: Tempo Squats, Plank Standoff | 5 | Big Kettle. Wardrobe opens |\n| 3 | Boardwalk: Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap | 7 | Yesterday You appears as a ghost. \"I am not comparing you\" |\n| 4 | Lagoon: Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup | 9 | Guests start whispering about the Big Stand |\n| 5 | The Big Stand, after the morning check | none | Finale, ending, free play |\n\n**Minutes:** the first clear of an event each day banks 1 + stars (0 to 3 stars, so 1 to 4 minutes); repeats bank 1. Resort minutes are openly not real minutes (\"Our minutes are longer. It is a wellness thing\").\n\n**Endings:** Balance Age 40 or better: you may check out, by rowboat (`LIB/core/rowboat`). Otherwise: the Extended Stay ending, gentle and funny. Both roll credits, then unlock Free Play: every event open, personal bests, star goals, and a calendar that keeps stamping real days.\n\n**Bot rule:** `Game::bot` must be able to play this entire flow, menus included, from New Stay to the credits. That is your scripted playthrough and the base of attract mode.\n\n## 3. Controls\n\nThe left stick is both walking and leaning. Prompts always show the glyph for the input used last.\n\n| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Walk on the island, lean in events | Left stick | W A S D (arrows also walk) | Island: click a place or thing to walk there. Events: cursor offset from screen centre is the lean |\n| Fine lean | Stick itself | Hold Shift (half key rate) | Small cursor moves |\n| Jog on the island | Hold R2 | Hold Shift | |\n| Action: talk, begin, inhale, squat, bounce | Cross | Space | Left button |\n| Left step / right step | L1 or L2 / R1 or R2 | Q or Left / E or Right | Left button / right button |\n| Brace (hold both) | L2+R2 or L1+R1 | Q+E | Both buttons |\n| Wave at someone | Square | F | |\n| Schedule | Triangle | Tab | |\n| Island camera | Right stick | | Right-drag, wheel zooms |\n| Pause | Options | Esc | |\n| Menus | D-pad or left stick, Cross confirms, Circle backs, L1/R1 change tabs | Arrows or W A S D, Enter or Space, Esc backs, Q/E change tabs | Hover moves focus, click activates, right-click backs |\n\nXbox glyphs (Settings option) swap A B X Y, LB RB LT RT, Menu. Ignore Options while Create is held: that pair belongs to the AI Hub. Disable the engine's own keys (F1 to F10, digits, H, Backspace rewind, right-drag tilt) outside dev mode. Keep F11 for fullscreen.\n\n## 4. The Balance Core\n\nOne struct, `BalanceCore`, used by every event. Its state is `cob` (the dot, unit disc, x right, y up on screen) and `vel`.\n\n```\ntarget = shaped lean input * reach + wobble(t)\nacc    = (target - cob) * stiffness - vel * damping + gust + nudge\nvel   += acc * dt\ncob   += vel * dt\ntip    = |cob| > 1 for tip_time seconds\n```\n\nStart with `stiffness 40`, `damping 8.5`, `reach 0.92`, `tip_time 0.35`. `wobble` is `amp * (0.7 * sin(2*pi*1.3*t + a) + 0.3 * sin(2*pi*2.9*t + b))` per axis, phases from `sim.state.rng`, base `amp 0.12`, scaled per event and by fatigue, plus a velocity kick of 0.1 units/s in a random direction every 1 to 2 seconds. Use sim time, never the clock.\n\n**Feel targets** (these numbers give them, by numeric simulation at 60 ticks/s): full stick reaches 90% in about 0.4 s with about 5% overshoot, like a body. Release settles in about 0.45 s. Left alone, the dot wanders at a mean radius of 0.05, at most 0.08. A held full lean does not tip by itself; a gust on top of it does.\n\n**Input shaping** (in `pav_app`, passed as `InputFrame.lean`, screen space):\n- **Stick:** deadzone 0.12, response curve `x^1.5` so small motions are fine.\n- **Keyboard:** keys move the target at 1.6 units/s and it returns at 1.2 units/s when released. Tapping gives small nudges, so keys feel native, not bang-bang.\n- **Mouse:** cursor offset from the screen centre divided by 0.38 of the window height, clamped to the disc. No pointer lock. The device moved last wins.\n\n**Body:** the figure tilts with the dot (`cob * 14` degrees about the feet, engine change in section 14). Beyond |cob| 0.75 an upper-body arm-flail clip fades in. A tip plays a stumble and, over water, a splash. Tips never end the game; they cost time or score.\n\n**HUD, the Puck:** a large circular gauge drawn in egui: a pale disc, a green target ring, a coral dot, and stars at the edge when streaking. It must read from 10 feet. It looks good at 340 px diameter at 1080p (verified). Put it top centre or bottom centre, whichever does not cover the figure in that event.\n\n## 5. Events\n\n**Common frame:** event card (name, one-sentence goal, glyph prompts, one coach line), 3-2-1, play, result (score 0 to 1000, stars at 400, 650 and 850, a deadpan Title, minutes banked, personal best, difference from Yesterday You; Retry or Back).\n\n**Every event has:** a section of tunable numbers in `rules.toml`, a bot that earns at least 2 stars, an idle-input outcome below 1 star, a ghost lane, and an attract segment. Scenes `fit/event/<name>` start an event directly, for tools and tests.\n\n### Stillness Studio (Posey). Set: `studio`, a round white deck on a calm dawn lagoon. Camera: mirror view (yaw 0, tilt 12, distance 8.5, fov 36; the figure faces +Z, toward the camera, and stick right is screen right).\n\n**Breath Bloom** (45 s). Hold Action to inhale, release to exhale, following a guide ring: 4 s in, 4 s out, 5 cycles, the last one longer. `lungs` rises while held and falls when not. Keep the dot inside a centre ring of radius 0.35. Tick score: `0.7 * (1 - clamp(|lungs - guide| / 0.35)) + 0.3 * inRing`. Each good cycle opens a lotus on the water with a rising pentatonic chime; a perfect run blooms the whole pond. Scrub the clip `FIT/Breath` by `lungs`. No fail state. Bot: holds while the guide rises.\n\n**Pose Parade** (3 poses, 20 s each). Six hand-keyed poses with deadpan names: the Patient Heron, the Apologetic Lunge, the Tired Lighthouse, the Folded Deck Chair, the Reluctant Bridge, Seated Disappointment. Day 1 uses the first three. Posey holds the pose beside you. A target ring (radius 0.30 shrinking to 0.18) drifts on a slow Lissajous path (amplitude 0.35, 0.12 Hz). Inside the ring a streak multiplier climbs x1 to x4, one step per 2 s; leaving resets it. At 12 s of pose 2 a gull lands on your head and wobble is x1.6 for 5 s (\"There is a bird on you. Accept the bird\"). A tip breaks the pose for 1.5 s. Score: time in ring weighted by multiplier. Bot: PD toward the ring centre.\n\n### Iron Gazebo (Big Kettle). Set: `gazebo`, a white iron gazebo at golden hour. Camera: 3/4 front.\n\n**Tempo Squats** (10 reps, about 50 s). Hold Action to go down (2 s to full depth), release to rise (1 s). A guide bar shows the tempo; a low bell marks the bottom. Keep the dot in a band |x| < 0.25; wobble grows 8% per rep. Rep score: `0.7 * timing + 0.3 * band`. Scrub `FIT/Squat` by depth. Gag: rep 10 is followed by \"Ten. Also eleven.\" Bot: follows the guide.\n\n**Plank Standoff** (up to 60 s). Hold Brace and keep the dot in a ring shrinking from 0.40 to 0.20. Releasing, or leaving the ring for more than 1 s, collapses you in a comic flop. Fatigue ramps wobble; at 30 s add tremble; at 45 s Kettle laughs at his own joke and the nudge shakes the screen. Score: seconds survived / 60. Stars at 25, 40 and 55 s. Kettle, who has no arms, plank-talks you through it. Base the pose on one frame of `MESH2MOTION/Pushup`. Bot: survives at least 45 s.\n\n### Boardwalk (Bounce). Set: `boardwalk`, a beach boardwalk at bright midday.\n\n**Step Party** (64 s, 96 BPM, song 4). A rhythm game: notes in two lanes fall to two footprints, left, right or both, on an aerobic step box. Perfect within 55 ms, Good within 120 ms. About 100 notes, data in `charts.toml`, starting with quarter notes and building to eighths and doubles. Bounce bounces on the beat and guests clap on downbeats. Timing uses the audio clock (section 10). Camera: mirror view, slightly high. Bot: presses exactly on each note.\n\n**Floatie Spin** (50 s). Circle the lean (stick, mouse, or rolling W-D-S-A) to spin inflatable rings around your hips. Spin speed is the smoothed angular velocity of the lean while |lean| > 0.4; the sweet band is 6 to 9 rad/s, and a `spin_band_scale` rule widens it for keyboard. \"Switch!\" flips the required direction every 15 s. Guests toss new rings from left or right: press that side's step within 0.25 s of arrival to catch it. Out of band, rings sink; on the floor they are lost. Maximum 7 rings. Score: rings times time in band. Rings are no-physics entities positioned in code. Bot: 7.5 rad/s circle, presses on arrivals.\n\n**Morning Lap** (about 90 s, one lap of the hub island). Alternate left and right steps to set your pace (1.6 to 2.4 steps/s is the zone). Too fast raises a stitch meter that makes you stumble; too slow and Bounce, the pacer rolling ahead, gets away. The path steers you; lean moves you up to 1.2 m sideways to dodge crabs, sunbathers and towels and to grab ribbons. Flip-flops can be found here too. Score: time in zone, plus ribbons, minus bumps. Camera: chase with per-tick yaw. Use `MESH2MOTION/Jog` scaled to speed. Bot: 2 steps/s, steers to ribbons.\n\n### Lagoon (Commodore Gull). Sets: `tide`, `channel`, `pier`, `tower`.\n\n**Tide Table** (3 boards, 60 s total). You stand on a floating square raft and your lean tilts it. Roll hermit crabs in shells into tide pools. Board 1: 3 shells. Board 2: 5 shells and a moving pool. Board 3: 7 shells, bumpers and a rising tide. Fast shells skip over pools. Write the shell physics as simple 2D code (`a = tilt * g - friction * v`, wall bounce 0.5), not rapier: it is more tunable and bot-friendly. Score: shells potted plus time left. Camera: high 3/4 (tilt 62). Bot: PD steering of the nearest shell toward the nearest pool.\n\n**Paddle Slalom** (about 45 s). Stand on a paddleboard on a long channel and pass buoy gates. Lean x steers. Lean forward speeds up and risks tipping, lean back brakes. Gusts, shown as ripple streaks, push the dot. A tip is a big splash and a 2 s remount. A missed gate adds 2 s. `score = clamp((1.6 * par - t) / (0.8 * par)) * 1000`. Standing on water uses the trick in section 15; a silent `Wake` event every few ticks draws the wake. Camera: chase (tilt 22, distance 10). Bot: steers to gate centres at forward lean 0.5.\n\n**Tray Trek** (about 50 s). Walk a long pier at a fixed pace, carrying a tray with a stack of 5 smoothies. Waves, plank gaps and swooping gulls jolt the tray. Your dot tilts it. Glasses slide with tilt and plop into the sea past the edge. Score: 200 per glass delivered, plus a no-spill bonus. Marjorie receives what is left and comments. Use `STYLE100/Balance_Walk` plus an upper-body `FIT/CarryTray` clip. Bot: counters the jolts it knows are coming.\n\n**Cannonball Cup** (3 dives, about 40 s). The board bounces with a 1.2 s period. Press Action at the bottom of 3 bounces to build power, the 4th press leaps. In the air, hold Action to tuck and lean to rotate. Enter tucked and high for the biggest splash. Three gull judges hold up cards: \"6.5\", \"7\", \"See me\". \"We are not here for form. We are here for splash.\" Score: height x tuck x timing. Camera: side view (yaw 90, tilt 6, distance 14). The splash must be huge: a new `BigSplash` event scales the water dents and particles. This is the attract mode's hero shot. Bot: presses on bottoms, tucks at the apex.\n\n### The Big Stand (finale, about 2.5 minutes). Set: `bay`, a tiny post in the bay at sunset, with the whole cast watching from rafts.\n\nFive phases, reusing event code with new numbers:\n1. Breathing, 4 cycles.\n2. A pose under rising gusts, 20 s.\n3. Step Party for 16 bars with a marching band of guests, wobble on.\n4. Brace while waves crash, 20 s.\n5. **The Long Stillness:** 30 s of nothing. Music fades to silence, the HUD vanishes except the Puck. At 15 s a fake prompt offers \"Press Cross to skip\". Pressing anything forfeits the Inner Peace bonus. Then Pip, quietly: \"...Oh. You're still here. Good.\"\n\nA tip drops you in the sea to a groan from the crowd and puts you back; it costs score and cannot end the run. Final Balance Age = morning age minus `final_score / 100` (up to 10).\n\n### Morning Wobble Check. Set: `studio`. About 70 s, four micro-tests, Pip presiding.\n\n| Test | What you do | Metric (0 to 1) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Stand Still (\"This is the whole test\") | Hold the dot centred for 8 s; one small nudge at 5 s | Mean distance from centre |\n| Lean Targets | A left/right bar: reach \"70% left\", then two more targets, within 6%, hold 1.5 s; 5 s limit each | Time taken |\n| Eyes Closed | 6 s. The screen dims to almost black, the Puck vanishes. A tone's pitch tells your offset, and rumble if the pad has it | Mean distance |\n| Step Test | 8 alternating steps to a 100 BPM metronome | Timing |\n\n```\nskill = 0.30*still + 0.25*targets + 0.25*blind + 0.20*steps\nage   = 24 + 56 * (1 - skill)^1.1 - 2*days_completed - min(total_stars/3, 8)\n```\nClamp to 18..99, round. A middling player (skill 0.5) starts at 50 and reaches about 34 by Day 5; a weak one (skill 0.2) starts at 68 and ends near 52, before the finale's bonus. The big number rolls like a slot machine. Pip's comment is chosen by the change since yesterday and by the worst metric. A sparkline of 5 big dots shows the week. Your figure's posture improves as the age falls (a small constant forward slump through the tilt field, shrinking each day): visible progress, no numbers needed.\n\n## 6. Meta systems\n\n- **Minute Clam:** a giant clam at reception that gulps banked minutes with a gibberish burp. Totals unlock wardrobe items.\n- **Calendar:** five big days, a stamp per completed day, then real days in free play. No tables.\n- **Titles:** after each event Pip awards a deadpan title by score: Human Soup, Acceptable Human, Certified Lean-To, Wobble Enthusiast, Seasoned Tilter, Stillness Intern, Professional Standing Person, Alarmingly Balanced. At least 30, in `script.toml`.\n- **Wardrobe:** reuse the engine's `GearLook`, which needs no new drawing (verified): `helm = cap` (sun cap), `helm = hood` (towel turban), `crown`, `halo`; `gloves` (sweatbands), `belt`, `pauldrons` (reads as arm floaties, funny). Plus shirt, pants and shoe colours. Skip `cape`: it draws long sticks.\n- **Lost flip-flops:** 5 hidden on the island, for Two-Towel Tom. Reward: Golden Flip-Flops (gold shoes) and a line. This is the exploration layer.\n- **Yesterday You:** your best run of each event is recorded and replayed as a tinted figure in a neighbouring lane, from Day 3.\n- **Absence comments:** the page passes today's date to the game at boot, and the save stores the last day played. \"You were away for 2 days. I did not count them. There were 2.\" Passing the date in as data keeps the rule that the sim never reads the clock.\n- **Saves:** versioned JSON in `localStorage`: guest slots (name, look, day, minutes, stars, bests, ghosts, ages, flip-flops, unlocks) and global settings. Save on every change of day and every result.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"reasoning","text":"**Inspecting hub lines**"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"DEV='Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701'; sed -n '200,490p' \\\"\"'$DEV/hub/session.js\"; rg -n '\"'AIHub|onStart|onMessage|send\\\\(|finish\\\\(|ready\\\\(' \\\"\"'$DEV/hub/harness.html\"; rg -n '\"'canvas|gameGlue|loadGame|id=\\\"msg\\\"|</body>' \\\"\"'$DEV/engine/web/index.html\"; rg -n '\"'LOADER|</body>|replace_one|theme-color|description' \\\"\"'$DEV/engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py\"; sed -n '\"'1,150p' \\\"\"'$DEV/engine/scripts/build-web.sh\"; sed -n '\"'1,240p' \\\"\"'$DEV/hub/round.js\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"DEV='Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701'; sed -n '200,490p' \\\"\"'$DEV/hub/session.js\"; rg -n '\"'AIHub|onStart|onMessage|send\\\\(|finish\\\\(|ready\\\\(' \\\"\"'$DEV/hub/harness.html\"; rg -n '\"'canvas|gameGlue|loadGame|id=\\\"msg\\\"|</body>' \\\"\"'$DEV/engine/web/index.html\"; rg -n '\"'LOADER|</body>|replace_one|theme-color|description' \\\"\"'$DEV/engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py\"; sed -n '\"'1,150p' \\\"\"'$DEV/engine/scripts/build-web.sh\"; sed -n '\"'1,240p' \\\"\"'$DEV/hub/round.js\"'","aggregated_output":"  function post(type, fields) {\n    var msg = { aihub: 1, type: type };\n    for (var key in fields) if (own(fields, key)) msg[key] = fields[key];\n    try {\n      root.parent.postMessage(msg, origin);\n    } catch (e) {\n      warn('could not reach the hub: ' + e.message);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function emit(type, args) {\n    var list = handlers[type];\n    if (!list || !list.length || pending[type]) {\n      (pending[type] = pending[type] || []).push(args);\n      return;\n    }\n    for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\n      try {\n        list[i].apply(null, args);\n      } catch (e) {\n        setTimeout(function () {\n          throw e;\n        });\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  function onMessage(event) {\n    if (event.source !== root.parent) return;\n    var m = event.data;\n    if (!m || m.aihub !== 1 || typeof m.type !== 'string') return;\n    if (m.type === 'welcome') {\n      if (welcomed) return;\n      welcomed = true;\n      origin = event.origin && event.origin !== 'null' ? event.origin : '*';\n      // Every field the hub sends is kept, so a newer hub can add one without a newer client.\n      for (var key in m) {\n        if (!own(m, key) || KEEP[key] || typeof hub[key] === 'function') continue;\n        hub[key] = m[key];\n      }\n      hub.players = (m.players || []).slice();\n      hub.seed = m.seed >>> 0;\n      hub.isHost = m.me === m.host;\n      hub.splash = m.splash === true;\n      if (m.limits) {\n        for (var l in limits) if (own(limits, l) && Number(m.limits[l]) > 0) limits[l] = Number(m.limits[l]);\n        tokens = limits.burst;\n      }\n      if (connecting) connecting.resolve(info());\n      return;\n    }\n    if (m.type === 'fullscreen') {\n      fullscreenOn = m.on === true;\n      try {\n        root.document.dispatchEvent(new root.Event('fullscreenchange'));\n      } catch (e) {}\n      return;\n    }\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return;\n    if (m.type === 'start') {\n      goAt = now() + Number(m.in || 0);\n      emit('start', [{ in: Number(m.in || 0) }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'message') {\n      emit('message', [m.data, m.from]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'leave') {\n      hub.players = hub.players.filter(function (p) {\n        return p.id !== m.id;\n      });\n      emit('leave', [{ id: m.id, reason: m.reason }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'time-up') {\n      emit('time-up', [{ graceMs: m.graceMs }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'end') {\n      ended = true;\n      if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\n      emit('end', [{ reason: m.reason, standings: m.standings || null }]);\n    } else {\n      // An event this client has never heard of: hand it on as it came.\n      var detail = {};\n      for (var k in m) if (own(m, k) && k !== 'aihub' && k !== 'type') detail[k] = m[k];\n      emit(m.type, [detail]);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function info() {\n    var out = {};\n    for (var key in hub) if (own(hub, key) && typeof hub[key] !== 'function' && !KEEP[key]) out[key] = hub[key];\n    out.players = hub.players.slice();\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  /** Join the session. Resolves with the round's info, or null when there is no hub: play normally. */\n  hub.connect = function (opts) {\n    if (connecting) return connecting.promise;\n    var done;\n    var promise = new Promise(function (resolve) {\n      done = resolve;\n    });\n    connecting = { promise: promise, resolve: done };\n    if (!hub.active) {\n      done(null);\n      return promise;\n    }\n    opts = opts || {};\n    root.addEventListener('message', onMessage);\n    var started = now();\n    var hello = function () {\n      if (welcomed) return;\n      if (now() - started > HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS) {\n        standAlone();\n        warn('no hub answered; playing normally');\n        done(null);\n        return;\n      }\n      post('hello', { v: 1, client: VERSION, mode: opts.mode || null, seats: opts.seats || null, card: opts.card === true });\n      setTimeout(hello, HELLO_EVERY_MS);\n    };\n    hello();\n    return promise;\n  };\n\n  /** Everything is loaded: at once when info.splash, otherwise from the player's ready gesture. */\n  hub.ready = function () {\n    if (!welcomed || sentReady || ended) return;\n    sentReady = true;\n    post('ready', {});\n  };\n\n  /** On the game's own card (connect({ card: true })): this player is 'ready', or asks for 'more' time (again takes it back). */\n  hub.answer = function (what) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || goAt !== null) return;\n    if (what !== 'ready' && what !== 'more') return warn('answer is ready or more');\n    post('answer', { answer: what });\n  };\n\n  hub.on = function (type, fn) {\n    (handlers[type] = handlers[type] || []).push(fn);\n    if (pending[type] && !pending[type].flushing) {\n      pending[type].flushing = true;\n      setTimeout(function () {\n        var queued = pending[type];\n        delete pending[type];\n        for (var i = 0; i < queued.length; i++) emit(type, queued[i]);\n      });\n    }\n    return function () {\n      var list = handlers[type] || [];\n      var at = list.indexOf(fn);\n      if (at !== -1) list.splice(at, 1);\n    };\n  };\n\n  /** Send JSON data to every other player, or to one with {to: id}. {reliable: false} may drop or reorder. */\n  hub.send = function (data, opts) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return false;\n    opts = opts || {};\n    var text;\n    try {\n      text = JSON.stringify(data);\n    } catch (e) {\n      warn('send: data is not JSON');\n      return false;\n    }\n    if (text === undefined) return false;\n    if (text.length > limits.maxBytes) {\n      warn('send: message over ' + limits.maxBytes + ' bytes dropped');\n      return false;\n    }\n    var t = now();\n    tokens = Math.min(limits.burst, tokens + ((t - refilled) / 1000) * limits.ratePerS);\n    refilled = t;\n    if (tokens < 1) {\n      warn('send: over ' + limits.ratePerS + ' messages a second, dropped');\n      return false;\n    }\n    tokens -= 1;\n    var fields = { data: JSON.parse(text), reliable: opts.reliable !== false };\n    if (opts.to !== undefined && opts.to !== null) fields.to = opts.to;\n    post('send', fields);\n    return true;\n  };\n\n  /** Milliseconds since the synchronized start: negative during the countdown, -Infinity before start. */\n  hub.time = function () {\n    return goAt === null ? -Infinity : now() - goAt;\n  };\n\n  /** A seeded random number generator (0 ≤ n < 1), the same sequence on every device for the same label. */\n  hub.rng = function (label) {\n    var h = 2166136261;\n    var s = String(label === undefined ? '' : label);\n    for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n      h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\n      h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\n    }\n    return generator((hub.seed ^ h) >>> 0);\n  };\n\n  /** A number the hub can rank: finite, given as a number or as text. Not null, '' or true, which JSON or Number would make 0. */\n  function finite(v) {\n    return (typeof v === 'number' || (typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '')) && isFinite(v);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * The whole outcome as plain JSON, field by field: the hub checks and trims\n   * it, so new optional fields need no new client. A field that is not JSON\n   * (a cycle, a BigInt) is left out, not the whole outcome.\n   */\n  function outcomeOf(outcome) {\n    if (!outcome || typeof outcome !== 'object' || Array.isArray(outcome)) {\n      warn('the outcome is not a plain object');\n      return null;\n    }\n    var copy = {};\n    for (var key in outcome) {\n      if (!own(outcome, key)) continue;\n      var value = json(outcome[key]);\n      if (value !== undefined) copy[key] = value;\n      else if (outcome[key] !== undefined) warn('the outcome\\'s ' + key + ' is not JSON: left out');\n    }\n    return copy;\n  }\n\n  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\n  hub.result = function (outcome) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\n    if (!fields) return;\n    var given = outcome || {};\n    delete fields.time;\n    delete fields.score;\n    if (finite(given.time)) fields.time = Number(given.time);\n    if (finite(given.score)) fields.score = Number(given.score);\n    if (!own(fields, 'time') && !own(fields, 'score')) return warn('result needs a finite time or score');\n    reported = true;\n    if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\n    post('result', fields);\n  };\n\n  /** Versus and co-op: the host reports the standings once, best first, ties grouped: [[2], [0, 3], [1]]. */\n  hub.finish = function (outcome) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\n    if (!hub.isHost) return warn('finish is for the host only');\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\n    if (!fields) return;\n    if (!Array.isArray(fields.standings)) return warn('finish needs standings');\n    reported = true;\n    post('finish', fields);\n  };\n\n  function sendProgress() {\n    progressTimer = null;\n    if (!nextProgress || ended || reported) return;\n    lastProgress = now();\n    post('progress', nextProgress);\n    nextProgress = null;\n  }\n\n  /** Your standing during play, for the hub's scoreboard: {score, label}. Call it as often as you like; the hub hears it about once a second. */\n  hub.progress = function (p) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported || !p || !finite(p.score)) return;\n    nextProgress = { score: Number(p.score) };\n    if (p.label != null) nextProgress.label = String(p.label).slice(0, 24);\n    var wait = lastProgress + PROGRESS_EVERY_MS - now();\n    if (wait <= 0) sendProgress();\n    else if (!progressTimer) progressTimer = setTimeout(sendProgress, wait);\n  };\n\n  /** For the harness, in or out of a session: fn() → { scene, menu, world, input }, read with inspect(). */\n  hub.probe = function (fn) {\n    probeFn = typeof fn === 'function' ? fn : null;\n  };\n\n  hub.inspect = function () {\n    if (!probeFn) return null;\n    try {\n      return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(probeFn()));\n    } catch (e) {\n      return { error: String((e && e.message) || e) };\n    }\n  };\n\n  /** The game cannot run here (no WebGL, failed load): the hub skips it. */\n  hub.fail = function (message) {\n    if (!hub.active) return;\n    post('error', { message: String(message || 'error').slice(0, 500), fatal: true });\n  };\n\n  root.AIHub = hub;\n})(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis);\n194:    deliver: (key, m) => hubEnd.send(key, { k: 'h', r: round, m }),\n202:  hubEnd.onMessage((from, env) => {\n246:    endpoint.onMessage((from, env) => cell.bridge.fromNet(from, env));\n473:      const seeded = state.cells.every((c) => c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.seeded === true);\n474:      check(`${mode}: Math.random is seeded, the same on every copy`, seeded, state.cells.map((c) => `${c.key}: client ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.version ?? '?'} seeded ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.seeded}`).join('; '));\n19:  /* winit appends the game canvas to <body>; it fills the page and the game follows its size.\n21:  canvas { display: block; width: 100vw !important; height: 100vh !important; height: 100dvh !important;\n34:<div id=\"msg\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">Loading Shardfall…</div>\n45:    // The game hides this message once its canvas exists, and takes keyboard focus.\n47:      const c = document.querySelector('canvas');\n64:      // (scripts/pack_single_html.py) carries both inside the page and sets window.loadGame.\n65:      if (window.loadGame) await window.loadGame();\n74:</body>\n4:usage: python3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py BINDGEN_DIR [--title T] [--description D]\n5:           [--theme-color C] [--scene NAME] [--out PATH]\n9:its <title>, <meta name=description> and <meta name=theme-color> (left as they are when not\n10:given), the manifest link dropped, and, before </body>, the gzipped wasm as base64 text, a\n29:LOADER = \"\"\"\n82:def replace_one(page, pattern, make, what):\n91:    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split(\"\\n\")[0])\n94:    ap.add_argument(\"--description\", help=\"<meta name=description> (default: index.html's)\")\n95:    ap.add_argument(\"--theme-color\", help=\"<meta name=theme-color> (default: index.html's)\")\n117:        page = replace_one(page, r\"<title>[^<]*</title>\", lambda m: f\"<title>{html.escape(a.title)}</title>\", \"<title>\")\n118:    for name, value in ((\"description\", a.description), (\"theme-color\", a.theme_color)):\n120:            page = replace_one(\n127:    page = replace_one(page, r'[ \\t]*<link rel=\"manifest\"[^>]*>\\n', lambda m: \"\", \"manifest link\")\n132:    loader = LOADER.replace(\"__SCENE__\", json.dumps(a.scene or None).replace(\"<\", \"\\\\u003c\"))\n139:    page = replace_one(page, r\"</body>\", lambda m: tail + \"</body>\", \"</body>\")\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Builds the browser version (WebAssembly + WebGPU). Output: target/web/{index.html,manifest.webmanifest,shardfall.js,shardfall_bg.wasm}\n# Serve that folder over HTTP (e.g. `python3 -m http.server -d target/web`) and open it in Chrome or Edge.\n# --single-file writes only target/web/<title>.html (shardfall.html): one page with the glue and gzipped wasm inside\n#   that runs from file:// or any host (scripts/pack_single_html.py; also --title, --description, --theme-color,\n#   --scene NAME for the start scene when the address names none, --out PATH).\n# Needs: rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown\n#        cargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version <the wasm-bindgen version in Cargo.lock>\nset -euo pipefail\ncaller=$PWD\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\"\nsingle=false\npack=()\nwhile (($#)); do\n\tcase $1 in\n\t--single-file) single=true ;;\n\t--title | --description | --theme-color | --scene | --out)\n\t\t(($# > 1)) || { echo \"build-web.sh: $1 needs a value\" >&2; exit 2; }\n\t\tvalue=$2\n\t\t[[ $1 == --out && $value != /* ]] && value=$caller/$value\n\t\tpack+=(\"$1\" \"$value\")\n\t\tshift\n\t\t;;\n\t*) echo \"build-web.sh: unknown option $1 (options are listed at the top of $0)\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n\tesac\n\tshift\ndone\nif ((${#pack[@]})) && ! $single; then\n\techo \"build-web.sh: ${pack[0]} needs --single-file\" >&2\n\texit 2\nfi\ncargo build --locked --profile dist --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p pav_app\nwasm=${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/wasm32-unknown-unknown/dist/shardfall.wasm\nout=target/web\nif $single; then\n\tbindgen=$(mktemp -d)\n\ttrap 'rm -rf \"$bindgen\"' EXIT\n\twasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \"$bindgen\" --out-name shardfall \"$wasm\"\n\tpython3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py \"$bindgen\" \"${pack[@]}\"\n\texit\nfi\nrm -rf \"$out\"\nmkdir -p \"$out\"\nwasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \"$out\" --out-name shardfall \"$wasm\"\ncp web/index.html web/manifest.webmanifest \"$out/\"\nls -la \"$out\"\n/**\n * round.js — one round of an AI Hub session, run by the hub that coordinates\n * it (the harness page, or the session host's tab).\n *\n * It never touches the network or a frame itself: every message for a game\n * goes out through `deliver(key, msg)`, and everything the games report comes\n * in through `receive(key, msg)` and `leave(key, reason)`. The clock is\n * injected, so `scripts/hub.test.mjs` can walk a round through every timeout\n * without waiting for one.\n *\n * Players are known by `key` (whatever the session calls them); games see\n * contiguous ids 0..N-1 in slot order.\n */\n\nexport const TIMINGS = Object.freeze({\n  helloMs: 10_000,\n  readyMs: 45_000,\n  /** Gated rounds: a game still loading when the hub releases the round gets this long more. */\n  loadGraceMs: 20_000,\n  countdownMs: 3_000,\n  graceMs: 5_000,\n  hiddenMs: 20_000,\n  maxRoundMs: 15 * 60_000,\n});\n\n/** P1 red, P2 blue, P3 green, P4 yellow: the colour follows the seat. */\nexport const SLOT_COLORS = Object.freeze(['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700']);\n\nexport const MODES = Object.freeze(['parallel', 'ghost', 'shared-world']);\n\n/** Each mode's name on screen. */\nexport const MODE_NAMES = Object.freeze({ parallel: 'Parallel', ghost: 'Ghost', 'shared-world': 'Shared world' });\n\n/** Older tags, still played: race as ghost, co-op and versus as a shared world. */\nconst MODE_ALIASES = Object.freeze({ race: 'ghost', 'co-op': 'shared-world', versus: 'shared-world' });\n\n/** The mode a tag or a hello names, older tags included; null for anything else. */\nexport function modeOf(word) {\n  const w = String(word ?? '').trim().toLowerCase();\n  return MODES.includes(w) ? w : (MODE_ALIASES[w] ?? null);\n}\n\n/** Modes where every copy runs its own world: each reports its own result, and nothing depends on a host. */\nexport const SELF_REPORTED = Object.freeze(['parallel', 'ghost']);\n\n/**\n * Whether a game's round carries the seed in its address, so the client seeds\n * Math.random and every copy starts the same: read from the game's own tag,\n * parallel or ghost. A game still tagged race was built for an unseeded start\n * (ids it makes from Math.random must differ between its copies), so it keeps one.\n */\nexport const seedsRandom = (tag) => ['parallel', 'ghost'].includes(String(tag ?? '').trim().toLowerCase());\n\nconst REAL_CLOCK = {\n  now: () => Date.now(),\n  setTimeout: (fn, ms) => setTimeout(fn, ms),\n  clearTimeout: (handle) => clearTimeout(handle),\n};\n\n/** A round's hard cap: half again its declared length, never past 15 minutes; the longest when it declares none. */\nexport function limitFor(minutes, { maxRoundMs = TIMINGS.maxRoundMs } = {}) {\n  const typical = Number(minutes);\n  if (!(typical > 0)) return maxRoundMs;\n  return Math.min(maxRoundMs, Math.round(typical * 1.5 * 60_000));\n}\n\n/**\n * Parallel and ghost order: finishers by time, then the rest by score,\n * then anyone who reported nothing, tied last. Equal times or scores share a\n * place.\n */\nexport function rankResults(results, ids) {\n  const timed = [];\n  const scored = [];\n  const silent = [];\n  for (const id of ids) {\n    const r = results.get(id);\n    if (r && Number.isFinite(r.time)) timed.push([id, r.time]);\n    else if (r && Number.isFinite(r.score)) scored.push([id, r.score]);\n    else silent.push(id);\n  }\n  const groups = (list, order) => {\n    list.sort((a, b) => order * (a[1] - b[1]) || a[0] - b[0]);\n    const out = [];\n    for (const [id, value] of list) {\n      const last = out[out.length - 1];\n      if (last && last.value === value) last.ids.push(id);\n      else out.push({ value, ids: [id] });\n    }\n    return out.map((g) => g.ids);\n  };\n  return [...groups(timed, 1), ...groups(scored, -1), ...(silent.length ? [silent] : [])];\n}\n\n/** A time or score as a number: finite, given as a number or as text; NaN for null, '' or true, which Number() would make 0. */\nconst asNumber = (v) => (typeof v === 'number' || (typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '') ? Number(v) : NaN);\n\n/** The protocol's limits on a round's highlights (README §10). */\nexport const HIGHLIGHTS = Object.freeze({ stats: 6, statName: 16, statText: 16, awards: 3, title: 24, detail: 40 });\n\n/** One player's stats, trimmed: up to six names, each a finite number or a short text. Null when none survive. */\nexport function cleanStats(stats) {\n  if (!stats || typeof stats !== 'object' || Array.isArray(stats)) return null;\n  const out = {};\n  for (const [name, value] of Object.entries(stats).slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.stats)) {\n    const label = String(name).trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.statName);\n    if (!label) continue;\n    if (typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value)) out[label] = value;\n    else if (typeof value === 'string' && value.trim()) out[label] = value.trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.statText);\n  }\n  return Object.keys(out).length ? out : null;\n}\n\n/**\n * Awards, trimmed: `{ id, title, detail? }`, at most three a player, for\n * players of this round. A result's awards are about its own player: `self` is its id.\n */\nexport function cleanAwards(awards, ids, self = null) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(awards)) return [];\n  const given = new Map();\n  const out = [];\n  for (const a of awards) {\n    const id = self ?? a?.id;\n    const title = String(a?.title ?? '').trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.title);\n    if (!title || !ids.includes(id) || (given.get(id) || 0) >= HIGHLIGHTS.awards) continue;\n    given.set(id, (given.get(id) || 0) + 1);\n    const detail = String(a.detail ?? '').trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.detail);\n    out.push(detail ? { id, title, detail } : { id, title });\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\n/**\n * Check a host's standings: groups of ids, best first, every present player\n * exactly once. Players already gone may be placed or left out; whoever is\n * left out lands in a last group of their own.\n */\nexport function checkStandings(standings, presentIds, allIds) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(standings)) return { ok: false, problem: 'standings is not an array' };\n  const all = new Set(allIds);\n  const seen = new Set();\n  const groups = [];\n  for (const group of standings) {\n    const ids = Array.isArray(group) ? group : [group];\n    const kept = [];\n    for (const id of ids) {\n      if (!Number.isInteger(id) || !all.has(id)) return { ok: false, problem: `unknown player id ${JSON.stringify(id)}` };\n      if (seen.has(id)) return { ok: false, problem: `player ${id} is placed twice` };\n      seen.add(id);\n      kept.push(id);\n    }\n    if (kept.length) groups.push(kept);\n  }\n  const missing = presentIds.filter((id) => !seen.has(id));\n  if (missing.length) return { ok: false, problem: `standings leave out player${missing.length > 1 ? 's' : ''} ${missing.join(', ')}` };\n  const absent = allIds.filter((id) => !seen.has(id));\n  if (absent.length) groups.push(absent);\n  return { ok: true, standings: groups };\n}\n\n/**\n * @param {object} o\n * @param {number} o.round            round number, carried on every message\n * @param {{key:string, slot:number, name:string}[]} o.players\n * @param {string} o.hostKey          whose game runs a shared world\n * @param {string} [o.serverKey]      a copy with no player of its own that runs the shared world\n *                                    instead (a server): one more copy after the players, welcomed\n *                                    with server: true, never ranked; the round is void if it goes\n * @param {string|null} o.mode        parallel | ghost | shared-world, or an older tag (modeOf); null takes the first hello's\n * @param {number} o.seed\n * @param {number} o.limitMs\n * @param {{now:()=>number, setTimeout:Function, clearTimeout:Function}} [o.clock]\n * @param {(key:string, msg:object) => void} o.deliver\n * @param {(status:object) => void} [o.onStatus]\n * @param {(record:object) => void} [o.onEnd]\n * @param {boolean} [o.gate]          the hub shows a splash and collects the players' ready itself:\n *                                    games ready up once loaded, and the round starts on release()\n */\nexport function createRound({\n  round,\n  players,\n  hostKey,\n  mode = null,\n  seed,\n  limitMs,\n  clock = REAL_CLOCK,\n  deliver,\n  onStatus = () => {},\n  onEnd = () => {},\n  timings = TIMINGS,\n  gate = false,\n  serverKey = null,\n}) {\n  mode = modeOf(mode);\n  const t = { ...TIMINGS, ...timings };\n  const seats = [...players]\n    .sort((a, b) => a.slot - b.slot)\n    .map((p, id) => ({\n      id,\n      key: p.key,\n      slot: p.slot,\n      name: p.name,\n      color: SLOT_COLORS[p.slot % SLOT_COLORS.length],\n      hello: false,\n      ready: false,\n      out: null,\n      result: null,\n      /** The last progress score the hub saw: the result of a player who never reports one. */\n      progress: null,\n      stats: null,\n      awards: [],\n      caps: null,\n      hidden: null,\n    }));\n  const server = serverKey\n    ? { id: seats.length, key: serverKey, slot: null, name: 'Server', color: null, hello: false, ready: false, out: null, result: null, progress: null, stats: null, awards: [], caps: null, hidden: null }\n    : null;\n  /** Every copy in the round: the players, then the server when there is one. */\n  const copies = server ? [...seats, server] : seats;\n  const byKey = new Map(copies.map((s) => [s.key, s]));\n  const ids = seats.map((s) => s.id);\n  const host = server ?? byKey.get(hostKey) ?? seats[0];\n  const timers = new Set();\n  const issues = [];\n  let phase = 'loading';\n  let goAt = null;\n  let record = null;\n  let released = !gate;\n\n  const later = (ms, fn) => {\n    const handle = clock.setTimeout(() => {\n      timers.delete(handle);\n      fn();\n    }, Math.max(0, ms));\n    timers.add(handle);\n    return handle;\n  };\n  const cancel = (handle) => {\n    if (handle == null) return;\n    clock.clearTimeout(handle);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"DEV='Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701'; sed -n '345,470p' \\\"\"'$DEV/hub/session.js\"; rg -n '\"'canvas|gameGlue|loadGame|id=\\\"msg\\\"|</body>' \\\"\"'$DEV/engine/web/index.html\"; rg -n '\"'LOADER|</body>|replace_one|theme-color|description' \\\"\"'$DEV/engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py\"; sed -n '\"'1,110p' \\\"\"'$DEV/engine/scripts/build-web.sh\"; sed -n '\"'55,145p' PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"DEV='Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701'; sed -n '345,470p' \\\"\"'$DEV/hub/session.js\"; rg -n '\"'canvas|gameGlue|loadGame|id=\\\"msg\\\"|</body>' \\\"\"'$DEV/engine/web/index.html\"; rg -n '\"'LOADER|</body>|replace_one|theme-color|description' \\\"\"'$DEV/engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py\"; sed -n '\"'1,110p' \\\"\"'$DEV/engine/scripts/build-web.sh\"; sed -n '\"'55,145p' PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"      var list = handlers[type] || [];\n      var at = list.indexOf(fn);\n      if (at !== -1) list.splice(at, 1);\n    };\n  };\n\n  /** Send JSON data to every other player, or to one with {to: id}. {reliable: false} may drop or reorder. */\n  hub.send = function (data, opts) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return false;\n    opts = opts || {};\n    var text;\n    try {\n      text = JSON.stringify(data);\n    } catch (e) {\n      warn('send: data is not JSON');\n      return false;\n    }\n    if (text === undefined) return false;\n    if (text.length > limits.maxBytes) {\n      warn('send: message over ' + limits.maxBytes + ' bytes dropped');\n      return false;\n    }\n    var t = now();\n    tokens = Math.min(limits.burst, tokens + ((t - refilled) / 1000) * limits.ratePerS);\n    refilled = t;\n    if (tokens < 1) {\n      warn('send: over ' + limits.ratePerS + ' messages a second, dropped');\n      return false;\n    }\n    tokens -= 1;\n    var fields = { data: JSON.parse(text), reliable: opts.reliable !== false };\n    if (opts.to !== undefined && opts.to !== null) fields.to = opts.to;\n    post('send', fields);\n    return true;\n  };\n\n  /** Milliseconds since the synchronized start: negative during the countdown, -Infinity before start. */\n  hub.time = function () {\n    return goAt === null ? -Infinity : now() - goAt;\n  };\n\n  /** A seeded random number generator (0 ≤ n < 1), the same sequence on every device for the same label. */\n  hub.rng = function (label) {\n    var h = 2166136261;\n    var s = String(label === undefined ? '' : label);\n    for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n      h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\n      h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\n    }\n    return generator((hub.seed ^ h) >>> 0);\n  };\n\n  /** A number the hub can rank: finite, given as a number or as text. Not null, '' or true, which JSON or Number would make 0. */\n  function finite(v) {\n    return (typeof v === 'number' || (typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '')) && isFinite(v);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * The whole outcome as plain JSON, field by field: the hub checks and trims\n   * it, so new optional fields need no new client. A field that is not JSON\n   * (a cycle, a BigInt) is left out, not the whole outcome.\n   */\n  function outcomeOf(outcome) {\n    if (!outcome || typeof outcome !== 'object' || Array.isArray(outcome)) {\n      warn('the outcome is not a plain object');\n      return null;\n    }\n    var copy = {};\n    for (var key in outcome) {\n      if (!own(outcome, key)) continue;\n      var value = json(outcome[key]);\n      if (value !== undefined) copy[key] = value;\n      else if (outcome[key] !== undefined) warn('the outcome\\'s ' + key + ' is not JSON: left out');\n    }\n    return copy;\n  }\n\n  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\n  hub.result = function (outcome) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\n    if (!fields) return;\n    var given = outcome || {};\n    delete fields.time;\n    delete fields.score;\n    if (finite(given.time)) fields.time = Number(given.time);\n    if (finite(given.score)) fields.score = Number(given.score);\n    if (!own(fields, 'time') && !own(fields, 'score')) return warn('result needs a finite time or score');\n    reported = true;\n    if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\n    post('result', fields);\n  };\n\n  /** Versus and co-op: the host reports the standings once, best first, ties grouped: [[2], [0, 3], [1]]. */\n  hub.finish = function (outcome) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\n    if (!hub.isHost) return warn('finish is for the host only');\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\n    if (!fields) return;\n    if (!Array.isArray(fields.standings)) return warn('finish needs standings');\n    reported = true;\n    post('finish', fields);\n  };\n\n  function sendProgress() {\n    progressTimer = null;\n    if (!nextProgress || ended || reported) return;\n    lastProgress = now();\n    post('progress', nextProgress);\n    nextProgress = null;\n  }\n\n  /** Your standing during play, for the hub's scoreboard: {score, label}. Call it as often as you like; the hub hears it about once a second. */\n  hub.progress = function (p) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported || !p || !finite(p.score)) return;\n    nextProgress = { score: Number(p.score) };\n    if (p.label != null) nextProgress.label = String(p.label).slice(0, 24);\n    var wait = lastProgress + PROGRESS_EVERY_MS - now();\n    if (wait <= 0) sendProgress();\n    else if (!progressTimer) progressTimer = setTimeout(sendProgress, wait);\n  };\n\n  /** For the harness, in or out of a session: fn() → { scene, menu, world, input }, read with inspect(). */\n  hub.probe = function (fn) {\n    probeFn = typeof fn === 'function' ? fn : null;\n  };\n19:  /* winit appends the game canvas to <body>; it fills the page and the game follows its size.\n21:  canvas { display: block; width: 100vw !important; height: 100vh !important; height: 100dvh !important;\n34:<div id=\"msg\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">Loading Shardfall…</div>\n45:    // The game hides this message once its canvas exists, and takes keyboard focus.\n47:      const c = document.querySelector('canvas');\n64:      // (scripts/pack_single_html.py) carries both inside the page and sets window.loadGame.\n65:      if (window.loadGame) await window.loadGame();\n74:</body>\n4:usage: python3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py BINDGEN_DIR [--title T] [--description D]\n5:           [--theme-color C] [--scene NAME] [--out PATH]\n9:its <title>, <meta name=description> and <meta name=theme-color> (left as they are when not\n10:given), the manifest link dropped, and, before </body>, the gzipped wasm as base64 text, a\n29:LOADER = \"\"\"\n82:def replace_one(page, pattern, make, what):\n91:    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split(\"\\n\")[0])\n94:    ap.add_argument(\"--description\", help=\"<meta name=description> (default: index.html's)\")\n95:    ap.add_argument(\"--theme-color\", help=\"<meta name=theme-color> (default: index.html's)\")\n117:        page = replace_one(page, r\"<title>[^<]*</title>\", lambda m: f\"<title>{html.escape(a.title)}</title>\", \"<title>\")\n118:    for name, value in ((\"description\", a.description), (\"theme-color\", a.theme_color)):\n120:            page = replace_one(\n127:    page = replace_one(page, r'[ \\t]*<link rel=\"manifest\"[^>]*>\\n', lambda m: \"\", \"manifest link\")\n132:    loader = LOADER.replace(\"__SCENE__\", json.dumps(a.scene or None).replace(\"<\", \"\\\\u003c\"))\n139:    page = replace_one(page, r\"</body>\", lambda m: tail + \"</body>\", \"</body>\")\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Builds the browser version (WebAssembly + WebGPU). Output: target/web/{index.html,manifest.webmanifest,shardfall.js,shardfall_bg.wasm}\n# Serve that folder over HTTP (e.g. `python3 -m http.server -d target/web`) and open it in Chrome or Edge.\n# --single-file writes only target/web/<title>.html (shardfall.html): one page with the glue and gzipped wasm inside\n#   that runs from file:// or any host (scripts/pack_single_html.py; also --title, --description, --theme-color,\n#   --scene NAME for the start scene when the address names none, --out PATH).\n# Needs: rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown\n#        cargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version <the wasm-bindgen version in Cargo.lock>\nset -euo pipefail\ncaller=$PWD\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\"\nsingle=false\npack=()\nwhile (($#)); do\n\tcase $1 in\n\t--single-file) single=true ;;\n\t--title | --description | --theme-color | --scene | --out)\n\t\t(($# > 1)) || { echo \"build-web.sh: $1 needs a value\" >&2; exit 2; }\n\t\tvalue=$2\n\t\t[[ $1 == --out && $value != /* ]] && value=$caller/$value\n\t\tpack+=(\"$1\" \"$value\")\n\t\tshift\n\t\t;;\n\t*) echo \"build-web.sh: unknown option $1 (options are listed at the top of $0)\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n\tesac\n\tshift\ndone\nif ((${#pack[@]})) && ! $single; then\n\techo \"build-web.sh: ${pack[0]} needs --single-file\" >&2\n\texit 2\nfi\ncargo build --locked --profile dist --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p pav_app\nwasm=${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/wasm32-unknown-unknown/dist/shardfall.wasm\nout=target/web\nif $single; then\n\tbindgen=$(mktemp -d)\n\ttrap 'rm -rf \"$bindgen\"' EXIT\n\twasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \"$bindgen\" --out-name shardfall \"$wasm\"\n\tpython3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py \"$bindgen\" \"${pack[@]}\"\n\texit\nfi\nrm -rf \"$out\"\nmkdir -p \"$out\"\nwasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \"$out\" --out-name shardfall \"$wasm\"\ncp web/index.html web/manifest.webmanifest \"$out/\"\nls -la \"$out\"\n1. Wake on the cabana deck. Pip greets you, with an absence comment if real days have passed.\n2. Morning Wobble Check (about 70 seconds), Balance Age reveal, Pip's comment.\n3. Free time on the island: walk, talk to guests, find lost flip-flops, step on an event mat. The Schedule (Triangle or Tab) lists everything and fast-travels.\n4. When the day's minute goal is met, Pip says so. Sleep at your cabana (or choose End Day in the Schedule). A big stamp lands on the Calendar. Next day.\n\n| Day | Opens | Minute goal | Story beat |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Stillness Studio: Breath Bloom, Pose Parade | 3 | Arrival. The checkout rule. \"Nobody has asked to leave yet\" |\n| 2 | Iron Gazebo: Tempo Squats, Plank Standoff | 5 | Big Kettle. Wardrobe opens |\n| 3 | Boardwalk: Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap | 7 | Yesterday You appears as a ghost. \"I am not comparing you\" |\n| 4 | Lagoon: Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup | 9 | Guests start whispering about the Big Stand |\n| 5 | The Big Stand, after the morning check | none | Finale, ending, free play |\n\n**Minutes:** the first clear of an event each day banks 1 + stars (0 to 3 stars, so 1 to 4 minutes); repeats bank 1. Resort minutes are openly not real minutes (\"Our minutes are longer. It is a wellness thing\").\n\n**Endings:** Balance Age 40 or better: you may check out, by rowboat (`LIB/core/rowboat`). Otherwise: the Extended Stay ending, gentle and funny. Both roll credits, then unlock Free Play: every event open, personal bests, star goals, and a calendar that keeps stamping real days.\n\n**Bot rule:** `Game::bot` must be able to play this entire flow, menus included, from New Stay to the credits. That is your scripted playthrough and the base of attract mode.\n\n## 3. Controls\n\nThe left stick is both walking and leaning. Prompts always show the glyph for the input used last.\n\n| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Walk on the island, lean in events | Left stick | W A S D (arrows also walk) | Island: click a place or thing to walk there. Events: cursor offset from screen centre is the lean |\n| Fine lean | Stick itself | Hold Shift (half key rate) | Small cursor moves |\n| Jog on the island | Hold R2 | Hold Shift | |\n| Action: talk, begin, inhale, squat, bounce | Cross | Space | Left button |\n| Left step / right step | L1 or L2 / R1 or R2 | Q or Left / E or Right | Left button / right button |\n| Brace (hold both) | L2+R2 or L1+R1 | Q+E | Both buttons |\n| Wave at someone | Square | F | |\n| Schedule | Triangle | Tab | |\n| Island camera | Right stick | | Right-drag, wheel zooms |\n| Pause | Options | Esc | |\n| Menus | D-pad or left stick, Cross confirms, Circle backs, L1/R1 change tabs | Arrows or W A S D, Enter or Space, Esc backs, Q/E change tabs | Hover moves focus, click activates, right-click backs |\n\nXbox glyphs (Settings option) swap A B X Y, LB RB LT RT, Menu. Ignore Options while Create is held: that pair belongs to the AI Hub. Disable the engine's own keys (F1 to F10, digits, H, Backspace rewind, right-drag tilt) outside dev mode. Keep F11 for fullscreen.\n\n## 4. The Balance Core\n\nOne struct, `BalanceCore`, used by every event. Its state is `cob` (the dot, unit disc, x right, y up on screen) and `vel`.\n\n```\ntarget = shaped lean input * reach + wobble(t)\nacc    = (target - cob) * stiffness - vel * damping + gust + nudge\nvel   += acc * dt\ncob   += vel * dt\ntip    = |cob| > 1 for tip_time seconds\n```\n\nStart with `stiffness 40`, `damping 8.5`, `reach 0.92`, `tip_time 0.35`. `wobble` is `amp * (0.7 * sin(2*pi*1.3*t + a) + 0.3 * sin(2*pi*2.9*t + b))` per axis, phases from `sim.state.rng`, base `amp 0.12`, scaled per event and by fatigue, plus a velocity kick of 0.1 units/s in a random direction every 1 to 2 seconds. Use sim time, never the clock.\n\n**Feel targets** (these numbers give them, by numeric simulation at 60 ticks/s): full stick reaches 90% in about 0.4 s with about 5% overshoot, like a body. Release settles in about 0.45 s. Left alone, the dot wanders at a mean radius of 0.05, at most 0.08. A held full lean does not tip by itself; a gust on top of it does.\n\n**Input shaping** (in `pav_app`, passed as `InputFrame.lean`, screen space):\n- **Stick:** deadzone 0.12, response curve `x^1.5` so small motions are fine.\n- **Keyboard:** keys move the target at 1.6 units/s and it returns at 1.2 units/s when released. Tapping gives small nudges, so keys feel native, not bang-bang.\n- **Mouse:** cursor offset from the screen centre divided by 0.38 of the window height, clamped to the disc. No pointer lock. The device moved last wins.\n\n**Body:** the figure tilts with the dot (`cob * 14` degrees about the feet, engine change in section 14). Beyond |cob| 0.75 an upper-body arm-flail clip fades in. A tip plays a stumble and, over water, a splash. Tips never end the game; they cost time or score.\n\n**HUD, the Puck:** a large circular gauge drawn in egui: a pale disc, a green target ring, a coral dot, and stars at the edge when streaking. It must read from 10 feet. It looks good at 340 px diameter at 1080p (verified). Put it top centre or bottom centre, whichever does not cover the figure in that event.\n\n## 5. Events\n\n**Common frame:** event card (name, one-sentence goal, glyph prompts, one coach line), 3-2-1, play, result (score 0 to 1000, stars at 400, 650 and 850, a deadpan Title, minutes banked, personal best, difference from Yesterday You; Retry or Back).\n\n**Every event has:** a section of tunable numbers in `rules.toml`, a bot that earns at least 2 stars, an idle-input outcome below 1 star, a ghost lane, and an attract segment. Scenes `fit/event/<name>` start an event directly, for tools and tests.\n\n### Stillness Studio (Posey). Set: `studio`, a round white deck on a calm dawn lagoon. Camera: mirror view (yaw 0, tilt 12, distance 8.5, fov 36; the figure faces +Z, toward the camera, and stick right is screen right).\n\n**Breath Bloom** (45 s). Hold Action to inhale, release to exhale, following a guide ring: 4 s in, 4 s out, 5 cycles, the last one longer. `lungs` rises while held and falls when not. Keep the dot inside a centre ring of radius 0.35. Tick score: `0.7 * (1 - clamp(|lungs - guide| / 0.35)) + 0.3 * inRing`. Each good cycle opens a lotus on the water with a rising pentatonic chime; a perfect run blooms the whole pond. Scrub the clip `FIT/Breath` by `lungs`. No fail state. Bot: holds while the guide rises.\n\n**Pose Parade** (3 poses, 20 s each). Six hand-keyed poses with deadpan names: the Patient Heron, the Apologetic Lunge, the Tired Lighthouse, the Folded Deck Chair, the Reluctant Bridge, Seated Disappointment. Day 1 uses the first three. Posey holds the pose beside you. A target ring (radius 0.30 shrinking to 0.18) drifts on a slow Lissajous path (amplitude 0.35, 0.12 Hz). Inside the ring a streak multiplier climbs x1 to x4, one step per 2 s; leaving resets it. At 12 s of pose 2 a gull lands on your head and wobble is x1.6 for 5 s (\"There is a bird on you. Accept the bird\"). A tip breaks the pose for 1.5 s. Score: time in ring weighted by multiplier. Bot: PD toward the ring centre.\n\n### Iron Gazebo (Big Kettle). Set: `gazebo`, a white iron gazebo at golden hour. Camera: 3/4 front.\n\n**Tempo Squats** (10 reps, about 50 s). Hold Action to go down (2 s to full depth), release to rise (1 s). A guide bar shows the tempo; a low bell marks the bottom. Keep the dot in a band |x| < 0.25; wobble grows 8% per rep. Rep score: `0.7 * timing + 0.3 * band`. Scrub `FIT/Squat` by depth. Gag: rep 10 is followed by \"Ten. Also eleven.\" Bot: follows the guide.\n\n**Plank Standoff** (up to 60 s). Hold Brace and keep the dot in a ring shrinking from 0.40 to 0.20. Releasing, or leaving the ring for more than 1 s, collapses you in a comic flop. Fatigue ramps wobble; at 30 s add tremble; at 45 s Kettle laughs at his own joke and the nudge shakes the screen. Score: seconds survived / 60. Stars at 25, 40 and 55 s. Kettle, who has no arms, plank-talks you through it. Base the pose on one frame of `MESH2MOTION/Pushup`. Bot: survives at least 45 s.\n\n### Boardwalk (Bounce). Set: `boardwalk`, a beach boardwalk at bright midday.\n\n**Step Party** (64 s, 96 BPM, song 4). A rhythm game: notes in two lanes fall to two footprints, left, right or both, on an aerobic step box. Perfect within 55 ms, Good within 120 ms. About 100 notes, data in `charts.toml`, starting with quarter notes and building to eighths and doubles. Bounce bounces on the beat and guests clap on downbeats. Timing uses the audio clock (section 10). Camera: mirror view, slightly high. Bot: presses exactly on each note.\n\n**Floatie Spin** (50 s). Circle the lean (stick, mouse, or rolling W-D-S-A) to spin inflatable rings around your hips. Spin speed is the smoothed angular velocity of the lean while |lean| > 0.4; the sweet band is 6 to 9 rad/s, and a `spin_band_scale` rule widens it for keyboard. \"Switch!\" flips the required direction every 15 s. Guests toss new rings from left or right: press that side's step within 0.25 s of arrival to catch it. Out of band, rings sink; on the floor they are lost. Maximum 7 rings. Score: rings times time in band. Rings are no-physics entities positioned in code. Bot: 7.5 rad/s circle, presses on arrivals.\n\n**Morning Lap** (about 90 s, one lap of the hub island). Alternate left and right steps to set your pace (1.6 to 2.4 steps/s is the zone). Too fast raises a stitch meter that makes you stumble; too slow and Bounce, the pacer rolling ahead, gets away. The path steers you; lean moves you up to 1.2 m sideways to dodge crabs, sunbathers and towels and to grab ribbons. Flip-flops can be found here too. Score: time in zone, plus ribbons, minus bumps. Camera: chase with per-tick yaw. Use `MESH2MOTION/Jog` scaled to speed. Bot: 2 steps/s, steers to ribbons.\n\n### Lagoon (Commodore Gull). Sets: `tide`, `channel`, `pier`, `tower`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
