{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"set -e\nD='Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701'\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- workspace ---'; ls -lah\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- syntax ---'; node --check \\\"\"'$D/web/game.js\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- bundler options ---'; sed -n '1,200p' \\\"\"'$D/engine/scripts/build-web.sh\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- task hand-in/debug ---'; rg -n -C 4 'exit-interview|Source Information|Testing Feedback|Engine Feedback|Prompt Feedback|__gameBoot|__gameStatus|tests|bundle' TASK.md PLAN.md\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- hub API ---'; rg -n -C 2 'function (connect|send|probe|result)|const (connect|send)|on\\\\(' \\\"\"'$D/hub/session.js\" | head -120\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- relevant CSS ---'; rg -n 'phase-card|hud-right|meter-track|overlay|tiny|speaker|touch-guard|target|puck|world' \\\"\"'$D/web/game.css\"'","aggregated_output":"--- workspace ---\ntotal 96K\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha 4.0K Nov  4 22:28 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 micha micha 4.0K Nov  4 22:27 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  63K Nov  4 22:27 PLAN.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  645 Nov  4 22:38 PROGRESS.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  13K Nov  4 22:27 TASK.md\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 micha micha 4.0K Nov  4 22:41 Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701\n--- syntax ---\n--- bundler options ---\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Builds the browser version (WebAssembly + WebGPU). Output: target/web/{index.html,manifest.webmanifest,shardfall.js,shardfall_bg.wasm}\n# Serve that folder over HTTP (e.g. `python3 -m http.server -d target/web`) and open it in Chrome or Edge.\n# --single-file writes only target/web/<title>.html (shardfall.html): one page with the glue and gzipped wasm inside\n#   that runs from file:// or any host (scripts/pack_single_html.py; also --title, --description, --theme-color,\n#   --scene NAME for the start scene when the address names none, --out PATH).\n# Needs: rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown\n#        cargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version <the wasm-bindgen version in Cargo.lock>\nset -euo pipefail\ncaller=$PWD\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\"\nsingle=false\npack=()\nwhile (($#)); do\n\tcase $1 in\n\t--single-file) single=true ;;\n\t--title | --description | --theme-color | --scene | --out)\n\t\t(($# > 1)) || { echo \"build-web.sh: $1 needs a value\" >&2; exit 2; }\n\t\tvalue=$2\n\t\t[[ $1 == --out && $value != /* ]] && value=$caller/$value\n\t\tpack+=(\"$1\" \"$value\")\n\t\tshift\n\t\t;;\n\t*) echo \"build-web.sh: unknown option $1 (options are listed at the top of $0)\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n\tesac\n\tshift\ndone\nif ((${#pack[@]})) && ! $single; then\n\techo \"build-web.sh: ${pack[0]} needs --single-file\" >&2\n\texit 2\nfi\ncargo build --locked --profile dist --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p pav_app\nwasm=${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/wasm32-unknown-unknown/dist/shardfall.wasm\nout=target/web\nif $single; then\n\tbindgen=$(mktemp -d)\n\ttrap 'rm -rf \"$bindgen\"' EXIT\n\twasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \"$bindgen\" --out-name shardfall \"$wasm\"\n\tpython3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py \"$bindgen\" \"${pack[@]}\"\n\texit\nfi\nrm -rf \"$out\"\nmkdir -p \"$out\"\nwasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \"$out\" --out-name shardfall \"$wasm\"\ncp web/index.html web/manifest.webmanifest \"$out/\"\nls -la \"$out\"\n--- task hand-in/debug ---\nPLAN.md-13-- **Reading cost:** you do not need to read the engine's source to start. Read `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` whole (about 3k tokens) and `engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/starter.rs`, then use this plan. Search `engine/docs/REFERENCE.md` and `engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md` when you need a tool or a prop field.\nPLAN.md-14-\nPLAN.md-15-## 1. The game in one page\nPLAN.md-16-\nPLAN.md:17:You have won a five-day stay at Tippy Cay, a small wellness resort staffed entirely by talking gym equipment. You do not remember entering. Each morning a relentlessly pleasant wobble cushion tests your balance and gives you a Balance Age. Each day you walk the island, try short stillness, strength, cardio and balance events, and bank minutes in a giant clam. Checkout requires a Balance Age of 40 or better. Day 5 ends in the Big Stand, a finale whose last test is to do nothing at all for thirty seconds while the game tries to make you press something.\nPLAN.md-18-\nPLAN.md-19-- **Genre:** sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame (daily ritual, unlocks, wardrobe). Catalogue genre: Sports.\nPLAN.md-20-- **Perspective:** third person throughout, with a camera chosen per activity: 3/4 follow on the island, a mirror-style front view for exercises on the spot, chase for the jog and the paddle, high 3/4 for the table, side view for the dives.\nPLAN.md-21-- **Length:** a first run takes 25 to 40 minutes. It shows every feature. Free play follows.\n--\nPLAN.md-119-## 5. Events\nPLAN.md-120-\nPLAN.md-121-**Common frame:** event card (name, one-sentence goal, glyph prompts, one coach line), 3-2-1, play, result (score 0 to 1000, stars at 400, 650 and 850, a deadpan Title, minutes banked, personal best, difference from Yesterday You; Retry or Back).\nPLAN.md-122-\nPLAN.md:123:**Every event has:** a section of tunable numbers in `rules.toml`, a bot that earns at least 2 stars, an idle-input outcome below 1 star, a ghost lane, and an attract segment. Scenes `fit/event/<name>` start an event directly, for tools and tests.\nPLAN.md-124-\nPLAN.md-125-### Stillness Studio (Posey). Set: `studio`, a round white deck on a calm dawn lagoon. Camera: mirror view (yaw 0, tilt 12, distance 8.5, fov 36; the figure faces +Z, toward the camera, and stick right is screen right).\nPLAN.md-126-\nPLAN.md-127-**Breath Bloom** (45 s). Hold Action to inhale, release to exhale, following a guide ring: 4 s in, 4 s out, 5 cycles, the last one longer. `lungs` rises while held and falls when not. Keep the dot inside a centre ring of radius 0.35. Tick score: `0.7 * (1 - clamp(|lungs - guide| / 0.35)) + 0.3 * inRing`. Each good cycle opens a lotus on the water with a rising pentatonic chime; a perfect run blooms the whole pond. Scrub the clip `FIT/Breath` by `lungs`. No fail state. Bot: holds while the guide rises.\n--\nPLAN.md-162-5. **The Long Stillness:** 30 s of nothing. Music fades to silence, the HUD vanishes except the Puck. At 15 s a fake prompt offers \"Press Cross to skip\". Pressing anything forfeits the Inner Peace bonus. Then Pip, quietly: \"...Oh. You're still here. Good.\"\nPLAN.md-163-\nPLAN.md-164-A tip drops you in the sea to a groan from the crowd and puts you back; it costs score and cannot end the run. Final Balance Age = morning age minus `final_score / 100` (up to 10).\nPLAN.md-165-\nPLAN.md:166:### Morning Wobble Check. Set: `studio`. About 70 s, four micro-tests, Pip presiding.\nPLAN.md-167-\nPLAN.md-168-| Test | What you do | Metric (0 to 1) |\nPLAN.md-169-|---|---|---|\nPLAN.md-170-| Stand Still (\"This is the whole test\") | Hold the dot centred for 8 s; one small nudge at 5 s | Mean distance from centre |\n--\nPLAN.md-311-\nPLAN.md-312-- **Buses:** music, sfx and voice, each a gain applied per voice in `Mixer::render`. Settings defaults: **music 10%** as your brief requires (0.10 linear), sfx 80%, voice 80%.\nPLAN.md-313-- **New events:** add `SimEvent` variants `Sfx { id, gain, pitch }`, `Syllable { speaker, vowel, pitch }`, `Music { song }`, `BigSplash { pos, size }`. `pav_audio::sounds_for` is a closed match; add arms there.\nPLAN.md-314-- **Sequencer:** `pav_audio/src/music.rs`, running inside `Mixer::render` so timing is sample-accurate. A song is BPM, steps per beat and tracks of patch plus pattern, written by hand as arrays of scale degrees over a chord progression. Add a low-pass LFO patch option for pads.\nPLAN.md:315:- **Rhythm clock:** the mixer counts rendered samples in an atomic. `pav_app` reads it, runs a small phase-locked clock (`clock += dt; clock += (audio_pos - clock) * 0.05`), subtracts a latency offset (default 0.10 s, Settings: Rhythm Offset), and sends it as `InputFrame.song_pos`. The sim uses `song_pos` when present, its own tick time otherwise. Replays and tests stay deterministic, because the value is part of the recorded input.\nPLAN.md-316-- **Latency:** cpal's web backend defaults to 2048 frames per buffer, about 43 ms (read in its source, not measured on a real device). Try `BufferSize::Fixed(1024)` in `AudioOut::start` for snappier effects.\nPLAN.md-317-- **Autoplay:** `resume_audio` runs on key, mouse and touch only. Also call it on the first gamepad activity. Attract mode is silent until a real input arrives; that is expected.\nPLAN.md-318-\nPLAN.md-319-| Song | Where | Feel (all original) |\n--\nPLAN.md-331-**Voices (Animalese style).** A formant-filtered saw blip per syllable: add two parallel band-pass filters to `Patch`/`Voice`, with a table of formant pairs for 5 vowels, plus a tiny noise click for consonants. The dialogue system fires one `Syllable` per 2 to 3 revealed letters, vowel from the letter, pitch falling at \".\" and rising at \"?\". Each speaker has a base pitch, rate and timbre: Pip high and rubbery, Posey soft with wood-block attack, Kettle very low, Bounce fast and breathless, Gull nasal and clipped. No real words are ever spoken.\nPLAN.md-332-\nPLAN.md-333-## 11. UI and UX\nPLAN.md-334-\nPLAN.md:335:**Route: egui in `pav_ui`, painter-drawn, no default windows.** This was verified at 1920x1080: rounded fonts, soft-shadow cards and painted glyphs look right and appear in headless `pav capture`. Keep all UI state in the sim (section 14), so tests can drive it.\nPLAN.md-336-\nPLAN.md-337-**Fonts:** `npm pack @expo-google-fonts/fredoka` and `@expo-google-fonts/nunito` (SIL OFL, static TTFs). Unpack into their own folder and copy `Fredoka_600SemiBold.ttf` (titles, 50 KB) and `Nunito_700Bold.ttf` (body, 132 KB) to `engine/crates/pav_ui/fonts/`. Embed with `include_bytes!`. Credit them on the About screen.\nPLAN.md-338-\nPLAN.md-339-**Rules:** at 1080p, body text at least 34 px and titles at least 64 px. Scale everything by `min(w/1920, h/1080)`, so it also works in small hub frames. Cards are white with radius 36. Focus is a thick teal outline, scale 1.05 and a soft bounce, with a sound on every move. At most 6 items visible. No tables, no dense stats, at most 4 numbers on a screen, and the About screen is pages, not a scrolling wall. Everything works by pad alone. Keyboard and mouse use the same screens. Hover moves focus, and click activates.\n--\nPLAN.md-398-**Hub logic lives in about 30 lines of plain JS in the page; Rust only reads and writes window fields.** This exact block passed the harness on a real engine build at 2 players, at 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, and with `scenario=host-leave`, in 14 to 19 s each, and the page ran clean outside a session (verified):\nPLAN.md-399-\nPLAN.md-400-```js\nPLAN.md-401-(() => {\nPLAN.md:402:  const boot = window.__gameBoot = { scene: null, seed: null, today: Math.floor(Date.now() / 86400000),\nPLAN.md-403-                                     about: document.getElementById('about-data')?.textContent ?? '' };\nPLAN.md-404-  if (!window.AIHub || !AIHub.active) return;\nPLAN.md-405-  const hub = window.__hub = { go: false, ended: false, players: [], me: 0, ghosts: {} };\nPLAN.md-406-  boot.scene = 'fit/medley';\n--\nPLAN.md-409-    if (!info) { location.replace(location.pathname); return; }   // no hub after all\nPLAN.md-410-    if (!navigator.gpu) { AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU'); return; }\nPLAN.md-411-    hub.me = info.me; hub.players = info.players;\nPLAN.md-412-    // Before the first status arrives, report a zero: the hub must always hear a number.\nPLAN.md:413:    const status = () => { try { return JSON.parse(window.__gameStatus || 'null')?.hub ?? null; } catch { return null; } };\nPLAN.md:414:    const waitReady = () => (window.__gameStatus ? AIHub.ready() : setTimeout(waitReady, 50));\nPLAN.md-415-    waitReady();\nPLAN.md-416-    let reported = false;\nPLAN.md-417-    const report = () => { if (reported) return; reported = true; const s = status(); AIHub.result({ score: s?.score ?? 0, stats: s?.stats ?? {} }); };\nPLAN.md-418-    setInterval(() => {\n--\nPLAN.md-441-These reuse the hub's ghost drawing and scoring, so there is one multiplayer system with three sources of ghosts.\nPLAN.md-442-\nPLAN.md-443-## 14. Architecture\nPLAN.md-444-\nPLAN.md:445:**Decision: all game state and flow live in the sim, in one `Game`.** Menus, dialogue, pause, settings values and dev toggles are state in `FitGame`, driven by `InputFrame`, so `cargo test` can play the whole game with no browser or GPU in seconds. `pav_ui` is a pure view of a `UiFrame`: it draws the frame, and returns what the pointer hovered and clicked, which the app sends back as `InputFrame.ui` (clear PRIMARY that frame if the UI took the click) and publishes as item rects in `window.__gameUi` for browser tests. Pause freezes the world by an early return in `Sim::step_inner`, not by `TimeControl`.\nPLAN.md-446-\nPLAN.md-447-```\nPLAN.md-448-engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/\nPLAN.md-449-  mod.rs           FitGame: Flow state machine, Game impl, build(), scene routing\n--\nPLAN.md-460-engine/crates/pav_ui/src/fit_ui.rs, glyphs.rs, fonts/\nPLAN.md-461-engine/crates/pav_audio/src/music.rs, voice.rs\nPLAN.md-462-engine/crates/pav_app/src/weblink.rs  window field reads and writes\nPLAN.md-463-engine/web/index.html                 hub client, tags, JS, about-data\nPLAN.md:464:tests/  tools/  hub/  notes/  README.md  (how to add an event, set or song)\nPLAN.md-465-```\nPLAN.md-466-Register it as `entry::<fit::FitGame>(..., fit::build)`, `KEY = \"fit\"`. Scene names: `fit`, `fit/medley`, `fit/event/<name>`. Read data with `games::level_text(\"fit/rules\", include_str!(\"rules.toml\"))`: running from `engine/`, it reads the disk file, so text, numbers and set layouts change with no rebuild. Do not put sets in `engine/rooms/`: that folder feeds the pavilion demo.\nPLAN.md-467-\nPLAN.md-468-**Every set is a room on one `Sim`** (verified: two rooms, each with its own `[camera]` and `[view]`, switching live in the browser):\n--\nPLAN.md-487-**Per-state cameras:** `sim.state.courses.sticky_cue = Some(Arc::new(CameraCue { set, sweep, flip_ortho: 0.0 })); sim.state.courses.cue_serial += 1;` blends over 0.7 s in the window and in the tools. Use `sweep` for slow result-screen orbits. Lighting per state: `courses.view` and `view_serial`.\nPLAN.md-488-\nPLAN.md-489-| File | Change | Why |\nPLAN.md-490-|---|---|---|\nPLAN.md:491:| `pav_core/src/input.rs` | Add to `InputFrame`: `lean: Vec2`, `any: bool`, `ui: Option<UiEvent>` (Copy: `Hover(u16)`, `Click(u16)`, `Slider(u16, f32)`), `song_pos: Option<f32>`, all `#[serde(default)]`. New `buttons`: CONFIRM, BACK, MENU_UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT, TAB_L, TAB_R, PAUSE, SCHEDULE, WAVE, STEP_L, STEP_R, HUB_GO | Everything the game needs is input, so replays and tests cover it |\nPLAN.md-492-| `pav_core/src/games/mod.rs`, `sim.rs` | `Game::frozen()` with a default of false (add it to the trait and its `DynGame` and `GameBox` wrappers); when true, `step_inner` skips everything after `play_pre` except tick++ and events | Pause freezes the world while menus still run |\nPLAN.md-493-| `pav_core/src/frame.rs`, `sim.rs` | `HudFrame.status: Option<String>` (the game's status JSON), `HudFrame.fit: Option<Arc<UiFrame>>` and `HudFrame.camera_yaw: Option<f32>`, which `pav_app` and `pav_tools/src/session.rs` apply to the rig each frame | Link to JS and to the UI; Morning Lap's chase camera, since cues blend over 0.7 s and cannot follow per tick |\nPLAN.md-494-| `pav_view/src/build.rs`, `fx.rs` | Handle `BigSplash` (bigger water dents and bursts) and a silent `Wake { pos }` event (a small dent, no sound; `Splash` is loud if repeated) | The dive's payoff and the paddle's wake |\nPLAN.md-495-| `pav_core/src/puppet.rs` | `tilt_side`, `tilt_fwd` in `PuppetState` (add to `lerp`), applied in `body_motion` as a rotation about the feet | The whole figure leans with the dot |\n--\nPLAN.md-507-```rust\nPLAN.md-508-use web_sys::js_sys::{Array, Reflect};\nPLAN.md-509-use web_sys::wasm_bindgen::{JsCast, JsValue};\nPLAN.md-510-let win = web_sys::window().unwrap();\nPLAN.md:511:Reflect::set(&win, &JsValue::from_str(\"__gameStatus\"), &JsValue::from_str(&status)).ok();\nPLAN.md-512-let v = Reflect::get(&win, &JsValue::from_str(\"__hub\")).unwrap_or(JsValue::UNDEFINED);\nPLAN.md-513-// Array::from(&v) makes a copy, so clearing it leaves the original full (verified).\nPLAN.md-514-// To read and clear a JS array in place: let arr: Array = v.unchecked_into(); ... arr.set_length(0);\nPLAN.md-515-```\nPLAN.md:516:`pack_single_html.py` refuses wasm-bindgen snippets (`inline_js`, `module`), so use `Reflect`. Do not use `host.exec` or `host.query` per frame: in the browser they re-publish a frame and rotate prev/curr, which stutters the interpolation. Read `curr.hud.status` instead. `Settings::load` should read `window.__gameBoot.scene` and `.seed` when present.\nPLAN.md-517-\nPLAN.md:518:**About text stays in plain text in the page.** Put it in `<script id=\"about-data\" type=\"application/json\">` in the `<head>`, not in the wasm. The agent that imports the game edits the Usage line later, and it cannot edit text inside a gzipped wasm. Rust reads it from `__gameBoot.about`.\nPLAN.md-519-\nPLAN.md-520-## 15. Verified facts and traps\nPLAN.md-521-\nPLAN.md-522-Build times with `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8`:\n--\nPLAN.md-526-- `pav capture ... width=1920 height=1080`: about 0.5 s. `pav play bot=true seeds=5`: under 1 s.\nPLAN.md-527-- Batch Rust edits and keep numbers in TOML.\nPLAN.md-528-\nPLAN.md-529-Browser:\nPLAN.md:530:- **Software rendering is slow, so size the window to the test.** Measured ticks per second: 1280x720 gives 12, 640x360 gives 42, 320x180 gives 60. Run browser tests at 320x180; only then does a 10-second attract timer take 10 seconds. Slow rendering at large sizes is not a game bug.\nPLAN.md-531-- Chromium flags that work: `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`. The set with `--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader` also works. Only Chromium has WebGPU here: Firefox and WebKit show the page's no-WebGPU message.\nPLAN.md-532-- Run your own Playwright scripts with plain `python3`. `python3 -I` cannot import Playwright here (verified).\nPLAN.md-533-- **Server port through a pipe:** `python3 -m http.server 0` buffers its \"port\" line when piped, and a script reading it hangs forever. Use `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory <dir>`. Stop only that PID, from a `finally` and a SIGTERM handler.\nPLAN.md-534-- **Controller stub (verified: gilrs reads it, stick moves the player, Cross registers):**\n--\nPLAN.md-541-```\nPLAN.md-542-- **Measuring sound (verified):** cpal plays `AudioBufferSourceNode`s, so patch `AudioBufferSourceNode.prototype.start` in an init script, read `this.buffer.getChannelData(0)`, and accumulate RMS and peak. Sample rate 48000; context `running` after a click.\nPLAN.md-543-\nPLAN.md-544-Engine:\nPLAN.md:545:- `egui::Context::set_fonts` takes effect next pass; using a font family in the same pass panics \"not bound to any fonts\". Install fonts before the first `run_ui`, in `App::new` and in `Headless::frame`, which makes a new context per frame. In the browser that panic stopped the frame loop with nothing on the page to say so: `__gameStatus` simply stopped changing (verified). Log console errors and assert that the tick advances in every browser test.\nPLAN.md-546-- **Blob colour** is `shirt`. **Rounded legend tiles** make stripes. **Default water** is a strong blue until the zone has a `color`.\nPLAN.md-547-- **Mirror view is yaw 0.** The default figure faces +Z, toward a yaw-0 camera. A room `[camera]` of yaw 180 shows its back (verified).\nPLAN.md-548-- **Horizon lines:** full-scene outlines draw a dark line at the sea's edge; `outlines_on = \"objects\"` removes it (verified).\nPLAN.md-549-- **Standing on water without swimming (verified):** floor blocks with top at `-0.06` inside a water zone with `y1 = 0`. Posture stays `stand`, `swimming` false.\n--\nPLAN.md-555-- The harness's Enter key test applies only to a game's own card. With the hub's card there is no key test.\nPLAN.md-556-\nPLAN.md-557-## 16. Testing\nPLAN.md-558-\nPLAN.md:559:One command: `tests/run.sh [core|browser|hub|all]`. It prints only failures and a final line like `212 passed, 0 failed`. Rerun a part only after changing code it covers. Keep a running count in `notes/feedback.md` of issues found and how bad, so your testing feedback is honest.\nPLAN.md-560-\nPLAN.md-561-**`core` (`cargo test -q --locked -p pav_core --test fit`, then `cargo test -q --locked -p pav_audio -p pav_ui`; seconds to run once built):**\nPLAN.md-562-- The bot plays New Stay to credits on 3 seeds: outcome Won, 5 stamps, every event played, under 60 sim-minutes.\nPLAN.md-563-- Each event: the bot earns at least 2 stars on 5 seeds; idle input earns under 1 star; a careless random input earns less than the bot.\n--\nPLAN.md-565-- Morning Check: better input gives a lower age; bounds hold.\nPLAN.md-566-- Attract: starts at 600 idle ticks, cycles all events, any input exits, saves nothing.\nPLAN.md-567-- Pause freezes the world. Settings: music defaults to 0.10. Dev sliders change values and reset. Dev jump lands where it says.\nPLAN.md-568-- Save round trip and version. Medley on a seed gives the same score for the same inputs. Play Together completes. Ghosts match by area.\nPLAN.md:569:- Snapshot, rewind and replay exactness (copy `crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs`).\nPLAN.md-570-- UI: `Headless::frame` readings show the right prompts per device and glyph setting; no text under the size rule (enforce in the draw helper).\nPLAN.md-571-- Audio: music at 10% is 0.10 of full-scale render; every SFX and song is non-silent; speakers differ.\nPLAN.md-572-- Content lint: no `TODO` or placeholder text in `script.toml`, and every event has a card, rules and a bot.\nPLAN.md-573-\nPLAN.md:574:**`browser` (Playwright, one browser, 320x180, `file://`):** boots with no errors; `__gameStatus` appears; the pad stub moves focus and confirms; keyboard does the same; mouse hover moves focus and click activates, using rects the UI publishes in `window.__gameUi`; prompts switch with the device; Settings has the Xbox option; attract starts after 10 s and any input exits it; music reaches about 10% by the sound patch. Touch: Chromium with a phone and a tablet profile (it has WebGPU) must show \"Controller or keyboard required\", run attract, and respond to a Settings tap by `page.touchscreen.tap`. WebKit with an iPhone profile, which has no WebGPU here, must show the fallback message from section 11.\nPLAN.md-575-\nPLAN.md-576-**`hub`:** copy the page and `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` into one served folder, open `harness.html?game=<page>&players=N&auto=1`, wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === \"true\"`, and require `window.__hubCheck.pass`. Run 2 players; 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; and `scenario=host-leave`. Then a solo check like the hub's: open outside a session, press Enter and Space, expect no errors, `AIHub.active` false, and `Math.random` not seeded. Also byte-compare the pasted client with `hub/session.js`.\nPLAN.md-577-\nPLAN.md-578-**Second player:** the harness's copies, the only multi-player check possible on one computer. **TV:** judge 1920x1080 `pav capture`s.\n--\nPLAN.md-580-**Screenshots** only for what scripts cannot check: `pav capture` for composition, `filmstrip` and `animsheet` for motion, one 1080p sheet per set at the end. Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\nPLAN.md-581-\nPLAN.md-582-## 17. Build order\nPLAN.md-583-\nPLAN.md:584:Each step ends with its tests passing. Early steps close the risks first.\nPLAN.md-585-\nPLAN.md:586:1. **Setup.** Pick the title. `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall engine` (it is public). Copy the starter to `games/fit/`, register it, build `pav` and the web page, first `tests/run.sh`.\nPLAN.md:587:2. **Seams.** Hide the chrome, fit input layout, `lean`, fonts, `fit_ui` with a Title and a Pause, Flow state machine, `weblink`, `__gameStatus`, save, a one-event Medley stub, hub JS. Get the harness and the browser smoke green now, before content exists.\nPLAN.md-588-3. **First slice.** Balance Core, Puck, tilt, `studio` set, Pose Parade, event card and result, bot, one result screen in full art. Play it by bot and capture it. Tune until a ring streak feels good.\nPLAN.md-589-4. **Island and voice.** `hub` set and props, walking, interactables, dialogue with syllables, audio buses, Lobby Bossa, Pip, the Morning Check, Balance Age, Calendar, Clam.\nPLAN.md-590-5. **Events** in this order: Cannonball Cup, Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Tempo Squats, Breath Bloom, Step Party (with sequencer and rhythm clock), Morning Lap, Plank Standoff, Floatie Spin, Tray Trek.\nPLAN.md-591-6. **Meta.** Days, unlocks, titles, wardrobe, flip-flops, Yesterday You, absence comments, all songs and SFX.\n--\nPLAN.md-599-\nPLAN.md-600-## 18. Finishing\nPLAN.md-601-\nPLAN.md-602-1. Write the exit interview your brief names. Fill every field honestly; `usage` is exactly \"added on import\". Suggested `aiHub` values: type `Game`, genre `Sports`, source `Wii Fit`, series `Wii Fit`, players `1–4`, tags from `3d`, `third-person`, `comedy`, `sports`, `versus`, `low-poly`. Check that it parses.\nPLAN.md:603:2. Run `tools/build.sh`: copy the exit interview into `about-data` in the page, run the single-file build with your title, description and theme colour, and write the HTML where your brief says. The About screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback from that block, including the fonts' and motion libraries' credits (`engine/store/CREDITS.md`, each clip set's `credit`).\nPLAN.md:604:3. Run `tests/run.sh all` on the final page. Open it once from `file://` at 1920x1080 and look at one frame.\nPLAN.md:605:4. Put the same Source Information and feedback in your chat reply.\nPLAN.md:606:5. Delete `engine/target` and other caches. Leave the source, tests and notes in the dev folder.\nPLAN.md-607-\nPLAN.md-608-### What each brief item maps to\nPLAN.md-609-\nPLAN.md-610-| Brief item | Section |\n--\nPLAN.md-628-| Narrative tone | 7 |\nPLAN.md-629-| 10-foot, controller-first, native keyboard and mouse, glyphs, Xbox option, no dense screens | 3, 11 |\nPLAN.md-630-| Touch-only behaviour | 11, 12 |\nPLAN.md-631-| No TODOs or stubs | 16, 17 |\nPLAN.md:632:| Source Information and all feedback in chat and on About, exit interview | 11, 14, 18 |\n--\nTASK.md-20-\nTASK.md-21-Online: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub\nTASK.md-22-\nTASK.md-23-Working Environment and deliverable:\nTASK.md:24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\nTASK.md-25-\nTASK.md-26-Performance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\nTASK.md-27-\nTASK.md-28-Testing: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n--\nTASK.md-88-\nTASK.md-89-## Done\nTASK.md-90-No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\nTASK.md-91-\nTASK.md:92:## Source Information\nTASK.md:93:CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\nTASK.md-94-- Date: 2026-11-04 22:27:01\nTASK.md-95-- Source: the work it's based on\nTASK.md-96-- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\nTASK.md-97-- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n--\nTASK.md-105-- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\nTASK.md-106-- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\nTASK.md-107-- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\nTASK.md-108-\nTASK.md:109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\nTASK.md-110-{\nTASK.md-111-  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\nTASK.md:112:  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\nTASK.md:113:  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\nTASK.md:114:  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\nTASK.md-115-  \"aiHub\": {\nTASK.md-116-    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\nTASK.md-117-    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\nTASK.md-118-    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n--\nTASK.md-126-  }\nTASK.md-127-}\nTASK.md-128-The catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\nTASK.md-129-\nTASK.md:130:Testing Feedback\nTASK.md-131-\nTASK.md-132-- How many issues did testing catch?\nTASK.md-133-- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\nTASK.md-134-- What was the most helpful test you ran?\nTASK.md-135-- What was the least helpful test you ran?\nTASK.md-136-\nTASK.md:137:Engine Feedback\nTASK.md-138-\nTASK.md-139-- What did you like most about the engine?\nTASK.md-140-- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\nTASK.md-141-- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\nTASK.md-142-- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\nTASK.md-143-- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\nTASK.md-144-- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\nTASK.md-145-\nTASK.md:146:Prompt Feedback\nTASK.md-147-\nTASK.md-148-- What did you like most about this prompt?\nTASK.md-149-- What was confusing?\nTASK.md-150-- What was the hardest thing to do?\n--- hub API ---\n189-\n190-  /** A plain JSON copy, or undefined when it is not JSON. */\n191:  function json(value) {\n192-    try {\n193-      var text = JSON.stringify(value);\n--\n413-    for (var key in outcome) {\n414-      if (!own(outcome, key)) continue;\n415:      var value = json(outcome[key]);\n416-      if (value !== undefined) copy[key] = value;\n417-      else if (outcome[key] !== undefined) warn('the outcome\\'s ' + key + ' is not JSON: left out');\n--\n447-  };\n448-\n449:  function sendProgress() {\n450-    progressTimer = null;\n451-    if (!nextProgress || ended || reported) return;\n--- relevant CSS ---\n2:html,body{background:#a7e8e5}body{overflow:hidden}#msg,#turn{display:none!important}body>canvas:not(#world){position:fixed!important;inset:0;z-index:-2;pointer-events:none}#world{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:0;display:block;width:100vw!important;height:100vh!important;height:100dvh!important;pointer-events:none}#app{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:2;overflow:hidden}button{font:inherit;color:inherit;cursor:pointer}button:focus-visible{outline:4px solid #ffca66;outline-offset:3px}.screen{height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:clamp(18px,3.2vw,54px);display:flex;flex-direction:column}.topbar{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;flex:none}.logo{font-size:14px;font-weight:1000;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase}.logo i{font-style:normal;color:#ec765f}.pill,.eyebrow{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase}.pill{padding:10px 14px;background:rgba(255,253,242,.84);box-shadow:0 3px 0 rgba(25,90,91,.12)}.eyebrow{color:#087e7a}.sun-dot{width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:50%;background:#ffab65}.title-layout{flex:1;min-height:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(300px,520px) 1fr;align-items:center;gap:3vw}.title-panel{max-width:530px}.overline{font-size:clamp(11px,1vw,15px);font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#1c7775}.title-panel h1,.headline{font-size:clamp(50px,7vw,102px);line-height:.88;letter-spacing:-.065em;margin:18px 0 20px;font-weight:1000}.title-