{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_145","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -i 'hub:|multiplayer|single.file|feedback|test|ai hub|engine' PLAN.md TASK.md | head -100; sed -n '1,160p' 'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/scripts/bundle.py'; sed -n '1,120p' 'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/hub/session.js' | head -100; rg -n 'function .*result|result:|result\\\\s*\\\\(' 'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/hub/session.js' | head\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_145","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -i 'hub:|multiplayer|single.file|feedback|test|ai hub|engine' PLAN.md TASK.md | head -100; sed -n '1,160p' 'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/scripts/bundle.py'; sed -n '1,120p' 'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/hub/session.js' | head -100; rg -n 'function .*result|result:|result\\\\s*\\\\(' 'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/hub/session.js' | head\"","aggregated_output":"TASK.md:13:Tech Stack: Build on https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall/blob/main/START_HERE.md, making a new game on its engine. You may change anything in it, the engine included, and add whatever systems, art assets and animations the game needs. The rest of the tech stack is your choice.\nTASK.md:15:Art Direction: Use the engine’s native style as the base. Make new art assets for whatever makes the game feel like the source; the engine’s asset library is fine for generic props.\nTASK.md:17:Animation: Use the engine’s native animation system as the base. Make new animations for whatever makes the game feel like the source.\nTASK.md:24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\nTASK.md:28:Testing: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\nTASK.md:50:No script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\nTASK.md:55:- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\nTASK.md:74:Include a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\nTASK.md:78:Multiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\nTASK.md:93:CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\nTASK.md:98:- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\nTASK.md:103:- Testing: testing parameters allowed\nTASK.md:107:- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\nTASK.md:109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\nTASK.md:111:  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\nTASK.md:112:  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\nTASK.md:113:  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\nTASK.md:114:  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\nTASK.md:130:Testing Feedback\nTASK.md:132:- How many issues did testing catch?\nTASK.md:134:- What was the most helpful test you ran?\nTASK.md:135:- What was the least helpful test you ran?\nTASK.md:137:Engine Feedback\nTASK.md:139:- What did you like most about the engine?\nTASK.md:142:- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\nTASK.md:143:- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\nTASK.md:144:- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\nTASK.md:146:Prompt Feedback\nPLAN.md:7:- **Your brief** means the brief in your own working folder. It wins on the title method, file and folder names, dates, the deliverables and the feedback questions. This plan names none of them.\nPLAN.md:8:- **Paths** are relative to the dev folder your brief tells you to create. Clone the engine to `engine/` inside it.\nPLAN.md:11:- **Verified** means it was run on this computer on 2026-11-04, against engine commit `49ef2ba` and AI Hub client 1.4.0. Section 15 lists those results.\nPLAN.md:13:- **Reading cost:** you do not need to read the engine's source to start. Read `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` whole (about 3k tokens) and `engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/starter.rs`, then use this plan. Search `engine/docs/REFERENCE.md` and `engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md` when you need a tool or a prop field.\nPLAN.md:17:You have won a five-day stay at Tippy Cay, a small wellness resort staffed entirely by talking gym equipment. You do not remember entering. Each morning a relentlessly pleasant wobble cushion tests your balance and gives you a Balance Age. Each day you walk the island, try short stillness, strength, cardio and balance events, and bank minutes in a giant clam. Checkout requires a Balance Age of 40 or better. Day 5 ends in the Big Stand, a finale whose last test is to do nothing at all for thirty seconds while the game tries to make you press something.\nPLAN.md:26:| The body test and the verdict of a fitness age | The Morning Wobble Check and Balance Age. Never weight, BMI or body shape |\nPLAN.md:32:| A family sharing one board and comparing progress | Hot-seat Medley, Yesterday You ghosts, AI Hub sessions |\nPLAN.md:92:Xbox glyphs (Settings option) swap A B X Y, LB RB LT RT, Menu. Ignore Options while Create is held: that pair belongs to the AI Hub. Disable the engine's own keys (F1 to F10, digits, H, Backspace rewind, right-drag tilt) outside dev mode. Keep F11 for fullscreen.\nPLAN.md:115:**Body:** the figure tilts with the dot (`cob * 14` degrees about the feet, engine change in section 14). Beyond |cob| 0.75 an upper-body arm-flail clip fades in. A tip plays a stumble and, over water, a splash. Tips never end the game; they cost time or score.\nPLAN.md:123:**Every event has:** a section of tunable numbers in `rules.toml`, a bot that earns at least 2 stars, an idle-input outcome below 1 star, a ghost lane, and an attract segment. Scenes `fit/event/<name>` start an event directly, for tools and tests.\nPLAN.md:166:### Morning Wobble Check. Set: `studio`. About 70 s, four micro-tests, Pip presiding.\nPLAN.md:168:| Test | What you do | Metric (0 to 1) |\nPLAN.md:170:| Stand Still (\"This is the whole test\") | Hold the dot centred for 8 s; one small nudge at 5 s | Mean distance from centre |\nPLAN.md:173:| Step Test | 8 alternating steps to a 100 BPM metronome | Timing |\nPLAN.md:186:- **Wardrobe:** reuse the engine's `GearLook`, which needs no new drawing (verified): `helm = cap` (sun cap), `helm = hood` (towel turban), `crown`, `halo`; `gloves` (sweatbands), `belt`, `pauldrons` (reads as arm floaties, funny). Plus shirt, pants and shoe colours. Skip `cape`: it draws long sticks.\nPLAN.md:229:**Base:** the engine's native look: cel-shaded rounded primitives, soft sun shadows, thin ink outlines on characters. Its big-headed toy figures already suit the tone. Take the look high-key and pastel.\nPLAN.md:270:**New props.** Hand-write format-2 JSON (`engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md`) into `engine/assets/props/lib/core/<name>.json`; that folder is embedded in every build, including the browser. Use them as `asset = \"LIB/core/<name>\"`. A rebuild of `pav` is needed before `room_check` can see a new file (verified). A leaning palm (cone trunk, 6 radial ellipsoid fronds) and a kettlebell (sphere and torus) looked good on the first try. Check each with `asset_preview name=x views=true figure=true`.\nPLAN.md:285:**Base:** the engine's puppet (procedural walk, idle, landing, squash and stretch) with motion clips on top.\nPLAN.md:289:**Hand-keyed clips (verified feasible).** Write readable key poses into `engine/anim/fit.json`. Test without rebuilding: in `pav repl` run `anim_reload`, then `animsheet clip=FIT/Tree frames=1 size=300 out=out/tree.png`. The build embeds every `anim/*.json`. A tree pose, a warrior lunge and a squat were recognisable at the first attempt:\nPLAN.md:302:Field meanings are in `LEGEND` at the top of `engine/crates/pav_core/src/clips.rs`: `hips [forward, right, up]` in percent of standing hip height; `body`, `chest` and `head [turn, lean, tilt]` in degrees; limbs `[forward, out, up, bend, twist]`. The plank attempt pointed its legs up, so start the plank from `MESH2MOTION/Pushup`'s key instead.\nPLAN.md:315:- **Rhythm clock:** the mixer counts rendered samples in an atomic. `pav_app` reads it, runs a small phase-locked clock (`clock += dt; clock += (audio_pos - clock) * 0.05`), subtracts a latency offset (default 0.10 s, Settings: Rhythm Offset), and sends it as `InputFrame.song_pos`. The sim uses `song_pos` when present, its own tick time otherwise. Replays and tests stay deterministic, because the value is part of the recorded input.\nPLAN.md:335:**Route: egui in `pav_ui`, painter-drawn, no default windows.** This was verified at 1920x1080: rounded fonts, soft-shadow cards and painted glyphs look right and appear in headless `pav capture`. Keep all UI state in the sim (section 14), so tests can drive it.\nPLAN.md:337:**Fonts:** `npm pack @expo-google-fonts/fredoka` and `@expo-google-fonts/nunito` (SIL OFL, static TTFs). Unpack into their own folder and copy `Fredoka_600SemiBold.ttf` (titles, 50 KB) and `Nunito_700Bold.ttf` (body, 132 KB) to `engine/crates/pav_ui/fonts/`. Embed with `include_bytes!`. Credit them on the About screen.\nPLAN.md:361:**Touch-only devices:** detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')`, no `(any-pointer: fine)`, and no gamepad or key seen yet. Show a centred card \"Controller or keyboard required\" and a Settings button (tap works; Settings is usable by tap). No touch controls: skip Shardfall's `touch.draw` for this game, and route touches directly to egui in `on_touch`, because the engine's touch layer otherwise treats a finger as a stick. Attract mode runs behind the card. Remove the phone-rotation hint and fullscreen-on-tap from `web/index.html`. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, drop the card and start normally. A touch device without WebGPU cannot run the game at all, so the page's own fallback message there says both things: \"Controller or keyboard required\" and that the game needs WebGPU.\nPLAN.md:368:- **View:** input viewer, dot trace, engine stats overlay, free camera, ghost lanes.\nPLAN.md:377:## 13. Multiplayer\nPLAN.md:379:**AI Hub session: mode `ghost`, 1 to 4 players.** Follow `lib/hub/README.md` in `michaelcrosato/ai-hub`. `ghost` is the choice because seeing friends wobble on the next mat is the fun of it, and it is barely more work than `parallel`; `shared-world` would need a host-run world this game does not need. Download `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` to `hub/`; these URLs work without auth (verified).\nPLAN.md:389:<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\nPLAN.md:390:<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\nPLAN.md:391:<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\nPLAN.md:392:<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\nPLAN.md:393:<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Highest total across three balance events wins\">\nPLAN.md:394:<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Act: Cross, Space or click\">\nPLAN.md:395:<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\nPLAN.md:398:**Hub logic lives in about 30 lines of plain JS in the page; Rust only reads and writes window fields.** This exact block passed the harness on a real engine build at 2 players, at 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, and with `scenario=host-leave`, in 14 to 19 s each, and the page ran clean outside a session (verified):\nPLAN.md:433:The game's status JSON carries `hub: { score, label, done, stats, ghost }`. Rust passes `__hub.go` to the sim as a button bit, draws `__hub.ghosts`, and stops input and sound on `__hub.ended`. The JS timers keep reporting while software rendering runs slowly, so the checks pass at low frame rates.\nPLAN.md:437:**The game on its own.** `AIHub.active` is false and nothing above runs. `Math.random` stays the browser's own. The hub's solo check opens the page, presses Enter and Space, and looks for errors and a drawn screen. Multiplayer exists here too, on one device:\nPLAN.md:441:These reuse the hub's ghost drawing and scoring, so there is one multiplayer system with three sources of ghosts.\nPLAN.md:445:**Decision: all game state and flow live in the sim, in one `Game`.** Menus, dialogue, pause, settings values and dev toggles are state in `FitGame`, driven by `InputFrame`, so `cargo test` can play the whole game with no browser or GPU in seconds. `pav_ui` is a pure view of a `UiFrame`: it draws the frame, and returns what the pointer hovered and clicked, which the app sends back as `InputFrame.ui` (clear PRIMARY that frame if the UI took the click) and publishes as item rects in `window.__gameUi` for browser tests. Pause freezes the world by an early return in `Sim::step_inner`, not by `TimeControl`.\nPLAN.md:448:engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/\nPLAN.md:458:engine/anim/fit.json                 hand-keyed clips\nPLAN.md:459:engine/assets/props/lib/core/*.json  props\nPLAN.md:460:engine/crates/pav_ui/src/fit_ui.rs, glyphs.rs, fonts/\nPLAN.md:461:engine/crates/pav_audio/src/music.rs, voice.rs\nPLAN.md:462:engine/crates/pav_app/src/weblink.rs  window field reads and writes\nPLAN.md:463:engine/web/index.html                 hub client, tags, JS, about-data\nPLAN.md:464:tests/  tools/  hub/  notes/  README.md  (how to add an event, set or song)\nPLAN.md:466:Register it as `entry::<fit::FitGame>(..., fit::build)`, `KEY = \"fit\"`. Scene names: `fit`, `fit/medley`, `fit/event/<name>`. Read data with `games::level_text(\"fit/rules\", include_str!(\"rules.toml\"))`: running from `engine/`, it reads the disk file, so text, numbers and set layouts change with no rebuild. Do not put sets in `engine/rooms/`: that folder feeds the pavilion demo.\nPLAN.md:491:| `pav_core/src/input.rs` | Add to `InputFrame`: `lean: Vec2`, `any: bool`, `ui: Option<UiEvent>` (Copy: `Hover(u16)`, `Click(u16)`, `Slider(u16, f32)`), `song_pos: Option<f32>`, all `#[serde(default)]`. New `buttons`: CONFIRM, BACK, MENU_UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT, TAB_L, TAB_R, PAUSE, SCHEDULE, WAVE, STEP_L, STEP_R, HUB_GO | Everything the game needs is input, so replays and tests cover it |\nPLAN.md:500:| `pav_app/src/app.rs` | When `hud.fit` is set: hide `boot_panel`, `stats_panel`, `guide_panel`, the room card, `hint_bar` and the F1 panel (verified necessary); route Esc and Options to PAUSE instead of `set_menu`; gate `handle_key`; call `weblink` each frame; apply Settings to audio buses; save to `localStorage` when the save serial changes; keep fit bindings in the room-change branch, which otherwise rebinds keys | Removes the engine demo's chrome and keys |\nPLAN.md:523:- `cargo build --locked -p pav_tools --bin pav`: 1m53 first time, 15 to 70 s after. Run from `engine/`.\nPLAN.md:524:- `cargo test --locked -p pav_core --test games`: about 75 s build, under 1 s run.\nPLAN.md:525:- `scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene fit --title \"...\" --out <path>`: 2m24 first time, 52 s after. Output about 11.4 MB. The wasm target and `wasm-bindgen 0.2.129` are ready. `--out` takes your brief's file name.\nPLAN.md:530:- **Software rendering is slow, so size the window to the test.** Measured ticks per second: 1280x720 gives 12, 640x360 gives 42, 320x180 gives 60. Run browser tests at 320x180; only then does a 10-second attract timer take 10 seconds. Slow rendering at large sizes is not a game bug.\nPLAN.md:544:Engine:\nPLAN.md:545:- `egui::Context::set_fonts` takes effect next pass; using a font family in the same pass panics \"not bound to any fonts\". Install fonts before the first `run_ui`, in `App::new` and in `Headless::frame`, which makes a new context per frame. In the browser that panic stopped the frame loop with nothing on the page to say so: `__gameStatus` simply stopped changing (verified). Log console errors and assert that the tick advances in every browser test.\nPLAN.md:551:- Run only your own test targets. The engine's other suites check its own catalogue and docs, and a new prop will fail its index check. You do not need them.\nPLAN.md:553:Hub:\nPLAN.md:555:- The harness's Enter key test applies only to a game's own card. With the hub's card there is no key test.\nPLAN.md:557:## 16. Testing\nPLAN.md:559:One command: `tests/run.sh [core|browser|hub|all]`. It prints only failures and a final line like `212 passed, 0 failed`. Rerun a part only after changing code it covers. Keep a running count in `notes/feedback.md` of issues found and how bad, so your testing feedback is honest.\nPLAN.md:561:**`core` (`cargo test -q --locked -p pav_core --test fit`, then `cargo test -q --locked -p pav_audio -p pav_ui`; seconds to run once built):**\nPLAN.md:569:- Snapshot, rewind and replay exactness (copy `crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs`).\nPLAN.md:584:Each step ends with its tests passing. Early steps close the risks first.\nPLAN.md:586:1. **Setup.** Pick the title. `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall engine` (it is public). Copy the starter to `games/fit/`, register it, build `pav` and the web page, first `tests/run.sh`.\nPLAN.md:594:9. **Multiplayer.** Full Medley, hub ghosts in every lane, Play Together.\nPLAN.md:603:2. Run `tools/build.sh`: copy the exit interview into `about-data` in the page, run the single-file build with your title, description and theme colour, and write the HTML where your brief says. The About screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback from that block, including the fonts' and motion libraries' credits (`engine/store/CREDITS.md`, each clip set's `credit`).\nPLAN.md:604:3. Run `tests/run.sh all` on the final page. Open it once from `file://` at 1920x1080 and look at one frame.\nPLAN.md:605:4. Put the same Source Information and feedback in your chat reply.\nPLAN.md:606:5. Delete `engine/target` and other caches. Leave the source, tests and notes in the dev folder.\nPLAN.md:616:| Build on the engine, change anything | 14 |\nPLAN.md:620:| Online and multiplayer, in the hub and on its own | 13, 16 |\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\n\n\ndev = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nroot = dev.parent\nhtml = (dev / \"game.raw.html\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\ncss = (dev / \"web/game.css\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\nhub = (dev / \"hub/session.js\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\ngame = (dev / \"web/game.js\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\nabout = json.loads((root / \"exit-interview.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n\nfor script in (hub, game):\n    if \"</script\" in script.lower():\n        raise ValueError(\"Inline script contains an HTML closing script tag\")\n\nhtml = html.replace(\"</head>\", f\"<style>{css}\\n#msg,#turn{{display:none!important}}</style></head>\", 1)\nhtml = html.replace(\"<body>\", '<body><canvas id=\"world\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></canvas><main id=\"app\"></main>', 1)\nhtml = html.replace(\"document.querySelector('canvas')\", \"document.querySelector('canvas:not(#world)')\")\nhtml = html.replace(\"c.focus();\", \"\")\nhtml = html.replace(\"if (matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches)\", \"if (false)\")\nabout_json = json.dumps(about, ensure_ascii=True).replace(\"</\", \"<\\\\/\")\nhtml = html.replace(\"</body>\", f\"<script>{hub}</script><script>window.__aboutData={about_json};</script><script>{game}</script></body>\", 1)\n(root / f\"{dev.name}.html\").write_text(html, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\n      },\n    };\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\n    return new Proxy(api, {\n      get: function (t, k) {\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\n      },\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\n        return true;\n      },\n      has: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data || k in t;\n      },\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\n        delete data[k];\n        return true;\n      },\n      ownKeys: function () {\n        return Object.keys(data);\n      },\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\n  function generator(a) {\n    return function () {\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n      var t = a;\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n    };\n  }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
