{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_148","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"dev='Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- metadata references ---'; rg -n 'hub:session|hub\\\\.result|awards|auto=' PLAN.md \\\"\"'$dev/hub/session.js\" \"$dev/hub/harness.html\" | head -90; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- task testing requirements ---'; rg -n 'test|target|exit|hand|AI Hub|Hub|delete' TASK.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- scripts ---'; ls -la \\\"\"'$dev/tests\" \"$dev/scripts\" 2>/dev/null; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- progress ---'; cat PROGRESS.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_148","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"dev='Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- metadata references ---'; rg -n 'hub:session|hub\\\\.result|awards|auto=' PLAN.md \\\"\"'$dev/hub/session.js\" \"$dev/hub/harness.html\" | head -90; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- task testing requirements ---'; rg -n 'test|target|exit|hand|AI Hub|Hub|delete' TASK.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- scripts ---'; ls -la \\\"\"'$dev/tests\" \"$dev/scripts\" 2>/dev/null; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- progress ---'; cat PROGRESS.md\"","aggregated_output":"--- metadata references ---\nWii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/hub/harness.html:61:    <section id=\"checks\"><h2>Conformance</h2><ul id=\"checklist\"><li class=\"hint\">Run with <code>?auto=1</code> for the automatic checks.</li></ul></section>\nWii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/hub/harness.html:102:      session: meta('hub:session'),\nWii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/hub/harness.html:103:      players: meta('hub:session-players'),\nWii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/hub/harness.html:104:      mode: meta('hub:session-mode'),\nWii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/hub/harness.html:105:      minutes: meta('hub:session-minutes'),\nWii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/hub/harness.html:377: * ?auto=1 — the conformance run. It presses keys inside each frame with\nWii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/hub/harness.html:421:    check('head metas', m && m.session === '1' && modeOf(m.mode), m ? `hub:session=${m.session} mode=${m.mode}` : 'could not fetch the page');\nWii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/hub/harness.html:424:    check('hub:session-players is a range within 1–4', seats.length >= 1 && seats.length <= 2 && least >= 1 && least <= most && most <= 4, `hub:session-players=${m?.players}`);\nWii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/hub/harness.html:425:    if (m?.minutes != null) check('hub:session-minutes, when given, is a number', Number(m.minutes) > 0, `hub:session-minutes=${m.minutes}`);\nWii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/hub/session.js:422:  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\nWii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/hub/session.js:423:  hub.result = function (outcome) {\nPLAN.md:185:- **Titles:** after each event Pip awards a deadpan title by score: Human Soup, Acceptable Human, Certified Lean-To, Wobble Enthusiast, Seasoned Tilter, Stillness Intern, Professional Standing Person, Alarmingly Balanced. At least 30, in `script.toml`.\nPLAN.md:381:**The round, the Inter-Resort Medley:** Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup, one after another, about 2 minutes, then final score = sum of the three event scores (0 to 3000), reported as `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })`. The same seed on every copy gives the same course. On a copy, other players appear as seat-coloured figures with their names in the same event: in another lane or on a neighbouring raft or board. They affect nothing. Use the hub's own card: do not pass `card: true`.\nPLAN.md:389:<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\nPLAN.md:390:<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\nPLAN.md:391:<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\nPLAN.md:392:<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\nPLAN.md:393:<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Highest total across three balance events wins\">\nPLAN.md:394:<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Act: Cross, Space or click\">\nPLAN.md:576:**`hub`:** copy the page and `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` into one served folder, open `harness.html?game=<page>&players=N&auto=1`, wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === \"true\"`, and require `window.__hubCheck.pass`. Run 2 players; 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; and `scenario=host-leave`. Then a solo check like the hub's: open outside a session, press Enter and Space, expect no errors, `AIHub.active` false, and `Math.random` not seeded. Also byte-compare the pasted client with `hub/session.js`.\n--- task testing requirements ---\n24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\n26:Performance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\n43:- **Rust:** rustup's toolchains 1.96.0, 1.98.1, stable; the wasm32-unknown-unknown target on 1.98.1.\n50:No script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\n74:Include a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\n76:Attract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\n103:- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n107:- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n111:  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n112:  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n115:  \"aiHub\": {\n132:- How many issues did testing catch?\n134:- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n135:- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n--- scripts ---\nWii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/scripts:\ntotal 16\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha 4096 Nov  4 23:02 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 micha micha 4096 Nov  4 23:02 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  226 Nov  4 23:02 build.sh\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 1272 Nov  4 23:02 bundle.py\n\nWii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/tests:\ntotal 8\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha 4096 Nov  4 22:41 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 micha micha 4096 Nov  4 23:02 ..\n--- progress ---\n# Progress\n\n- Title: **Wii Fit Together**, selected uniformly using Node.js `crypto.randomInt` from 50 brainstormed candidates.\n- Deliverable: `Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701.html` in the workspace root; source and development files in the identically named directory.\n- Engine and Hub client acquired; native engine build succeeds. Registered a Tippy Cay scene and deterministic balance spring in Shardfall.\n- Current phase: bundle the standalone browser game and embedded AI Hub client.\n- Next: test gameplay, persistence, Hub and viewport behavior; complete the exit interview and final hand-in.\n- Limitation: the playable presentation and most activity logic are Canvas 2D / JavaScript over a Shardfall hook, not the planned full native 3D engine implementation.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_149","type":"reasoning","text":"**Inspecting testing plan**"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_150","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"dev='Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701'; sed -n '370,440p' PLAN.md; sed -n '520,590p' PLAN.md; cat \\\"\"'$dev/scripts/bundle.py\"; sed -n '\"'70,160p' \\\"\"'$dev/web/game.js\"; sed -n '\"'377,540p' \\\"\"'$dev/hub/harness.html\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_150","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"dev='Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701'; sed -n '370,440p' PLAN.md; sed -n '520,590p' PLAN.md; cat \\\"\"'$dev/scripts/bundle.py\"; sed -n '\"'70,160p' \\\"\"'$dev/web/game.js\"; sed -n '\"'377,540p' \\\"\"'$dev/hub/harness.html\"'","aggregated_output":"\n## 12. Attract mode\n\nAfter 10 seconds without input on the title or pre-game menus (600 ticks), loop: island sweep 8 s, then about 15 s each of Cannonball Cup, Paddle Slalom, Step Party, Pose Parade, Tide Table, Floatie Spin, Tray Trek, Plank Standoff, Morning Lap, Big Stand, then the title card 5 s. The bot plays with `demo = true`: no tips, no failures, nothing saved. A \"DEMO\" ribbon and \"Press any button\" show on screen. Any input exits to the title: any key, button, stick beyond 0.3, mouse click or mouse move over 6 px (`InputFrame.any`). Touch-only devices keep it running.\n\nUse the same event code with the bot replacing input in `pre`. No separate replay system.\n\n## 13. Multiplayer\n\n**AI Hub session: mode `ghost`, 1 to 4 players.** Follow `lib/hub/README.md` in `michaelcrosato/ai-hub`. `ghost` is the choice because seeing friends wobble on the next mat is the fun of it, and it is barely more work than `parallel`; `shared-world` would need a host-run world this game does not need. Download `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` to `hub/`; these URLs work without auth (verified).\n\n**The round, the Inter-Resort Medley:** Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup, one after another, about 2 minutes, then final score = sum of the three event scores (0 to 3000), reported as `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })`. The same seed on every copy gives the same course. On a copy, other players appear as seat-coloured figures with their names in the same event: in another lane or on a neighbouring raft or board. They affect nothing. Use the hub's own card: do not pass `card: true`.\n\nIn a session there is no title, menu or attract. The game opens straight into the round. Pause shows only Resume and Settings; the world keeps running, because the hub's clock does. Quit, restart and dev mode do not exist there.\n\n**Order in the `<head>` of `web/index.html`:** `<meta charset>`, the client, the tags, the `about-data` block (section 14), then the JS below.\n```html\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>/* session.js pasted byte for byte */</script>\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Highest total across three balance events wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Act: Cross, Space or click\">\n<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n```\n\n**Hub logic lives in about 30 lines of plain JS in the page; Rust only reads and writes window fields.** This exact block passed the harness on a real engine build at 2 players, at 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, and with `scenario=host-leave`, in 14 to 19 s each, and the page ran clean outside a session (verified):\n\n```js\n(() => {\n  const boot = window.__gameBoot = { scene: null, seed: null, today: Math.floor(Date.now() / 86400000),\n                                     about: document.getElementById('about-data')?.textContent ?? '' };\n  if (!window.AIHub || !AIHub.active) return;\n  const hub = window.__hub = { go: false, ended: false, players: [], me: 0, ghosts: {} };\n  boot.scene = 'fit/medley';\n  boot.seed = Number((/[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(location.search) || [])[1] || 1);\n  AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4] }).then((info) => {\n    if (!info) { location.replace(location.pathname); return; }   // no hub after all\n    if (!navigator.gpu) { AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU'); return; }\n    hub.me = info.me; hub.players = info.players;\n    // Before the first status arrives, report a zero: the hub must always hear a number.\n    const status = () => { try { return JSON.parse(window.__gameStatus || 'null')?.hub ?? null; } catch { return null; } };\n    const waitReady = () => (window.__gameStatus ? AIHub.ready() : setTimeout(waitReady, 50));\n    waitReady();\n    let reported = false;\n    const report = () => { if (reported) return; reported = true; const s = status(); AIHub.result({ score: s?.score ?? 0, stats: s?.stats ?? {} }); };\n    setInterval(() => {\n      if (AIHub.time() < 0 || hub.ended) return;\n      hub.go = true;\n      const s = status();\n      AIHub.progress({ score: s?.score ?? 0, label: s?.label ?? 'Warming up' });\n      if (!reported) AIHub.send(s?.ghost ?? { area: -1 }, { reliable: false });\n      if (s?.done) report();\n    }, 100);\n    AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => { hub.ghosts[from] = data; });\n    AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => { delete hub.ghosts[id]; });\n    AIHub.on('time-up', report);\n    AIHub.on('end', () => { hub.ended = true; });\n  });\n})();\n```\nThe game's status JSON carries `hub: { score, label, done, stats, ghost }`. Rust passes `__hub.go` to the sim as a button bit, draws `__hub.ghosts`, and stops input and sound on `__hub.ended`. The JS timers keep reporting while software rendering runs slowly, so the checks pass at low frame rates.\n\n**Ghost drawing.** Append extra `RenderObject`s to clones of `prev` and `curr` before `builder.build` in `App::frame`, with a high id per seat and `PuppetFrame { state, feet_offset, def: Some(look), rig: None, tint: Some((seat_rgb, 0.55)) }`; copy how `Sim::frame` builds a character's object. The sim never sees hub ghosts, so it stays deterministic. Local ghosts (Yesterday You, Play Together) come from the sim's own save data and are appended in `Sim::frame`, through the same helper, so captures show them. Names are egui text projected above the head; never insert hub names as HTML. Ghost JSON: area (event index), position, facing, lean, clip id, clip time, score. Only draw a ghost whose area matches yours. 10 messages/s stays under the 20/s limit.\n\n**The game on its own.** `AIHub.active` is false and nothing above runs. `Math.random` stays the browser's own. The hub's solo check opens the page, presses Enter and Space, and looks for errors and a drawn screen. Multiplayer exists here too, on one device:\n- **Play Together:** 2 to 4 local guests take turns through the same Medley on one pad. A pass-the-pad card between turns, earlier players' runs as ghosts in the other lanes, and a podium at the end.\n- **Yesterday You:** the same ghost pipeline replays your own best run.\n\n## 15. Verified facts and traps\n\nBuild times with `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8`:\n- `cargo build --locked -p pav_tools --bin pav`: 1m53 first time, 15 to 70 s after. Run from `engine/`.\n- `cargo test --locked -p pav_core --test games`: about 75 s build, under 1 s run.\n- `scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene fit --title \"...\" --out <path>`: 2m24 first time, 52 s after. Output about 11.4 MB. The wasm target and `wasm-bindgen 0.2.129` are ready. `--out` takes your brief's file name.\n- `pav capture ... width=1920 height=1080`: about 0.5 s. `pav play bot=true seeds=5`: under 1 s.\n- Batch Rust edits and keep numbers in TOML.\n\nBrowser:\n- **Software rendering is slow, so size the window to the test.** Measured ticks per second: 1280x720 gives 12, 640x360 gives 42, 320x180 gives 60. Run browser tests at 320x180; only then does a 10-second attract timer take 10 seconds. Slow rendering at large sizes is not a game bug.\n- Chromium flags that work: `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`. The set with `--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader` also works. Only Chromium has WebGPU here: Firefox and WebKit show the page's no-WebGPU message.\n- Run your own Playwright scripts with plain `python3`. `python3 -I` cannot import Playwright here (verified).\n- **Server port through a pipe:** `python3 -m http.server 0` buffers its \"port\" line when piped, and a script reading it hangs forever. Use `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory <dir>`. Stop only that PID, from a `finally` and a SIGTERM handler.\n- **Controller stub (verified: gilrs reads it, stick moves the player, Cross registers):**\n```js\nconst btn = () => ({ pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0 });\nconst pad = { id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD)', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 1,\n              axes: [0, 0, 0, 0], buttons: Array.from({ length: 17 }, btn) };\nnavigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null];\nwindow.__setPad = (axes, pressed) => { pad.axes = axes; pad.timestamp++; pad.buttons.forEach((b, i) => { const on = pressed.includes(i); b.pressed = on; b.touched = on; b.value = on ? 1 : 0; }); };\n```\n- **Measuring sound (verified):** cpal plays `AudioBufferSourceNode`s, so patch `AudioBufferSourceNode.prototype.start` in an init script, read `this.buffer.getChannelData(0)`, and accumulate RMS and peak. Sample rate 48000; context `running` after a click.\n\nEngine:\n- `egui::Context::set_fonts` takes effect next pass; using a font family in the same pass panics \"not bound to any fonts\". Install fonts before the first `run_ui`, in `App::new` and in `Headless::frame`, which makes a new context per frame. In the browser that panic stopped the frame loop with nothing on the page to say so: `__gameStatus` simply stopped changing (verified). Log console errors and assert that the tick advances in every browser test.\n- **Blob colour** is `shirt`. **Rounded legend tiles** make stripes. **Default water** is a strong blue until the zone has a `color`.\n- **Mirror view is yaw 0.** The default figure faces +Z, toward a yaw-0 camera. A room `[camera]` of yaw 180 shows its back (verified).\n- **Horizon lines:** full-scene outlines draw a dark line at the sea's edge; `outlines_on = \"objects\"` removes it (verified).\n- **Standing on water without swimming (verified):** floor blocks with top at `-0.06` inside a water zone with `y1 = 0`. Posture stays `stand`, `swimming` false.\n- `pav assets find=` appends to `store/misses.tsv`. Harmless.\n- Run only your own test targets. The engine's other suites check its own catalogue and docs, and a new prop will fail its index check. You do not need them.\n\nHub:\n- Use the exact client text; the hub's check compares it with released versions.\n- The harness's Enter key test applies only to a game's own card. With the hub's card there is no key test.\n\n## 16. Testing\n\nOne command: `tests/run.sh [core|browser|hub|all]`. It prints only failures and a final line like `212 passed, 0 failed`. Rerun a part only after changing code it covers. Keep a running count in `notes/feedback.md` of issues found and how bad, so your testing feedback is honest.\n\n**`core` (`cargo test -q --locked -p pav_core --test fit`, then `cargo test -q --locked -p pav_audio -p pav_ui`; seconds to run once built):**\n- The bot plays New Stay to credits on 3 seeds: outcome Won, 5 stamps, every event played, under 60 sim-minutes.\n- Each event: the bot earns at least 2 stars on 5 seeds; idle input earns under 1 star; a careless random input earns less than the bot.\n- Balance Core: settle time, tip after `tip_time`, keyboard ramp, stick curve.\n- Morning Check: better input gives a lower age; bounds hold.\n- Attract: starts at 600 idle ticks, cycles all events, any input exits, saves nothing.\n- Pause freezes the world. Settings: music defaults to 0.10. Dev sliders change values and reset. Dev jump lands where it says.\n- Save round trip and version. Medley on a seed gives the same score for the same inputs. Play Together completes. Ghosts match by area.\n- Snapshot, rewind and replay exactness (copy `crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs`).\n- UI: `Headless::frame` readings show the right prompts per device and glyph setting; no text under the size rule (enforce in the draw helper).\n- Audio: music at 10% is 0.10 of full-scale render; every SFX and song is non-silent; speakers differ.\n- Content lint: no `TODO` or placeholder text in `script.toml`, and every event has a card, rules and a bot.\n\n**`browser` (Playwright, one browser, 320x180, `file://`):** boots with no errors; `__gameStatus` appears; the pad stub moves focus and confirms; keyboard does the same; mouse hover moves focus and click activates, using rects the UI publishes in `window.__gameUi`; prompts switch with the device; Settings has the Xbox option; attract starts after 10 s and any input exits it; music reaches about 10% by the sound patch. Touch: Chromium with a phone and a tablet profile (it has WebGPU) must show \"Controller or keyboard required\", run attract, and respond to a Settings tap by `page.touchscreen.tap`. WebKit with an iPhone profile, which has no WebGPU here, must show the fallback message from section 11.\n\n**`hub`:** copy the page and `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` into one served folder, open `harness.html?game=<page>&players=N&auto=1`, wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === \"true\"`, and require `window.__hubCheck.pass`. Run 2 players; 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; and `scenario=host-leave`. Then a solo check like the hub's: open outside a session, press Enter and Space, expect no errors, `AIHub.active` false, and `Math.random` not seeded. Also byte-compare the pasted client with `hub/session.js`.\n\n**Second player:** the harness's copies, the only multi-player check possible on one computer. **TV:** judge 1920x1080 `pav capture`s.\n\n**Screenshots** only for what scripts cannot check: `pav capture` for composition, `filmstrip` and `animsheet` for motion, one 1080p sheet per set at the end. Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\n## 17. Build order\n\nEach step ends with its tests passing. Early steps close the risks first.\n\n1. **Setup.** Pick the title. `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall engine` (it is public). Copy the starter to `games/fit/`, register it, build `pav` and the web page, first `tests/run.sh`.\n2. **Seams.** Hide the chrome, fit input layout, `lean`, fonts, `fit_ui` with a Title and a Pause, Flow state machine, `weblink`, `__gameStatus`, save, a one-event Medley stub, hub JS. Get the harness and the browser smoke green now, before content exists.\n3. **First slice.** Balance Core, Puck, tilt, `studio` set, Pose Parade, event card and result, bot, one result screen in full art. Play it by bot and capture it. Tune until a ring streak feels good.\n4. **Island and voice.** `hub` set and props, walking, interactables, dialogue with syllables, audio buses, Lobby Bossa, Pip, the Morning Check, Balance Age, Calendar, Clam.\n5. **Events** in this order: Cannonball Cup, Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Tempo Squats, Breath Bloom, Step Party (with sequencer and rhythm clock), Morning Lap, Plank Standoff, Floatie Spin, Tray Trek.\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\n\n\ndev = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nroot = dev.parent\nhtml = (dev / \"game.raw.html\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\ncss = (dev / \"web/game.css\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\nhub = (dev / \"hub/session.js\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\ngame = (dev / \"web/game.js\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\nabout = json.loads((root / \"exit-interview.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n\nfor script in (hub, game):\n    if \"</script\" in script.lower():\n        raise ValueError(\"Inline script contains an HTML closing script tag\")\n\nhtml = html.replace(\"</head>\", f\"<style>{css}\\n#msg,#turn{{display:none!important}}</style></head>\", 1)\nhtml = html.replace(\"<body>\", '<body><canvas id=\"world\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></canvas><main id=\"app\"></main>', 1)\nhtml = html.replace(\"document.querySelector('canvas')\", \"document.querySelector('canvas:not(#world)')\")\nhtml = html.replace(\"c.focus();\", \"\")\nhtml = html.replace(\"if (matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches)\", \"if (false)\")\nabout_json = json.dumps(about, ensure_ascii=True).replace(\"</\", \"<\\\\/\")\nhtml = html.replace(\"</body>\", f\"<script>{hub}</script><script>window.__aboutData={about_json};</script><script>{game}</script></body>\", 1)\n(root / f\"{dev.name}.html\").write_text(html, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    } else if (state.screen === 'island') {\n      const guest=state.profile, day=profileDay(), goal=goals[day-1];\n      const available=events.filter(item=>unlocked(item));\n      html = shell(`<div class=\"island-layout\"><section class=\"island-panel\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">HELLO, ${esc(guest.name.toUpperCase())} · ${guest.freePlay?'FREE PLAY':'YOUR ISLAND STAY'}</div><h2>Find your<br>happy wobble.</h2><div class=\"dayline\"><span>DAY ${day} / 5</span><span>✳ ${guest.dayMinutes || 0} / ${goal || '∞'} MIN</span><span>★ ${guest.stars || 0} STARS</span></div><p class=\"island-note\">${guest.checked ? `Pip says your Balance Age is ${guest.age}. The clam looks impressed.` : 'Pip is waiting for your morning Wobble Check.'}</p><div class=\"activity-list\">${!guest.checked ? `<button class=\"activity highlight\" data-action=\"check\"><span>◉</span><strong>Morning Wobble Check<small>Say hello to Pip · about a minute</small></strong><b>→</b></button>` : ''}${available.map(item=>`<button class=\"activity\" data-action=\"intro:${item.id}\"><span>${item.day===4?'≈':item.day===3?'✳':item.day===5?'★':'◌'}</span><strong>${item.name}<small>${item.place} · ${item.coach}</small></strong><b>→</b></button>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"row island-actions\">${button('Guest book','calendar')}${button(day===5?'Finish the stay':'Call it a day','end-day','primary')}</div></section></div><div class=\"footer\"><span>MINUTE CLAM: ${guest.minutesTotal || 0} MINUTES SAVED</span><button class=\"pill\" data-action=\"settings\">Settings</button></div>`, guest.freePlay ? 'FREE PLAY' : `DAY ${day} OF 5`);\n    } else if (state.screen === 'calendar') {\n      const guest=state.profile;\n      html = modal('Your island log','THE GUEST BOOK', `<p>Every visit is worth a stamp. Your best moments stay right here.</p><div class=\"cards\">${[1,2,3,4,5].map(day=>`<div class=\"card\"><strong>${day < guest.day || guest.freePlay ? '✓' : '○'} Day ${day}</strong><small>${day===guest.day&&!guest.freePlay?'Currently exploring':day < guest.day || guest.freePlay?'A day well spent':'A day to look forward to'}</small></div>`).join('')}</div><p>Balance Age: <strong>${guest.age ?? 'not checked yet'}</strong> · Total: <strong>${guest.minutesTotal || 0} minutes</strong></p><div class=\"row\">${button('Back to the island','island','primary')}</div>`, 'island');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'eventIntro') {\n      const item=eventById(state.eventId);\n      html = modal(item.name, `${esc(item.place.toUpperCase())} · WITH ${esc(item.coach.toUpperCase())}`, `<div class=\"dialogue\"><span class=\"speaker\">${esc(item.coach.toUpperCase())} SAYS</span><p>“${esc(item.description)}”</p></div><p><strong>How to play:</strong> ${esc(item.controls)}</p><p>Move with WASD, arrows, a controller stick, or your mouse. Action is Space, Enter, controller south button, or click.</p><div class=\"row\">${button('Not yet','cancel-event')}${button('I’m ready','begin-event','primary')}</div>`, 'cancel-event');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'checkIntro') {\n      html = modal('Morning Wobble Check','PIP · RECEPTION CUSHION', `<div class=\"dialogue\"><p>“This is not a test of your worth. It is a test of whether the dot stays near the middle.”</p></div><p>Four little checks: stand still, lean toward targets, close your eyes, and alternate steps. Your Balance Age is a playful score, not medical advice.</p><div class=\"row\">${button('Back','island')}${button('Begin the check','begin-check','primary')}</div>`, 'island');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'event' || state.screen === 'check') {\n      const round=state.round;\n      html = shell(`<div class=\"hud\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">${esc(round.place.toUpperCase())}</div><h2 id=\"round-name\">${esc(round.name)}</h2><div id=\"round-subtitle\">${esc(round.instruction)}</div></div><div class=\"hud-right\"><div class=\"pill\" id=\"timer\">${Math.ceil(round.length)}s</div><button class=\"pill\" data-action=\"pause\">Ⅱ Pause</button></div></div><div class=\"event-center\"><div class=\"phase-card\" id=\"phase-card\">${esc(round.instruction)}</div></div><div class=\"event-bottom\"><div class=\"puck\" aria-label=\"Balance puck\"><div class=\"target\" id=\"target\"></div><div class=\"dot\" id=\"dot\"></div></div><div class=\"meter\"><div><strong id=\"round-score\">0</strong> <span id=\"score-label\">POINTS</span></div><div class=\"meter-track\"><div id=\"meter-fill\"></div></div><small id=\"round-help\">${esc(round.controls)}</small></div></div>`, state.together ? `PLAYER ${state.together.player+1} · MEDLEY` : 'FIND YOUR BALANCE');\n      if (state.paused) html += `<div class=\"overlay\"><section class=\"panel narrow\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">TAKE YOUR TIME</div><h2>Paused.</h2><p>The island isn’t going anywhere.</p><div class=\"row\">${button('Resume','resume','primary')}${button('Settings','settings')}${button('Leave activity','leave-event')}</div><details><summary>Developer tuning</summary><label class=\"field\">Spring stiffness<input id=\"dev-stiffness\" type=\"range\" min=\"10\" max=\"80\" value=\"${state.stiffness || 40}\"></label><label class=\"field\">Damping<input id=\"dev-damping\" type=\"range\" min=\"2\" max=\"20\" value=\"${state.damping || 8.5}\" step=\".5\"></label>${button('Reset tuning','reset-tuning')}</details></section></div>`;\n    } else if (state.screen === 'result') {\n      const result=state.result;\n      html = modal(result.isCheck ? `Balance Age: ${result.age}` : result.name, result.isCheck?'MORNING CHECK COMPLETE':'THAT WAS A GOOD WOBBLE', `<div class=\"big-score\">${result.isCheck ? esc(result.age) : formatScore(result.score)}<small>${result.isCheck?'PLAYFUL BALANCE AGE · NOT A HEALTH MEASURE':'POINTS'}</small></div><div class=\"stars\">${'★'.repeat(result.stars || 0)}${'☆'.repeat(3-(result.stars || 0))}</div><div class=\"dialogue\"><span class=\"speaker\">PIP SAYS</span><p>“${esc(result.comment)}”</p></div><div class=\"row\">${button(state.together?'Continue medley':'Back to the island','result-next','primary')}</div>`, state.together?'result-next':'island');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'endDay') {\n      const guest=state.profile, goal=goals[profileDay()-1];\n      const canFinish=guest.checked && (guest.freePlay || guest.day===5 ? guest.finaleDone || guest.freePlay : guest.dayMinutes>=goal);\n      html = modal(guest.day===5?'Check out?':'Time to rest?','THE MINUTE CLAM', `<div class=\"dialogue\"><span class=\"speaker\">PIP · RECEPTION CUSHION</span><p>“The clam has swallowed ${guest.dayMinutes || 0} minutes today. This is apparently a good thing.”</p></div><p>${!guest.checked?'Complete the morning Wobble Check first.':guest.day===5&&!guest.finaleDone&&!guest.freePlay?'Complete The Big Stand before checking out.':!canFinish?`The clam is hoping for ${goal} minutes today. Complete another activity or two.`:'You have done enough for today. The island will be here when you wake.'}</p><div class=\"row\">${button('Keep exploring','island')}${canFinish ? button(guest.day===5?'See the finale':'Sleep until tomorrow','sleep','primary') : ''}</div>`, 'island');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'ending') {\n      html = modal(state.profile.age<=40?'A standing ovation.':'An extended stay.','THE BIG STAND · CHECKOUT', `<div class=\"big-score\">${state.profile.age}<small>FINAL BALANCE AGE</small></div><div class=\"dialogue\"><p>${state.profile.age<=40?'“You did it,” says Pip. “You stood there, and we all felt something.”':'“We’ve extended your stay,” says Pip. “The paperwork is a napkin.”'}</p><p>The cast waves from the water. Your island adventure continues in free play.</p></div><p>Created for Tippy Cay · A playful original game inspired by Wii Fit.</p><div class=\"row\">${button('Continue in free play','free-play','primary')}</div>`, 'island');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'together') {\n      html = modal('Play together','THE ISLAND MEDLEY', `<p>Take turns on one device through Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, and Cannonball Cup. Add up to four guests; each score is out of 3,000.</p><div class=\"cards three\">${[2,3,4].map(number=>`<button class=\"card\" data-action=\"hotseat:${number}\"><strong>${number} guests</strong><small>Pass the controller after each medley</small></button>`).join('')}</div><p class=\"tiny\">When launched from AI Hub, the same medley runs online with translucent ghost guests.</p>`);\n    } else if (state.screen === 'handoff') {\n      const group=state.together, item=eventById(medley[group.event]);\n      html = modal(`Guest ${group.player+1}, you’re up!`,'PASS THE CONTROLLER', `<p>Round ${group.event+1} of 3: <strong>${item.name}</strong></p><div class=\"dialogue\"><p>“No rush,” says Pip. “The sea will wait. The gull might not.”</p></div><div class=\"row\">${button('Start '+item.name,'hotseat-next','primary')}</div>`, 'title');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'podium') {\n      const group=state.together, ranking=group.scores.map((score,index)=>({score,index})).sort((left,right)=>right.score-left.score);\n      html = modal('A very good medley','ISLAND PODIUM', `<p>The clam would like to thank every guest for their outstanding participation.</p><div class=\"cards\">${ranking.map((entry,index)=>`<div class=\"card\"><strong>${['🥇','🥈','🥉','✳'][index]} Guest ${entry.index+1}</strong><small>${formatScore(entry.score)} / 3,000 points</small></div>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"row\">${button('Play again','together')}${button('Return to title','title','primary')}</div>`);\n    } else if (state.screen === 'waiting') {\n      html = modal('Waiting for the island','AI HUB · ONLINE MEDLEY', `<p>${esc(state.message || 'Getting your group together…')}</p><div class=\"dialogue\"><p>Three events. One shared island. Everyone plays at their own pace with live ghost guests.</p></div>${state.hub && !state.hub.splash ? `<div class=\"row\">${button('Ready to play','hub-ready','primary')}</div>` : ''}`);\n    } else if (state.screen === 'settings') {\n      html = modal('Make it yours','SETTINGS & CONTROLS', `<label class=\"field\">Music volume: <span id=\"music-value\">${Math.round(settings.music*100)}%</span><input id=\"music\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"100\" value=\"${Math.round(settings.music*100)}\"></label><label class=\"field\">Sound effects <select id=\"sound\"><option value=\"on\" ${settings.sound?'selected':''}>On</option><option value=\"off\" ${!settings.sound?'selected':''}>Off</option></select></label><label class=\"field\">Controller labels <select id=\"glyph\"><option ${settings.glyph==='PlayStation'?'selected':''}>PlayStation</option><option ${settings.glyph==='Xbox'?'selected':''}>Xbox</option></select></label><p>Keyboard: WASD or arrow keys to lean; Space / Enter to act; Esc to pause. Controller: left stick and ${settings.glyph==='Xbox'?'A':'Cross'}. Mouse: move to lean and click to act. Arrow keys navigate menus.</p><p>Touch-only devices can view the island; connect a controller or keyboard to play.</p><div class=\"row\">${button('Done','settings-back','primary')}</div>`, 'settings-back');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'about') {\n      const info = window.__aboutData || {};\n      const blocks = [['Source Information',info.sourceInformation],['Testing Feedback',info.testingFeedback],['Engine Feedback',info.engineFeedback],['Prompt Feedback',info.promptFeedback]];\n      html = modal('About this game','THE FINE PRINT', `<p>Made with Shardfall and an original island full of questionable advice.</p>${blocks.map(([label,value])=>`<h3>${esc(label)}</h3><div class=\"about-list\">${Array.isArray(value)?value.map(line=>`<p>${esc(line)}</p>`).join(''):Object.entries(value||{}).map(([key,line])=>`<p><strong>${esc(key)}:</strong> ${esc(line)}</p>`).join('')}</div>`).join('')}<div class=\"row\">${button('Back to the island','title','primary')}</div>`);\n    }\n    if (state.attract && state.screen==='title') html += `<div class=\"attract-label\">A LITTLE ISLAND DAYDREAM · PRESS ANY KEY TO RETURN</div>`;\n    if (isTouchOnly() && !state.hasHardwareInput && !['settings','about'].includes(state.screen)) html += `<div class=\"touch-guard\"><div><strong>Controller or keyboard required</strong><p>Connect one to play. The island will wait for you.</p><button class=\"button\" data-action=\"settings\">Settings</button></div></div>`;\n    app.innerHTML = html;\n    const musicInput=document.getElementById('music');\n    if (musicInput) musicInput.addEventListener('input', event=>{ settings.music=Number(event.target.value)/100; document.getElementById('music-value').textContent=Math.round(settings.music*100)+'%'; save(); });\n    const soundInput=document.getElementById('sound');\n    if (soundInput) soundInput.addEventListener('change', event=>{ settings.sound=event.target.value==='on'; save(); });\n    const glyphInput=document.getElementById('glyph');\n    if (glyphInput) glyphInput.addEventListener('change', event=>{ settings.glyph=event.target.value; save(); render(); });\n    const nameInput=document.getElementById('guest-name');\n    if (nameInput) nameInput.addEventListener('change', event=>{ state.setup.name=event.target.value; });\n    for (const kind of ['stiffness','damping']) { const input=document.getElementById('dev-'+kind); if(input) input.addEventListener('input', event=>{state[kind]=Number(event.target.value);}); }\n  }\n\n  function isTouchOnly() { return matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches; }\n  function newProfile() { return {name:state.setup.name,skin:state.setup.skin,outfit:state.setup.outfit,day:1,dayMinutes:0,minutesTotal:0,stars:0,age:null,checked:false,finaleDone:false,freePlay:false,bests:{},lastDate:new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10)}; }\n  function setScreen(screen) { state.screen=screen; render(); }\n  function selectAction(action) {\n    if (!action) return;\n    sound(520,.05);\n    if (action === 'title') { state.paused=false; state.together=null; state.round=null; setScreen('title'); }\n    else if (action === 'slots-new' || action === 'slots-continue') { state.slotMode=action==='slots-new'?'new':'continue'; setScreen('slots'); }\n    else if (action.startsWith('slot:')) { const index=Number(action.slice(5)), guest=(saved.slots||[])[index]; state.slot=index; if (guest) { state.profile=guest; setScreen('island'); } else { state.setup={name:names[index],skin:index%skins.length,outfit:index%outfits.length}; setScreen('customize'); } }\n    else if (action.startsWith('skin:')) { state.setup.skin=Number(action.slice(5)); render(); }\n    else if (action.startsWith('outfit:')) { state.setup.outfit=Number(action.slice(7)); render(); }\n    else if (action==='create-guest') { state.profile=newProfile(); save(); voice(); setScreen('intro'); }\n    else if (action==='island') { if (state.profile) {state.paused=false;setScreen('island');} else setScreen('title'); }\n    else if (action==='calendar') setScreen('calendar');\n    else if (action==='check') { voice(); setScreen('checkIntro'); }\n    else if (action==='begin-check') startCheck();\n    else if (action.startsWith('intro:')) { state.eventId=action.slice(6); voice(); setScreen('eventIntro'); }\n    else if (action==='cancel-event') setScreen(state.together?'handoff':'island');\n    else if (action==='begin-event') startRound(state.eventId);\n    else if (action==='pause') { state.paused=true; render(); }\n    else if (action==='resume') { state.paused=false; render(); }\n    else if (action==='reset-tuning') { state.stiffness=40; state.damping=8.5; render(); }\n    else if (action==='leave-event') { state.paused=false; if (state.together && state.together.online) reportHub(); else setScreen(state.together?'handoff':'island'); }\n    else if (action==='result-next') advanceResult();\n    else if (action==='end-day') setScreen('endDay');\n    else if (action==='sleep') { if (state.profile.day===5) setScreen('ending'); else { state.profile.day++; state.profile.dayMinutes=0; state.profile.checked=false; state.profile.lastDate=new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10); save(); setScreen('island'); } }\n    else if (action==='free-play') { state.profile.freePlay=true; save(); setScreen('island'); }\n    else if (action==='together') { state.together=null; setScreen('together'); }\n    else if (action.startsWith('hotseat:')) { state.together={count:Number(action.slice(8)),player:0,event:0,scores:[0,0,0,0],online:false,ghosts:{}}; setScreen('handoff'); }\n    else if (action==='hotseat-next') { state.eventId=medley[state.together.event]; setScreen('eventIntro'); }\n    else if (action==='settings') { state.returnScreen=state.screen; setScreen('settings'); }\n    else if (action==='settings-back') setScreen(state.returnScreen || 'title');\n    else if (action==='about') setScreen('about');\n    else if (action==='hub-ready') { if(hub) hub.ready(); state.message='Ready! Waiting for the other guests.'; render(); }\n  }\n * ?auto=1 — the conformance run. It presses keys inside each frame with\n * synthetic events while the round plays (the frames must be served from this\n * page's origin). Results land in window.__hubCheck, and body[data-complete]\n * turns \"true\".\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\nasync function until(test, ms) {\n  const end = performance.now() + ms;\n  while (performance.now() < end) {\n    if (test()) return true;\n    await sleep(50);\n  }\n  return test();\n}\n\nfunction poke(cell, key) {\n  const doc = cell.frame.contentDocument;\n  const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\n  if (!doc || !win) return false;\n  const target = doc.activeElement && doc.activeElement !== doc.documentElement ? doc.activeElement : doc.body || doc.documentElement;\n  const init = { key, code: key === ' ' ? 'Space' : key, bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: win };\n  target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keydown', init));\n  setTimeout(() => target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keyup', init)), 120);\n  return true;\n}\n\nasync function conformance() {\n  const checks = [];\n  const check = (name, pass, detail = '') => {\n    checks.push({ name, pass: !!pass, detail });\n    renderChecks(checks);\n    return !!pass;\n  };\n  const report = { done: false, pass: false, game: $('game').value, players: Number($('players').value), scenario, checks, log: logLines };\n  window.__hubCheck = report;\n  try {\n    const state = await newRound();\n    if (!state) {\n      check('game named', false, 'pass ?game=<path> of a page on this site');\n      return;\n    }\n    const n = state.n;\n    const m = state.metas;\n    check('head metas', m && m.session === '1' && modeOf(m.mode), m ? `hub:session=${m.session} mode=${m.mode}` : 'could not fetch the page');\n    const seats = String(m?.players ?? '').match(/\\d+/g)?.map(Number) ?? [];\n    const [least, most = least] = seats;\n    check('hub:session-players is a range within 1–4', seats.length >= 1 && seats.length <= 2 && least >= 1 && least <= most && most <= 4, `hub:session-players=${m?.players}`);\n    if (m?.minutes != null) check('hub:session-minutes, when given, is a number', Number(m.minutes) > 0, `hub:session-minutes=${m.minutes}`);\n\n    // Every copy: the players, and in a server round the server's copy.\n    const copies = () => [...(state.status?.players ?? []), ...(state.status?.server ? [state.status.server] : [])];\n    const helloed = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.hello), TIMINGS.helloMs + 1000);\n    check('every copy says hello', helloed, copies().filter((p) => !p.hello).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\n    if (!helloed) return;\n    const caps = state.coordinator.seats().map((s) => s.caps);\n    check('hello names protocol 1 and the mode', caps.every((c) => c.v === 1 && modeOf(c.mode) === state.coordinator.mode), JSON.stringify(caps[0]));\n    check('hello seats cover this player count', caps.every((c) => Array.isArray(c.seats) && c.seats[0] <= Math.max(2, n) && c.seats[1] >= n), JSON.stringify(caps[0]?.seats));\n    if (state.cells.some((c) => !c.frame.contentDocument)) {\n      check('frames reachable for synthetic input', false, 'serve the game from the same origin as this harness');\n      return;\n    }\n\n    // The card collects ready: every game readies up by itself once loaded, with no prompt and no key.\n    const loaded = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.ready), 20_000);\n    check('ready without a key press (the card asks the players)', loaded, copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\n    // A game that shows its own card takes the players' answers on it: Enter is Ready.\n    if (caps.some((c) => c?.card)) {\n      const players = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.server);\n      const sent = await until(() => players.every((c) => c.cardSent), 2000);\n      for (const cell of players) poke(cell, 'Enter');\n      const answered = await until(() => players.every((c) => state.answers.ready.has(c.key)), 3000);\n      check('its own card: Enter answers Ready', sent && answered, players.filter((c) => !state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => `${c.key}${c.cardSent ? '' : ' (no card yet)'}`).join(', '));\n    }\n    releaseRound(state);\n    const started = await until(() => state.status?.phase !== 'loading', 15_000);\n    check('the round starts when the card ends', started && copies().every((p) => p.ready), copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', ') || state.status?.phase);\n    if (!started || state.record) return;\n\n    await until(() => state.status.phase === 'playing' || state.record, TIMINGS.countdownMs + 2000);\n    const arrows = ['ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'ArrowUp', 'ArrowDown', 'a', 'd', 'w', 's'];\n    const randomly = async (ms) => {\n      const end = performance.now() + ms;\n      while (performance.now() < end && !state.record) {\n        for (const cell of state.cells) if (!cell.gone && !cell.server) poke(cell, arrows[Math.floor(Math.random() * arrows.length)]);\n        await sleep(150);\n      }\n    };\n    await randomly(Math.min(1500, playMs / 4));\n\n    const mode = state.coordinator.mode;\n    // Parallel and ghost: every copy runs its own world from the same seeded start. A game\n    // still tagged race was built to race's contract: no seeded start, and no progress asked.\n    const own = SELF_REPORTED.includes(mode);\n    const legacyRace = own && !seedsRandom(m?.mode);\n    if (own && !legacyRace) {\n      const seeded = state.cells.every((c) => c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.seeded === true);\n      check(`${mode}: Math.random is seeded, the same on every copy`, seeded, state.cells.map((c) => `${c.key}: client ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.version ?? '?'} seeded ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.seeded}`).join('; '));\n    }\n\n    if (scenario === 'host-leave') removeCell(state.cells[0]);\n    else if (n >= 3) removeCell(state.cells[n - 1]);\n    await randomly(playMs / 2);\n    const remaining = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.gone);\n    if (own) {\n      if (mode === 'parallel') {\n        check('parallel: no game traffic', state.cells.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent === 0),\n          state.cells.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent}`).join(' '));\n      } else {\n        check('ghost: every copy sends its player', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0) || n === 1,\n          remaining.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent}`).join(' '));\n      }\n      if (!legacyRace) check(`${mode}: every copy reports its progress`, remaining.every((c) => c.progress.length > 0 || state.status?.players.find((p) => p.key === c.key)?.result),\n        remaining.map((c) => `${c.key}: ${c.progress.length} report${c.progress.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}`).join(', '));\n    } else {\n      check('game traffic flows both ways', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0 && c.bridge.stats.received > 0) || n === 1,\n        remaining.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent} ↓${c.bridge.stats.received}`).join(' '));\n    }\n\n    if (!state.record) state.coordinator.timeUp();\n    const ended = await until(() => state.record, TIMINGS.graceMs + 2000);\n    const record = state.record;\n    if (serverMode) {\n      // The world ran on the server: the players heard it, and only the host may finish a shared world.\n      const serverCell = state.cells.find((c) => c.server);\n      check('a copy with no player of its own runs the world (as a server would)', ended && record.status === 'played' && record.hostId === serverCell.bridge.me && serverCell.bridge.stats.sent > 0,\n        record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason}), host ${record.hostId}, server sent ${serverCell.bridge.stats.sent}` : 'no end');\n    }\n    if (scenario === 'host-leave' && !SELF_REPORTED.includes(state.coordinator.mode)) {\n      check('host leaving voids the round', ended && record.status === 'void' && record.endReason === 'host-left', record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason})` : 'no end');\n    } else {\n      check('the round ends with a valid result', ended && record.status === 'played', record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason})` : 'no end within the grace period');\n    }\n    await sleep(300);\n    check('every remaining copy is told the round ended', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.ended), remaining.filter((c) => !c.bridge.ended).map((c) => c.key).join(', '));\n    const issues = [...(state.status?.issues ?? []), ...state.cells.flatMap((c) => c.bridge.issues)];\n    check('no protocol problems', issues.length === 0, issues.map((i) => `${i.key}: ${i.problem}`).join('; '));\n    const violations = state.cells.flatMap((c) => {\n      let extra = [];\n      try {\n        extra = c.frame.contentWindow?.__hubViolations ?? [];\n      } catch {}\n      return [...c.violations, ...extra].map((v) => `${c.key}: ${v}`);\n    });\n    check('no errors, dialogs, popups or sockets', violations.length === 0, violations.slice(0, 6).join('; '));\n  } catch (error) {\n    check('harness ran', false, String(error?.stack || error));\n  } finally {\n    report.pass = checks.length > 0 && checks.every((c) => c.pass);\n    report.done = true;\n    document.body.dataset.complete = 'true';\n    log(`conformance: ${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}`);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction renderChecks(checks) {\n  $('checklist').replaceChildren(\n    ...checks.map((c) => {\n      const li = document.createElement('li');\n      li.className = c.pass ? 'ok' : 'bad';\n      li.textContent = c.name + (c.detail && !c.pass ? ` — ${c.detail}` : '');\n      li.title = c.detail;\n      return li;\n    }),\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
