{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_202","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"dev='Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701'; rg -n 'touch-guard|matchMedia|touchOnly|coarse|Controller or keyboard' \\\"\"'$dev/web/game.js\"; sed -n '\"'1,170p' \\\"\"'$dev/tests/test_game.py\"; ls -l \"$dev/tests/artifacts\"; rg -n -i -C 2 '\"'touch.?only|touch screen|controller or keyboard' PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_202","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"dev='Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701'; rg -n 'touch-guard|matchMedia|touchOnly|coarse|Controller or keyboard' \\\"\"'$dev/web/game.js\"; sed -n '\"'1,170p' \\\"\"'$dev/tests/test_game.py\"; ls -l \"$dev/tests/artifacts\"; rg -n -i -C 2 '\"'touch.?only|touch screen|controller or keyboard' PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"113:    if (isTouchOnly() && !state.hasHardwareInput && !['settings','about'].includes(state.screen)) html += `<div class=\"touch-guard\"><div><strong>Controller or keyboard required</strong><p>Connect one to play. The island will wait for you.</p><button class=\"button\" data-action=\"settings\">Settings</button></div></div>`;\n126:  function isTouchOnly() { return matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches; }\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport threading\nimport traceback\nfrom functools import partial\nfrom http.server import SimpleHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom urllib.parse import urlencode\n\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\n\nDEV = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nROOT = DEV.parent\nHTML = ROOT / f\"{DEV.name}.html\"\nARTIFACTS = DEV / \"tests\" / \"artifacts\"\nfailures = []\nchecks = 0\n\n\ndef test(name, function):\n    global checks\n    checks += 1\n    try:\n        function()\n    except Exception:\n        failures.append(f\"{name}:\\n{traceback.format_exc()}\")\n\n\ndef status(page):\n    return json.loads(page.evaluate(\"window.__gameStatus()\"))\n\n\ndef click(page, action):\n    page.locator(f'[data-action=\"{action}\"]').first.click(timeout=5000)\n\n\ndef advance(page):\n    page.evaluate(\"window.__testAdvance(200)\")\n    assert status(page)[\"scene\"] == \"result\", status(page)\n\n\ndef load(browser, **kwargs):\n    context = browser.new_context(**kwargs)\n    page = context.new_page()\n    errors = []\n    page.on(\"pageerror\", lambda error: errors.append(str(error)))\n    page.goto(HTML.as_uri() + \"?test=1\", wait_until=\"domcontentloaded\")\n    page.wait_for_function(\"window.__gameBoot?.ready === true\")\n    return context, page, errors\n\n\ndef new_guest(page):\n    click(page, \"slots-new\")\n    click(page, \"slot:0\")\n    page.locator(\"#guest-name\").select_option(label=\"Ari\")\n    click(page, \"skin:2\")\n    click(page, \"outfit:3\")\n    click(page, \"create-guest\")\n    click(page, \"island\")\n    assert status(page)[\"guest\"] == \"Ari\"\n\n\ndef browser_tests(playwright):\n    for engine in (\"chromium\", \"firefox\", \"webkit\"):\n        browser = getattr(playwright, engine).launch(headless=True)\n\n        def smoke():\n            context, page, errors = load(browser, viewport={\"width\": 1280, \"height\": 800})\n            assert \"Wii Fit\" in page.title()\n            click(page, \"about\")\n            assert \"Source Information\" in page.locator(\"#app\").inner_text()\n            click(page, \"title\")\n            new_guest(page)\n            click(page, \"check\")\n            click(page, \"begin-check\")\n            page.keyboard.press(\"Escape\")\n            assert status(page)[\"paused\"]\n            page.keyboard.press(\"Escape\")\n            advance(page)\n            click(page, \"result-next\")\n            assert status(page)[\"checked\"]\n            click(page, \"intro:breath\")\n            click(page, \"begin-event\")\n            page.keyboard.press(\"Space\")\n            advance(page)\n            click(page, \"result-next\")\n            assert status(page)[\"minutes\"] == 2\n            page.screenshot(path=str(ARTIFACTS / f\"{engine}-island.png\"))\n            assert not errors, errors\n            context.close()\n\n        test(f\"{engine} guest, check and activity\", smoke)\n        browser.close()\n\n    browser = playwright.chromium.launch(headless=True)\n\n    def stay():\n        context, page, errors = load(browser, viewport={\"width\": 1280, \"height\": 800})\n        new_guest(page)\n        for day, repetitions in enumerate((2, 3, 4, 5, 1), 1):\n            assert status(page)[\"day\"] == day\n            click(page, \"check\")\n            click(page, \"begin-check\")\n            advance(page)\n            click(page, \"result-next\")\n            for _ in range(repetitions):\n                click(page, \"intro:finale\" if day == 5 else \"intro:breath\")\n                click(page, \"begin-event\")\n                advance(page)\n                click(page, \"result-next\")\n            click(page, \"end-day\")\n            click(page, \"sleep\")\n        assert status(page)[\"scene\"] == \"ending\"\n        click(page, \"free-play\")\n        assert status(page)[\"scene\"] == \"island\"\n        page.reload(wait_until=\"domcontentloaded\")\n        page.wait_for_function(\"window.__gameBoot?.ready === true\")\n        click(page, \"slots-continue\")\n        click(page, \"slot:0\")\n        assert status(page)[\"guest\"] == \"Ari\" and status(page)[\"day\"] == 5\n        assert not errors, errors\n        context.close()\n\n    test(\"five-day stay, ending and save persistence\", stay)\n\n    def medley():\n        context, page, errors = load(browser)\n        click(page, \"together\")\n        click(page, \"hotseat:2\")\n        for player in range(2):\n            for event in range(3):\n                current = status(page)[\"together\"]\n                assert current[\"player\"] == player and current[\"event\"] == event, current\n                click(page, \"hotseat-next\")\n                click(page, \"begin-event\")\n                advance(page)\n                click(page, \"result-next\")\n        assert status(page)[\"scene\"] == \"podium\"\n        assert not errors, errors\n        context.close()\n\n    test(\"two-player local medley\", medley)\n    browser.close()\n\n    browser = playwright.webkit.launch(headless=True)\n\n    def touch_guard():\n        context, page, errors = load(browser, **playwright.devices[\"iPhone SE (3rd gen)\"])\n        assert \"Controller or keyboard required\" in page.locator(\"#app\").inner_text()\n        page.screenshot(path=str(ARTIFACTS / \"iphone-touch.png\"))\n        click(page, \"settings\")\n        assert status(page)[\"scene\"] == \"settings\"\n        assert not errors, errors\n        context.close()\n\n    test(\"touch-only guard and settings\", touch_guard)\n    browser.close()\n\n\nclass QuietHandler(SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):\n    def log_message(self, *_args):\n        pass\n\n\ndef hub_tests(playwright):\n    server = ThreadingHTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", 0), partial(QuietHandler, directory=str(ROOT)))\n    thread = threading.Thread(target=server.serve_forever, daemon=True)\n    thread.start()\ntotal 544\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 149545 Nov  4 23:17 chromium-island.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 157839 Nov  4 23:17 firefox-island.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 114564 Nov  4 23:17 iphone-touch.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 130589 Nov  4 23:17 webkit-island.png\n315-- **Rhythm clock:** the mixer counts rendered samples in an atomic. `pav_app` reads it, runs a small phase-locked clock (`clock += dt; clock += (audio_pos - clock) * 0.05`), subtracts a latency offset (default 0.10 s, Settings: Rhythm Offset), and sends it as `InputFrame.song_pos`. The sim uses `song_pos` when present, its own tick time otherwise. Replays and tests stay deterministic, because the value is part of the recorded input.\n316-- **Latency:** cpal's web backend defaults to 2048 frames per buffer, about 43 ms (read in its source, not measured on a real device). Try `BufferSize::Fixed(1024)` in `AudioOut::start` for snappier effects.\n317:- **Autoplay:** `resume_audio` runs on key, mouse and touch only. Also call it on the first gamepad activity. Attract mode is silent until a real input arrives; that is expected.\n318-\n319-| Song | Where | Feel (all original) |\n--\n359-**Mouse in the world:** on the island `InputFrame.aim` already holds the cursor's ground point. The nearest interactable within 1.2 m of it gets a highlight ring; clicking walks there with `NavGrid::path`, then interacts. Clicking open ground walks there.\n360-\n361:**Touch-only devices:** detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')`, no `(any-pointer: fine)`, and no gamepad or key seen yet. Show a centred card \"Controller or keyboard required\" and a Settings button (tap works; Settings is usable by tap). No touch controls: skip Shardfall's `touch.draw` for this game, and route touches directly to egui in `on_touch`, because the engine's touch layer otherwise treats a finger as a stick. Attract mode runs behind the card. Remove the phone-rotation hint and fullscreen-on-tap from `web/index.html`. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, drop the card and start normally. A touch device without WebGPU cannot run the game at all, so the page's own fallback message there says both things: \"Controller or keyboard required\" and that the game needs WebGPU.\n362-\n363-**Dev Mode** (from Pause, not shown in hub sessions). Big rows, pad-navigable, in tabs:\n--\n371-## 12. Attract mode\n372-\n373:After 10 seconds without input on the title or pre-game menus (600 ticks), loop: island sweep 8 s, then about 15 s each of Cannonball Cup, Paddle Slalom, Step Party, Pose Parade, Tide Table, Floatie Spin, Tray Trek, Plank Standoff, Morning Lap, Big Stand, then the title card 5 s. The bot plays with `demo = true`: no tips, no failures, nothing saved. A \"DEMO\" ribbon and \"Press any button\" show on screen. Any input exits to the title: any key, button, stick beyond 0.3, mouse click or mouse move over 6 px (`InputFrame.any`). Touch-only devices keep it running.\n374-\n375-Use the same event code with the bot replacing input in `pre`. No separate replay system.\n--\n572-- Content lint: no `TODO` or placeholder text in `script.toml`, and every event has a card, rules and a bot.\n573-\n574:**`browser` (Playwright, one browser, 320x180, `file://`):** boots with no errors; `__gameStatus` appears; the pad stub moves focus and confirms; keyboard does the same; mouse hover moves focus and click activates, using rects the UI publishes in `window.__gameUi`; prompts switch with the device; Settings has the Xbox option; attract starts after 10 s and any input exits it; music reaches about 10% by the sound patch. Touch: Chromium with a phone and a tablet profile (it has WebGPU) must show \"Controller or keyboard required\", run attract, and respond to a Settings tap by `page.touchscreen.tap`. WebKit with an iPhone profile, which has no WebGPU here, must show the fallback message from section 11.\n575-\n576-**`hub`:** copy the page and `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` into one served folder, open `harness.html?game=<page>&players=N&auto=1`, wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === \"true\"`, and require `window.__hubCheck.pass`. Run 2 players; 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; and `scenario=host-leave`. Then a solo check like the hub's: open outside a session, press Enter and Space, expect no errors, `AIHub.active` false, and `Math.random` not seeded. Also byte-compare the pasted client with `hub/session.js`.\n--\n591-6. **Meta.** Days, unlocks, titles, wardrobe, flip-flops, Yesterday You, absence comments, all songs and SFX.\n592-7. **Finale and endings.** Big Stand, both endings, credits, Free Play.\n593:8. **Shell.** Attract, Settings, Dev Mode, touch-only card, How to Play, About.\n594-9. **Multiplayer.** Full Medley, hub ghosts in every lane, Play Together.\n595-10. **Polish.** Write the script to full length, feel pass on every event using the sliders, extra set dressing, particles, transitions, stingers.\n--\n628-| Narrative tone | 7 |\n629-| 10-foot, controller-first, native keyboard and mouse, glyphs, Xbox option, no dense screens | 3, 11 |\n630:| Touch-only behaviour | 11, 12 |\n631-| No TODOs or stubs | 16, 17 |\n632-| Source Information and all feedback in chat and on About, exit interview | 11, 14, 18 |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
