{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_494","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"dev='Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701'; rg -n '\"'^(  )?(function|const) (events|medley|goals|eventById|startRound|finishRound|tickRound|drawWorld|draw|music|sound|voice|render)'\"' \\\"\"'$dev/web/game.js\"; rg -n '\"'fit|cargo|build-web|wasm' \\\"\"'$dev/engine/scripts/build-web.sh\" | head -n 35; sed -n '\"'600,610p' PLAN.md; ls -l \\\"\"'$dev/tests/artifacts\" | tail -n 20'","aggregated_output":"12:  const events = [\n26:  const medley = ['paddle','tide','dive'];\n27:  const goals = [3,5,7,9,0];\n42:  function sound(frequency=440, length=.08, type='sine', volume=.06) {\n46:  function voice() { [490,610,520].forEach((tone,index) => setTimeout(() => sound(tone,.07,'sine',.025),index*75)); }\n47:  function music(dt) { if (!audio || !settings.music || document.hidden) return; musicClock -= dt; if (musicClock <= 0) { musicClock=.48; const notes=[261.63,329.63,392,329.63,293.66,349.23,440,349.23]; const index=Math.floor(performance.now()/480)%notes.length; try { const oscillator=audio.createOscillator(), gain=audio.createGain(); oscillator.type='sine'; oscillator.frequency.value=notes[index]; gain.gain.setValueAtTime(settings.music*.07,audio.currentTime); gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(.001,audio.currentTime+.32); oscillator.connect(gain).connect(audio.destination); oscillator.start(); oscillator.stop(audio.currentTime+.32); } catch (_) {} } }\n54:  function eventById(id) { return events.find(item => item.id === id); }\n58:  function render() {\n165:  function startRound(id) { const item=eventById(id); if(!item) return; center={x:0,y:0,vx:0,vy:0}; aim={x:0,y:0}; lastHubUpdate=0; lastHubProgress=0; state.paused=false; state.round={...item,instruction:item.controls,elapsed:0,sum:0,samples:0,actionHits:0,actionCount:0,steps:0,lastStep:'',shellX:0,shellY:0,shellVx:0,shellVy:0,potted:0,spin:0,prevAngle:0,gates:0,gateIndex:-1,stillBroken:false,ghostTrail:[]}; setScreen('event'); if(state.together?.online && hub) hub.progress({score:state.together.scores[0],label:`${item.name}: starting`}); }\n187:  function finishRound() {\n231:  function tickRound(dt) {\n285:  function drawWorld(now) {\n2:# Builds the browser version (WebAssembly + WebGPU). Output: target/web/{index.html,manifest.webmanifest,shardfall.js,shardfall_bg.wasm}\n4:# --single-file writes only target/web/<title>.html (shardfall.html): one page with the glue and gzipped wasm inside\n7:# Needs: rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown\n8:#        cargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version <the wasm-bindgen version in Cargo.lock>\n18:\t\t(($# > 1)) || { echo \"build-web.sh: $1 needs a value\" >&2; exit 2; }\n24:\t*) echo \"build-web.sh: unknown option $1 (options are listed at the top of $0)\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n29:\techo \"build-web.sh: ${pack[0]} needs --single-file\" >&2\n32:cargo build --locked --profile dist --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p pav_app\n33:wasm=${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/wasm32-unknown-unknown/dist/shardfall.wasm\n38:\twasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \"$bindgen\" --out-name shardfall \"$wasm\"\n44:wasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \"$out\" --out-name shardfall \"$wasm\"\n## 18. Finishing\n\n1. Write the exit interview your brief names. Fill every field honestly; `usage` is exactly \"added on import\". Suggested `aiHub` values: type `Game`, genre `Sports`, source `Wii Fit`, series `Wii Fit`, players `1–4`, tags from `3d`, `third-person`, `comedy`, `sports`, `versus`, `low-poly`. Check that it parses.\n2. Run `tools/build.sh`: copy the exit interview into `about-data` in the page, run the single-file build with your title, description and theme colour, and write the HTML where your brief says. The About screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback from that block, including the fonts' and motion libraries' credits (`engine/store/CREDITS.md`, each clip set's `credit`).\n3. Run `tests/run.sh all` on the final page. Open it once from `file://` at 1920x1080 and look at one frame.\n4. Put the same Source Information and feedback in your chat reply.\n5. Delete `engine/target` and other caches. Leave the source, tests and notes in the dev folder.\n\n### What each brief item maps to\n\n| Brief item | Section |\ntotal 960\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 148436 Nov  5 00:24 chromium-island.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 156074 Nov  5 00:24 firefox-island.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 115922 Nov  5 00:24 iphone-check.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 155963 Nov  5 00:24 iphone-pause.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 116046 Nov  5 00:24 iphone-touch.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 141099 Nov  5 00:24 pause-tuning.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 128825 Nov  5 00:24 webkit-island.png\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
