{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_497","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/README.md\n+# Wii Fit Together\n+\n+This is a playable prototype of the Tippy Cay stay and its local and AI Hub medleys. The visible island, activities, interface, audio, save data and multiplayer coordination are implemented in \"'`web/game.js` and `web/game.css`. Shardfall also contains a registered `fit` scene and balance spring, but it does not drive the visible game. The planned freely explorable native 3D island, full event-specific mechanics, expanded narrative and other features in `PLAN.md` remain incomplete.\n+\n+## Run and build\n+\n+Open the HTML file in the parent directory directly in a browser. A controller or keyboard is required; touch-only screens show the controller notice. Local progress is stored in browser local storage.\n+\n+From the parent directory, run `bash '\"'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/scripts/build.sh'\"'` to rebuild the engine'\"'s single-file web output and bundle the game. This requires Rust, the \"'`wasm32-unknown-unknown` target and the `wasm-bindgen` CLI version matching `engine/Cargo.lock`. The build cache is intentionally removed from the hand-in, so the first rebuild recompiles the engine. For changes confined to `web/` or `exit-interview.json`, run `python3 '\"'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/scripts/bundle.py'\"'` against the included `game.raw.html` instead.\n+\n+Run `bash '\"'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/tests/run.sh' all\"'` for the scripted browser and AI Hub checks. The tests use Playwright'\"'s installed browser binaries and an ephemeral loopback server for the Hub harness.\n+\n+## Extending the prototype\n+\n+- **Event:** Add an entry to \"'`events` in `web/game.js`, then implement its behavior in `tickRound`, scoring in `finishRound`, and any specialized presentation in `render` or `drawWorld`. Update the medley, unlocks and tests where applicable. Existing events share simplified mechanics rather than the full designs in the plan.\n+- **Set:** The current island is drawn procedurally by `drawWorld`; there is no data-driven set system. A new scene requires extending that drawing code and the screen flow, or implementing a native Shardfall scene if pursuing the planned 3D architecture.\n+- **Song:** `music` in `web/game.js` synthesizes a small looping note sequence with Web Audio. Change the notes and timing there, or introduce a separate sequencer and song selection before adding distinct tracks. `sound` and `voice` synthesize effects and chimes.\n+\n+In a separate headless Chromium/SwiftShader probe, Shardfall reached its first frame but its WebGPU device was then lost. The visible Canvas 2D game continued running; hardware WebGPU and real iOS Safari were not verified.\n*** Update File: exit-interview.json\n@@\n-    \"animation\": \"Procedural Canvas 2D motion and Shardfall'\"'s native simulation\\\",\n-    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Procedurally synthesized music, sound effects and gibberish voices; music defaults to 10%\\\",\n+    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Procedural Canvas 2D motion; the Shardfall scene and balance hook do not drive the visible game\\\",\n+    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Procedurally synthesized music, sound effects and chime-like voices; music defaults to 10%\\\",\n@@\n-    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless Chromium, Firefox and WebKit, scripted interaction and viewport screenshots\\\",\n+    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"13 scripted browser and AI Hub checks, 24 viewport launches and two Rust tests; headless WebGPU software-adapter probe failed; no physical devices or real iOS Safari\\\",\n@@\n-    \\\"unknown\\\",\n-    \\\"unknown\\\",\n-    \\\"unknown\\\",\n-    \\\"unknown\\\"\n+    \\\"At least five issues: startup injection, missing online progress, unclear labels, overlapping phone HUD and WebGPU device loss.\\\",\n+    \\\"One critical startup bug was fixed; the WebGPU loss also prevents the engine renderer in the tested software configuration.\\\",\n+    \\\"The cross-browser viewport sweep with visual inspection, together with the scripted full stay.\\\",\n+    \\\"The isolated balance-spring unit tests were least useful for end-to-end coverage, although they passed.\\\"\n@@\n-    \\\"The web presentation and input integration needed more work than expected.\\\",\n-    \\\"The island interface, activity rules, persistence and multiplayer flow.\\\",\n-    \\\"Connecting a full custom game and browser interface to the existing simulation.\\\",\n-    \\\"Registered a fit game, island scene and balance spring to establish a native engine hook.\\\",\n+    \\\"The WebGPU software-adapter run lost its device after the first frame; retaining the instance did not fix it.\\\",\n+    \\\"The visible Canvas 2D island interface, activity rules, persistence and multiplayer flow.\\\",\n+    \\\"Integrating a complete browser game into the native simulation; the planned 3D game remains unfinished.\\\",\n+    \\\"Registered a fit game, island scene and balance spring to establish a native engine hook, but the visible game does not use it.\\\",\n@@\n-    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Escape to Tippy Cay for a lighthearted island stay full of balance challenges. Play a local medley with friends or compare ghost performances through AI Hub.\\\",\n+    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A playable Tippy Cay prototype with simplified balance challenges. Play a local medley with friends or compare ghost performances through AI Hub.\\\",\n*** Update File: PROGRESS.md\n@@\n-- The browser suite passed ten checks, including three engines, the five-day stay, save persistence, the local medley, and 2–4-player AI Hub runs. Two Rust balance-spring tests passed.\n-- First-clear and repeat minute rewards now follow the plan. Rebuild the HTML, re-run the changed browser suite, and complete the exit interview.\n-- Limitation: the playable presentation and most activity logic are Canvas 2D / JavaScript over a Shardfall hook, not the planned full native 3D engine implementation.\n+- The browser suite passed 13 checks, including three engines, the five-day stay, rewards, save persistence, pause controls, the local medley, and 2–4-player AI Hub runs. Two Rust balance-spring tests passed.\n+- First-clear and repeat minute rewards follow the plan. The exit interview and development README document the current result.\n+- Limitations: the visible game and activity logic are Canvas 2D / JavaScript, not the planned full native 3D engine implementation. The explorable island and full event-specific mechanics, among other planned features, remain incomplete.\n+- In a separate headless Chromium/SwiftShader probe, Shardfall reached its first frame but then lost its WebGPU device. Retaining the engine instance did not fix this. Hardware WebGPU and real iOS Safari have not been verified.\n+- Next: re-bundle the completed interview, rerun the final browser suite, inspect a 1920×1080 frame, and remove engine build caches.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\npython3 -m json.tool exit-interview.json >/dev/null\npython3 'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/scripts/bundle.py'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
