{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_578","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"wc -l PLAN.md TASK.md 'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/web/game.js'; rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} |''^[0-9]+'\"\\\\. |must|Must|MUST|engine|Engine' PLAN.md | head -240\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_578","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"wc -l PLAN.md TASK.md 'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/web/game.js'; rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} |''^[0-9]+'\"\\\\. |must|Must|MUST|engine|Engine' PLAN.md | head -240\"","aggregated_output":"   632 PLAN.md\n   151 TASK.md\n   325 Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/web/game.js\n  1108 total\n1:# Game plan: a balance-and-wellness comedy inspired by Wii Fit\n5:## 0. How to read this plan\n8:- **Paths** are relative to the dev folder your brief tells you to create. Clone the engine to `engine/` inside it.\n11:- **Verified** means it was run on this computer on 2026-11-04, against engine commit `49ef2ba` and AI Hub client 1.4.0. Section 15 lists those results.\n13:- **Reading cost:** you do not need to read the engine's source to start. Read `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` whole (about 3k tokens) and `engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/starter.rs`, then use this plan. Search `engine/docs/REFERENCE.md` and `engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md` when you need a tool or a prop field.\n15:## 1. The game in one page\n36:1. **Small movements, big consequences.** Mastery means doing less. The best moments are held breaths.\n37:2. **Deadpan encouragement.** Everything you do is commented on, kindly, and slightly too honestly.\n38:3. **A daily ritual.** Check in, get a number, do your exercises, get a stamp.\n39:4. **Calm surface, silly underneath.** The screen stays serene while a seagull stands on your head.\n48:## 2. Structure of play\n55:1. Wake on the cabana deck. Pip greets you, with an absence comment if real days have passed.\n56:2. Morning Wobble Check (about 70 seconds), Balance Age reveal, Pip's comment.\n57:3. Free time on the island: walk, talk to guests, find lost flip-flops, step on an event mat. The Schedule (Triangle or Tab) lists everything and fast-travels.\n58:4. When the day's minute goal is met, Pip says so. Sleep at your cabana (or choose End Day in the Schedule). A big stamp lands on the Calendar. Next day.\n72:**Bot rule:** `Game::bot` must be able to play this entire flow, menus included, from New Stay to the credits. That is your scripted playthrough and the base of attract mode.\n74:## 3. Controls\n92:Xbox glyphs (Settings option) swap A B X Y, LB RB LT RT, Menu. Ignore Options while Create is held: that pair belongs to the AI Hub. Disable the engine's own keys (F1 to F10, digits, H, Backspace rewind, right-drag tilt) outside dev mode. Keep F11 for fullscreen.\n94:## 4. The Balance Core\n115:**Body:** the figure tilts with the dot (`cob * 14` degrees about the feet, engine change in section 14). Beyond |cob| 0.75 an upper-body arm-flail clip fades in. A tip plays a stumble and, over water, a splash. Tips never end the game; they cost time or score.\n117:**HUD, the Puck:** a large circular gauge drawn in egui: a pale disc, a green target ring, a coral dot, and stars at the edge when streaking. It must read from 10 feet. It looks good at 340 px diameter at 1080p (verified). Put it top centre or bottom centre, whichever does not cover the figure in that event.\n119:## 5. Events\n125:### Stillness Studio (Posey). Set: `studio`, a round white deck on a calm dawn lagoon. Camera: mirror view (yaw 0, tilt 12, distance 8.5, fov 36; the figure faces +Z, toward the camera, and stick right is screen right).\n131:### Iron Gazebo (Big Kettle). Set: `gazebo`, a white iron gazebo at golden hour. Camera: 3/4 front.\n137:### Boardwalk (Bounce). Set: `boardwalk`, a beach boardwalk at bright midday.\n145:### Lagoon (Commodore Gull). Sets: `tide`, `channel`, `pier`, `tower`.\n153:**Cannonball Cup** (3 dives, about 40 s). The board bounces with a 1.2 s period. Press Action at the bottom of 3 bounces to build power, the 4th press leaps. In the air, hold Action to tuck and lean to rotate. Enter tucked and high for the biggest splash. Three gull judges hold up cards: \"6.5\", \"7\", \"See me\". \"We are not here for form. We are here for splash.\" Score: height x tuck x timing. Camera: side view (yaw 90, tilt 6, distance 14). The splash must be huge: a new `BigSplash` event scales the water dents and particles. This is the attract mode's hero shot. Bot: presses on bottoms, tucks at the apex.\n155:### The Big Stand (finale, about 2.5 minutes). Set: `bay`, a tiny post in the bay at sunset, with the whole cast watching from rafts.\n158:1. Breathing, 4 cycles.\n159:2. A pose under rising gusts, 20 s.\n160:3. Step Party for 16 bars with a marching band of guests, wobble on.\n161:4. Brace while waves crash, 20 s.\n162:5. **The Long Stillness:** 30 s of nothing. Music fades to silence, the HUD vanishes except the Puck. At 15 s a fake prompt offers \"Press Cross to skip\". Pressing anything forfeits the Inner Peace bonus. Then Pip, quietly: \"...Oh. You're still here. Good.\"\n166:### Morning Wobble Check. Set: `studio`. About 70 s, four micro-tests, Pip presiding.\n181:## 6. Meta systems\n186:- **Wardrobe:** reuse the engine's `GearLook`, which needs no new drawing (verified): `helm = cap` (sun cap), `helm = hood` (towel turban), `crown`, `halo`; `gloves` (sweatbands), `belt`, `pauldrons` (reads as arm floaties, funny). Plus shirt, pants and shoe colours. Skip `cape`: it draws long sticks.\n192:## 7. World, cast and writing\n227:## 8. Art direction\n229:**Base:** the engine's native look: cel-shaded rounded primitives, soft sun shadows, thin ink outlines on characters. Its big-headed toy figures already suit the tone. Take the look high-key and pastel.\n258:# The sea: water zones near the action, one huge disc beyond them. Fog hides its edge.\n270:**New props.** Hand-write format-2 JSON (`engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md`) into `engine/assets/props/lib/core/<name>.json`; that folder is embedded in every build, including the browser. Use them as `asset = \"LIB/core/<name>\"`. A rebuild of `pav` is needed before `room_check` can see a new file (verified). A leaning palm (cone trunk, 6 radial ellipsoid fronds) and a kettlebell (sphere and torus) looked good on the first try. Check each with `asset_preview name=x views=true figure=true`.\n283:## 9. Animation\n285:**Base:** the engine's puppet (procedural walk, idle, landing, squash and stretch) with motion clips on top.\n289:**Hand-keyed clips (verified feasible).** Write readable key poses into `engine/anim/fit.json`. Test without rebuilding: in `pav repl` run `anim_reload`, then `animsheet clip=FIT/Tree frames=1 size=300 out=out/tree.png`. The build embeds every `anim/*.json`. A tree pose, a warrior lunge and a squat were recognisable at the first attempt:\n302:Field meanings are in `LEGEND` at the top of `engine/crates/pav_core/src/clips.rs`: `hips [forward, right, up]` in percent of standing hip height; `body`, `chest` and `head [turn, lean, tilt]` in degrees; limbs `[forward, out, up, bend, twist]`. The plank attempt pointed its legs up, so start the plank from `MESH2MOTION/Pushup`'s key instead.\n308:## 10. Audio\n333:## 11. UI and UX\n337:**Fonts:** `npm pack @expo-google-fonts/fredoka` and `@expo-google-fonts/nunito` (SIL OFL, static TTFs). Unpack into their own folder and copy `Fredoka_600SemiBold.ttf` (titles, 50 KB) and `Nunito_700Bold.ttf` (body, 132 KB) to `engine/crates/pav_ui/fonts/`. Embed with `include_bytes!`. Credit them on the About screen.\n361:**Touch-only devices:** detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')`, no `(any-pointer: fine)`, and no gamepad or key seen yet. Show a centred card \"Controller or keyboard required\" and a Settings button (tap works; Settings is usable by tap). No touch controls: skip Shardfall's `touch.draw` for this game, and route touches directly to egui in `on_touch`, because the engine's touch layer otherwise treats a finger as a stick. Attract mode runs behind the card. Remove the phone-rotation hint and fullscreen-on-tap from `web/index.html`. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, drop the card and start normally. A touch device without WebGPU cannot run the game at all, so the page's own fallback message there says both things: \"Controller or keyboard required\" and that the game needs WebGPU.\n367:- **Tuning:** live sliders, generated from `impl Tunable for Rules` with `params::list` and `params::set`, grouped by core and by event, with **Reset to Defaults** per group and for all. Must include: stiffness, damping, wobble, tip time, stick curve, key rates, each event's main difficulty number, rhythm windows, spin band, gust strength, bounce gain, Big Stand gusts.\n368:- **View:** input viewer, dot trace, engine stats overlay, free camera, ghost lanes.\n371:## 12. Attract mode\n377:## 13. Multiplayer\n398:**Hub logic lives in about 30 lines of plain JS in the page; Rust only reads and writes window fields.** This exact block passed the harness on a real engine build at 2 players, at 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, and with `scenario=host-leave`, in 14 to 19 s each, and the page ran clean outside a session (verified):\n412:    // Before the first status arrives, report a zero: the hub must always hear a number.\n443:## 14. Architecture\n448:engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/\n458:engine/anim/fit.json                 hand-keyed clips\n459:engine/assets/props/lib/core/*.json  props\n460:engine/crates/pav_ui/src/fit_ui.rs, glyphs.rs, fonts/\n461:engine/crates/pav_audio/src/music.rs, voice.rs\n462:engine/crates/pav_app/src/weblink.rs  window field reads and writes\n463:engine/web/index.html                 hub client, tags, JS, about-data\n466:Register it as `entry::<fit::FitGame>(..., fit::build)`, `KEY = \"fit\"`. Scene names: `fit`, `fit/medley`, `fit/event/<name>`. Read data with `games::level_text(\"fit/rules\", include_str!(\"rules.toml\"))`: running from `engine/`, it reads the disk file, so text, numbers and set layouts change with no rebuild. Do not put sets in `engine/rooms/`: that folder feeds the pavilion demo.\n500:| `pav_app/src/app.rs` | When `hud.fit` is set: hide `boot_panel`, `stats_panel`, `guide_panel`, the room card, `hint_bar` and the F1 panel (verified necessary); route Esc and Options to PAUSE instead of `set_menu`; gate `handle_key`; call `weblink` each frame; apply Settings to audio buses; save to `localStorage` when the save serial changes; keep fit bindings in the room-change branch, which otherwise rebinds keys | Removes the engine demo's chrome and keys |\n520:## 15. Verified facts and traps\n523:- `cargo build --locked -p pav_tools --bin pav`: 1m53 first time, 15 to 70 s after. Run from `engine/`.\n544:Engine:\n551:- Run only your own test targets. The engine's other suites check its own catalogue and docs, and a new prop will fail its index check. You do not need them.\n557:## 16. Testing\n574:**`browser` (Playwright, one browser, 320x180, `file://`):** boots with no errors; `__gameStatus` appears; the pad stub moves focus and confirms; keyboard does the same; mouse hover moves focus and click activates, using rects the UI publishes in `window.__gameUi`; prompts switch with the device; Settings has the Xbox option; attract starts after 10 s and any input exits it; music reaches about 10% by the sound patch. Touch: Chromium with a phone and a tablet profile (it has WebGPU) must show \"Controller or keyboard required\", run attract, and respond to a Settings tap by `page.touchscreen.tap`. WebKit with an iPhone profile, which has no WebGPU here, must show the fallback message from section 11.\n582:## 17. Build order\n586:1. **Setup.** Pick the title. `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall engine` (it is public). Copy the starter to `games/fit/`, register it, build `pav` and the web page, first `tests/run.sh`.\n587:2. **Seams.** Hide the chrome, fit input layout, `lean`, fonts, `fit_ui` with a Title and a Pause, Flow state machine, `weblink`, `__gameStatus`, save, a one-event Medley stub, hub JS. Get the harness and the browser smoke green now, before content exists.\n588:3. **First slice.** Balance Core, Puck, tilt, `studio` set, Pose Parade, event card and result, bot, one result screen in full art. Play it by bot and capture it. Tune until a ring streak feels good.\n589:4. **Island and voice.** `hub` set and props, walking, interactables, dialogue with syllables, audio buses, Lobby Bossa, Pip, the Morning Check, Balance Age, Calendar, Clam.\n590:5. **Events** in this order: Cannonball Cup, Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Tempo Squats, Breath Bloom, Step Party (with sequencer and rhythm clock), Morning Lap, Plank Standoff, Floatie Spin, Tray Trek.\n591:6. **Meta.** Days, unlocks, titles, wardrobe, flip-flops, Yesterday You, absence comments, all songs and SFX.\n592:7. **Finale and endings.** Big Stand, both endings, credits, Free Play.\n593:8. **Shell.** Attract, Settings, Dev Mode, touch-only card, How to Play, About.\n594:9. **Multiplayer.** Full Medley, hub ghosts in every lane, Play Together.\n595:10. **Polish.** Write the script to full length, feel pass on every event using the sliders, extra set dressing, particles, transitions, stingers.\n596:11. **Finish** (section 18).\n600:## 18. Finishing\n602:1. Write the exit interview your brief names. Fill every field honestly; `usage` is exactly \"added on import\". Suggested `aiHub` values: type `Game`, genre `Sports`, source `Wii Fit`, series `Wii Fit`, players `1–4`, tags from `3d`, `third-person`, `comedy`, `sports`, `versus`, `low-poly`. Check that it parses.\n603:2. Run `tools/build.sh`: copy the exit interview into `about-data` in the page, run the single-file build with your title, description and theme colour, and write the HTML where your brief says. The About screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback from that block, including the fonts' and motion libraries' credits (`engine/store/CREDITS.md`, each clip set's `credit`).\n604:3. Run `tests/run.sh all` on the final page. Open it once from `file://` at 1920x1080 and look at one frame.\n605:4. Put the same Source Information and feedback in your chat reply.\n606:5. Delete `engine/target` and other caches. Leave the source, tests and notes in the dev folder.\n608:### What each brief item maps to\n616:| Build on the engine, change anything | 14 |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_579","type":"reasoning","text":"**Assessing architecture gaps**\n**Inspecting source architecture**"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_580","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '15,227p' PLAN.md; printf '\\\\n--- IMPLEMENTATION ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,180p' 'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/web/game.js'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_580","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '15,227p' PLAN.md; printf '\\\\n--- IMPLEMENTATION ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,180p' 'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/web/game.js'\"","aggregated_output":"## 1. The game in one page\n\nYou have won a five-day stay at Tippy Cay, a small wellness resort staffed entirely by talking gym equipment. You do not remember entering. Each morning a relentlessly pleasant wobble cushion tests your balance and gives you a Balance Age. Each day you walk the island, try short stillness, strength, cardio and balance events, and bank minutes in a giant clam. Checkout requires a Balance Age of 40 or better. Day 5 ends in the Big Stand, a finale whose last test is to do nothing at all for thirty seconds while the game tries to make you press something.\n\n- **Genre:** sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame (daily ritual, unlocks, wardrobe). Catalogue genre: Sports.\n- **Perspective:** third person throughout, with a camera chosen per activity: 3/4 follow on the island, a mirror-style front view for exercises on the spot, chase for the jog and the paddle, high 3/4 for the table, side view for the dives.\n- **Length:** a first run takes 25 to 40 minutes. It shows every feature. Free play follows.\n\n| What makes Wii Fit distinctive | How this game turns it into play |\n|---|---|\n| A balance board: your centre of pressure is the only verb, and tiny movements matter | The Balance Core (section 4): one analog dot driven by lean. Every event is played through it |\n| The body test and the verdict of a fitness age | The Morning Wobble Check and Balance Age. Never weight, BMI or body shape |\n| Equipment that talks: cheerful, polite, quietly rude | Pip, a talking wobble cushion, plus a whole staff of talking gear |\n| A calm, uncanny instructor | Posey, a faceless wooden artist's mannequin |\n| Four disciplines: yoga, strength, aerobics, balance games | Four pavilions, each with its own coach and events |\n| The daily ritual: calendar stamps, banked minutes that unlock more | Calendar stamps and the Minute Clam |\n| Noticing how long you stayed away | Real-date absence comments from Pip |\n| A family sharing one board and comparing progress | Hot-seat Medley, Yesterday You ghosts, AI Hub sessions |\n| Clean, quiet, pastel, unintentionally funny | High-key pastel look, gentle lounge music, short deadpan text |\n\n**Pillars.** Check every decision against these.\n1. **Small movements, big consequences.** Mastery means doing less. The best moments are held breaths.\n2. **Deadpan encouragement.** Everything you do is commented on, kindly, and slightly too honestly.\n3. **A daily ritual.** Check in, get a number, do your exercises, get a stamp.\n4. **Calm surface, silly underneath.** The screen stays serene while a seagull stands on your head.\n\n**Originality rules.** This is an original game in the same genre, not a recreation.\n- Inside the game, use no Nintendo names (Wii, Mii, Balance Board and so on). The only exceptions are the Source line on the About screen and whatever your title's riff requires.\n- No white rectangular board with dot eyes. No pale human trainer in a tank top and ponytail. No Mii-style avatars or face editors. No island or plaza from the source series.\n- No source music, jingles, menu layouts or screen compositions. Do not quote or paraphrase its lines. Write your own.\n- Events have their own names and twists, as specified below.\n- Respect bodies: no weight, BMI, body-shape jokes or diet talk anywhere. Pip judges your wobble, your habits and your absences.\n\n## 2. Structure of play\n\n**Boot:** title screen over a slow island sweep. Menu: New Stay or Continue, Play Together, Settings, About. After 10 seconds with no input on the title or any pre-game menu, attract mode starts (section 12).\n\n**New Stay:** choose one of 4 guest slots, pick a name from a list of about 40 funny preset names (no on-screen keyboard), pick a look (6 skin tones, 8 outfits). Then a short intro with Pip at reception, skippable.\n\n**A day:**\n1. Wake on the cabana deck. Pip greets you, with an absence comment if real days have passed.\n2. Morning Wobble Check (about 70 seconds), Balance Age reveal, Pip's comment.\n3. Free time on the island: walk, talk to guests, find lost flip-flops, step on an event mat. The Schedule (Triangle or Tab) lists everything and fast-travels.\n4. When the day's minute goal is met, Pip says so. Sleep at your cabana (or choose End Day in the Schedule). A big stamp lands on the Calendar. Next day.\n\n| Day | Opens | Minute goal | Story beat |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Stillness Studio: Breath Bloom, Pose Parade | 3 | Arrival. The checkout rule. \"Nobody has asked to leave yet\" |\n| 2 | Iron Gazebo: Tempo Squats, Plank Standoff | 5 | Big Kettle. Wardrobe opens |\n| 3 | Boardwalk: Step Party, Floatie Spin, Morning Lap | 7 | Yesterday You appears as a ghost. \"I am not comparing you\" |\n| 4 | Lagoon: Tide Table, Paddle Slalom, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup | 9 | Guests start whispering about the Big Stand |\n| 5 | The Big Stand, after the morning check | none | Finale, ending, free play |\n\n**Minutes:** the first clear of an event each day banks 1 + stars (0 to 3 stars, so 1 to 4 minutes); repeats bank 1. Resort minutes are openly not real minutes (\"Our minutes are longer. It is a wellness thing\").\n\n**Endings:** Balance Age 40 or better: you may check out, by rowboat (`LIB/core/rowboat`). Otherwise: the Extended Stay ending, gentle and funny. Both roll credits, then unlock Free Play: every event open, personal bests, star goals, and a calendar that keeps stamping real days.\n\n**Bot rule:** `Game::bot` must be able to play this entire flow, menus included, from New Stay to the credits. That is your scripted playthrough and the base of attract mode.\n\n## 3. Controls\n\nThe left stick is both walking and leaning. Prompts always show the glyph for the input used last.\n\n| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Walk on the island, lean in events | Left stick | W A S D (arrows also walk) | Island: click a place or thing to walk there. Events: cursor offset from screen centre is the lean |\n| Fine lean | Stick itself | Hold Shift (half key rate) | Small cursor moves |\n| Jog on the island | Hold R2 | Hold Shift | |\n| Action: talk, begin, inhale, squat, bounce | Cross | Space | Left button |\n| Left step / right step | L1 or L2 / R1 or R2 | Q or Left / E or Right | Left button / right button |\n| Brace (hold both) | L2+R2 or L1+R1 | Q+E | Both buttons |\n| Wave at someone | Square | F | |\n| Schedule | Triangle | Tab | |\n| Island camera | Right stick | | Right-drag, wheel zooms |\n| Pause | Options | Esc | |\n| Menus | D-pad or left stick, Cross confirms, Circle backs, L1/R1 change tabs | Arrows or W A S D, Enter or Space, Esc backs, Q/E change tabs | Hover moves focus, click activates, right-click backs |\n\nXbox glyphs (Settings option) swap A B X Y, LB RB LT RT, Menu. Ignore Options while Create is held: that pair belongs to the AI Hub. Disable the engine's own keys (F1 to F10, digits, H, Backspace rewind, right-drag tilt) outside dev mode. Keep F11 for fullscreen.\n\n## 4. The Balance Core\n\nOne struct, `BalanceCore`, used by every event. Its state is `cob` (the dot, unit disc, x right, y up on screen) and `vel`.\n\n```\ntarget = shaped lean input * reach + wobble(t)\nacc    = (target - cob) * stiffness - vel * damping + gust + nudge\nvel   += acc * dt\ncob   += vel * dt\ntip    = |cob| > 1 for tip_time seconds\n```\n\nStart with `stiffness 40`, `damping 8.5`, `reach 0.92`, `tip_time 0.35`. `wobble` is `amp * (0.7 * sin(2*pi*1.3*t + a) + 0.3 * sin(2*pi*2.9*t + b))` per axis, phases from `sim.state.rng`, base `amp 0.12`, scaled per event and by fatigue, plus a velocity kick of 0.1 units/s in a random direction every 1 to 2 seconds. Use sim time, never the clock.\n\n**Feel targets** (these numbers give them, by numeric simulation at 60 ticks/s): full stick reaches 90% in about 0.4 s with about 5% overshoot, like a body. Release settles in about 0.45 s. Left alone, the dot wanders at a mean radius of 0.05, at most 0.08. A held full lean does not tip by itself; a gust on top of it does.\n\n**Input shaping** (in `pav_app`, passed as `InputFrame.lean`, screen space):\n- **Stick:** deadzone 0.12, response curve `x^1.5` so small motions are fine.\n- **Keyboard:** keys move the target at 1.6 units/s and it returns at 1.2 units/s when released. Tapping gives small nudges, so keys feel native, not bang-bang.\n- **Mouse:** cursor offset from the screen centre divided by 0.38 of the window height, clamped to the disc. No pointer lock. The device moved last wins.\n\n**Body:** the figure tilts with the dot (`cob * 14` degrees about the feet, engine change in section 14). Beyond |cob| 0.75 an upper-body arm-flail clip fades in. A tip plays a stumble and, over water, a splash. Tips never end the game; they cost time or score.\n\n**HUD, the Puck:** a large circular gauge drawn in egui: a pale disc, a green target ring, a coral dot, and stars at the edge when streaking. It must read from 10 feet. It looks good at 340 px diameter at 1080p (verified). Put it top centre or bottom centre, whichever does not cover the figure in that event.\n\n## 5. Events\n\n**Common frame:** event card (name, one-sentence goal, glyph prompts, one coach line), 3-2-1, play, result (score 0 to 1000, stars at 400, 650 and 850, a deadpan Title, minutes banked, personal best, difference from Yesterday You; Retry or Back).\n\n**Every event has:** a section of tunable numbers in `rules.toml`, a bot that earns at least 2 stars, an idle-input outcome below 1 star, a ghost lane, and an attract segment. Scenes `fit/event/<name>` start an event directly, for tools and tests.\n\n### Stillness Studio (Posey). Set: `studio`, a round white deck on a calm dawn lagoon. Camera: mirror view (yaw 0, tilt 12, distance 8.5, fov 36; the figure faces +Z, toward the camera, and stick right is screen right).\n\n**Breath Bloom** (45 s). Hold Action to inhale, release to exhale, following a guide ring: 4 s in, 4 s out, 5 cycles, the last one longer. `lungs` rises while held and falls when not. Keep the dot inside a centre ring of radius 0.35. Tick score: `0.7 * (1 - clamp(|lungs - guide| / 0.35)) + 0.3 * inRing`. Each good cycle opens a lotus on the water with a rising pentatonic chime; a perfect run blooms the whole pond. Scrub the clip `FIT/Breath` by `lungs`. No fail state. Bot: holds while the guide rises.\n\n**Pose Parade** (3 poses, 20 s each). Six hand-keyed poses with deadpan names: the Patient Heron, the Apologetic Lunge, the Tired Lighthouse, the Folded Deck Chair, the Reluctant Bridge, Seated Disappointment. Day 1 uses the first three. Posey holds the pose beside you. A target ring (radius 0.30 shrinking to 0.18) drifts on a slow Lissajous path (amplitude 0.35, 0.12 Hz). Inside the ring a streak multiplier climbs x1 to x4, one step per 2 s; leaving resets it. At 12 s of pose 2 a gull lands on your head and wobble is x1.6 for 5 s (\"There is a bird on you. Accept the bird\"). A tip breaks the pose for 1.5 s. Score: time in ring weighted by multiplier. Bot: PD toward the ring centre.\n\n### Iron Gazebo (Big Kettle). Set: `gazebo`, a white iron gazebo at golden hour. Camera: 3/4 front.\n\n**Tempo Squats** (10 reps, about 50 s). Hold Action to go down (2 s to full depth), release to rise (1 s). A guide bar shows the tempo; a low bell marks the bottom. Keep the dot in a band |x| < 0.25; wobble grows 8% per rep. Rep score: `0.7 * timing + 0.3 * band`. Scrub `FIT/Squat` by depth. Gag: rep 10 is followed by \"Ten. Also eleven.\" Bot: follows the guide.\n\n**Plank Standoff** (up to 60 s). Hold Brace and keep the dot in a ring shrinking from 0.40 to 0.20. Releasing, or leaving the ring for more than 1 s, collapses you in a comic flop. Fatigue ramps wobble; at 30 s add tremble; at 45 s Kettle laughs at his own joke and the nudge shakes the screen. Score: seconds survived / 60. Stars at 25, 40 and 55 s. Kettle, who has no arms, plank-talks you through it. Base the pose on one frame of `MESH2MOTION/Pushup`. Bot: survives at least 45 s.\n\n### Boardwalk (Bounce). Set: `boardwalk`, a beach boardwalk at bright midday.\n\n**Step Party** (64 s, 96 BPM, song 4). A rhythm game: notes in two lanes fall to two footprints, left, right or both, on an aerobic step box. Perfect within 55 ms, Good within 120 ms. About 100 notes, data in `charts.toml`, starting with quarter notes and building to eighths and doubles. Bounce bounces on the beat and guests clap on downbeats. Timing uses the audio clock (section 10). Camera: mirror view, slightly high. Bot: presses exactly on each note.\n\n**Floatie Spin** (50 s). Circle the lean (stick, mouse, or rolling W-D-S-A) to spin inflatable rings around your hips. Spin speed is the smoothed angular velocity of the lean while |lean| > 0.4; the sweet band is 6 to 9 rad/s, and a `spin_band_scale` rule widens it for keyboard. \"Switch!\" flips the required direction every 15 s. Guests toss new rings from left or right: press that side's step within 0.25 s of arrival to catch it. Out of band, rings sink; on the floor they are lost. Maximum 7 rings. Score: rings times time in band. Rings are no-physics entities positioned in code. Bot: 7.5 rad/s circle, presses on arrivals.\n\n**Morning Lap** (about 90 s, one lap of the hub island). Alternate left and right steps to set your pace (1.6 to 2.4 steps/s is the zone). Too fast raises a stitch meter that makes you stumble; too slow and Bounce, the pacer rolling ahead, gets away. The path steers you; lean moves you up to 1.2 m sideways to dodge crabs, sunbathers and towels and to grab ribbons. Flip-flops can be found here too. Score: time in zone, plus ribbons, minus bumps. Camera: chase with per-tick yaw. Use `MESH2MOTION/Jog` scaled to speed. Bot: 2 steps/s, steers to ribbons.\n\n### Lagoon (Commodore Gull). Sets: `tide`, `channel`, `pier`, `tower`.\n\n**Tide Table** (3 boards, 60 s total). You stand on a floating square raft and your lean tilts it. Roll hermit crabs in shells into tide pools. Board 1: 3 shells. Board 2: 5 shells and a moving pool. Board 3: 7 shells, bumpers and a rising tide. Fast shells skip over pools. Write the shell physics as simple 2D code (`a = tilt * g - friction * v`, wall bounce 0.5), not rapier: it is more tunable and bot-friendly. Score: shells potted plus time left. Camera: high 3/4 (tilt 62). Bot: PD steering of the nearest shell toward the nearest pool.\n\n**Paddle Slalom** (about 45 s). Stand on a paddleboard on a long channel and pass buoy gates. Lean x steers. Lean forward speeds up and risks tipping, lean back brakes. Gusts, shown as ripple streaks, push the dot. A tip is a big splash and a 2 s remount. A missed gate adds 2 s. `score = clamp((1.6 * par - t) / (0.8 * par)) * 1000`. Standing on water uses the trick in section 15; a silent `Wake` event every few ticks draws the wake. Camera: chase (tilt 22, distance 10). Bot: steers to gate centres at forward lean 0.5.\n\n**Tray Trek** (about 50 s). Walk a long pier at a fixed pace, carrying a tray with a stack of 5 smoothies. Waves, plank gaps and swooping gulls jolt the tray. Your dot tilts it. Glasses slide with tilt and plop into the sea past the edge. Score: 200 per glass delivered, plus a no-spill bonus. Marjorie receives what is left and comments. Use `STYLE100/Balance_Walk` plus an upper-body `FIT/CarryTray` clip. Bot: counters the jolts it knows are coming.\n\n**Cannonball Cup** (3 dives, about 40 s). The board bounces with a 1.2 s period. Press Action at the bottom of 3 bounces to build power, the 4th press leaps. In the air, hold Action to tuck and lean to rotate. Enter tucked and high for the biggest splash. Three gull judges hold up cards: \"6.5\", \"7\", \"See me\". \"We are not here for form. We are here for splash.\" Score: height x tuck x timing. Camera: side view (yaw 90, tilt 6, distance 14). The splash must be huge: a new `BigSplash` event scales the water dents and particles. This is the attract mode's hero shot. Bot: presses on bottoms, tucks at the apex.\n\n### The Big Stand (finale, about 2.5 minutes). Set: `bay`, a tiny post in the bay at sunset, with the whole cast watching from rafts.\n\nFive phases, reusing event code with new numbers:\n1. Breathing, 4 cycles.\n2. A pose under rising gusts, 20 s.\n3. Step Party for 16 bars with a marching band of guests, wobble on.\n4. Brace while waves crash, 20 s.\n5. **The Long Stillness:** 30 s of nothing. Music fades to silence, the HUD vanishes except the Puck. At 15 s a fake prompt offers \"Press Cross to skip\". Pressing anything forfeits the Inner Peace bonus. Then Pip, quietly: \"...Oh. You're still here. Good.\"\n\nA tip drops you in the sea to a groan from the crowd and puts you back; it costs score and cannot end the run. Final Balance Age = morning age minus `final_score / 100` (up to 10).\n\n### Morning Wobble Check. Set: `studio`. About 70 s, four micro-tests, Pip presiding.\n\n| Test | What you do | Metric (0 to 1) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Stand Still (\"This is the whole test\") | Hold the dot centred for 8 s; one small nudge at 5 s | Mean distance from centre |\n| Lean Targets | A left/right bar: reach \"70% left\", then two more targets, within 6%, hold 1.5 s; 5 s limit each | Time taken |\n| Eyes Closed | 6 s. The screen dims to almost black, the Puck vanishes. A tone's pitch tells your offset, and rumble if the pad has it | Mean distance |\n| Step Test | 8 alternating steps to a 100 BPM metronome | Timing |\n\n```\nskill = 0.30*still + 0.25*targets + 0.25*blind + 0.20*steps\nage   = 24 + 56 * (1 - skill)^1.1 - 2*days_completed - min(total_stars/3, 8)\n```\nClamp to 18..99, round. A middling player (skill 0.5) starts at 50 and reaches about 34 by Day 5; a weak one (skill 0.2) starts at 68 and ends near 52, before the finale's bonus. The big number rolls like a slot machine. Pip's comment is chosen by the change since yesterday and by the worst metric. A sparkline of 5 big dots shows the week. Your figure's posture improves as the age falls (a small constant forward slump through the tilt field, shrinking each day): visible progress, no numbers needed.\n\n## 6. Meta systems\n\n- **Minute Clam:** a giant clam at reception that gulps banked minutes with a gibberish burp. Totals unlock wardrobe items.\n- **Calendar:** five big days, a stamp per completed day, then real days in free play. No tables.\n- **Titles:** after each event Pip awards a deadpan title by score: Human Soup, Acceptable Human, Certified Lean-To, Wobble Enthusiast, Seasoned Tilter, Stillness Intern, Professional Standing Person, Alarmingly Balanced. At least 30, in `script.toml`.\n- **Wardrobe:** reuse the engine's `GearLook`, which needs no new drawing (verified): `helm = cap` (sun cap), `helm = hood` (towel turban), `crown`, `halo`; `gloves` (sweatbands), `belt`, `pauldrons` (reads as arm floaties, funny). Plus shirt, pants and shoe colours. Skip `cape`: it draws long sticks.\n- **Lost flip-flops:** 5 hidden on the island, for Two-Towel Tom. Reward: Golden Flip-Flops (gold shoes) and a line. This is the exploration layer.\n- **Yesterday You:** your best run of each event is recorded and replayed as a tinted figure in a neighbouring lane, from Day 3.\n- **Absence comments:** the page passes today's date to the game at boot, and the save stores the last day played. \"You were away for 2 days. I did not count them. There were 2.\" Passing the date in as data keeps the rule that the sim never reads the clock.\n- **Saves:** versioned JSON in `localStorage`: guest slots (name, look, day, minutes, stars, bests, ghosts, ages, flip-flops, unlocks) and global settings. Save on every change of day and every result.\n\n## 7. World, cast and writing\n\n**Tippy Cay** is about 64 x 48 m: reception at the centre (Pip's desk, Calendar wall, Minute Clam), a ring path for jogging, four pavilions around it, a row of cabanas, a pier, a diving tower and a water channel in the distance. Palms, grass, sand terraces, sea on all sides, circling gulls.\n\n| Character | What it is | Voice and manner |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Pip** | Sky-blue round wobble cushion, two dot eyes (`blob` plan, scale 0.7, squash 2.0, plus a small valve) | Front desk and scorekeeper. Relentlessly pleasant. Keeps records of everything. Never technically insults you. Squeaky rubber voice |\n| **Posey** | Faceless wooden artist's mannequin (biped with eyes the colour of its skin; verified look in section 8) | Stillness. Serene, short, oddly poetic. Soft wood-block voice. It has no eyes and never blinks; \"This has not been discussed\" |\n| **Big Kettle** | Cast-iron kettlebell (dark `blob` plus a torus handle part; add a `Handle` attach kind) | Strength. Booming, gentle, deeply supportive. No arms or legs, cannot do any exercise |\n| **Bounce** | Huge pink exercise ball that never stops hopping (`blob`, scale 1.2, `hop`) | Cardio. Breathless bursts, no full stops |\n| **Commodore Gull** | Small gull in a captain's cap: three no-physics entities, wings rotated in code | Lagoon. Dry, officious, steals snacks |\n| **Marjorie** | Guest in robe and towel turban (`helm = hood`, white) | On Day 5 for eleven years. Knows everything |\n| **Two-Towel Tom** | Guest with two towels | Lost his flip-flops. Asks you to find them |\n| **The Twins** | Two identical guests | Do everything in unison, finish each other's words |\n\n**Writing style.** Short polite sentences. Upbeat. Then one line too honest. Fitness facts of doubtful use. Numbers quoted precisely, for no reason. At most 2 lines on screen at 10 feet. Every coach has at least 25 lines, Pip at least 80, guests about 8 each, per day where it matters. Keep all text in `script.toml`.\n\nTone anchors, all original. Use these and write more like them:\n- Pip: \"Welcome! You have won a complimentary stay. You did not enter. Nobody enters.\"\n- Pip: \"Please stand on me. Gently. I remember everything.\"\n- Pip: \"Your Balance Age today is 61. That is a number. Numbers cannot hurt you. This one is trying.\"\n- Pip: \"You leaned left 64% of the time. Is everything all right on the right?\"\n- Pip: \"That was your best attempt so far. I am as surprised as you are.\"\n- Pip: \"You wobbled 41 times. I stopped counting at 40, out of respect.\"\n- Pip: \"Did you know? Standing still burns calories. Not many. Did you know that, though?\"\n- Pip, on a long pause: \"You have been paused for 4 minutes. Pausing is not an exercise. I checked.\"\n- Posey: \"Breathe in the sea. Not literally.\"\n- Posey: \"Be the heron. The heron does not check the score.\"\n- Big Kettle: \"Lift with your legs. I cannot. I have none. Lift for both of us.\"\n- Bounce: \"Keep going keep going keep- is that your heartbeat? Mine is just air!\"\n- Commodore Gull: \"That was a dive. I am legally required to say so.\"\n- Marjorie: \"Day five? Oh, I'm on day five as well. Eleven years now.\"\n\nDialogue types out with voice blips. Action completes the line, then advances. Keep a Text Speed setting.\n\n## 8. Art direction\n\n--- IMPLEMENTATION ---\n(() => {\n  'use strict';\n\n  const app = document.getElementById('app');\n  const canvas = document.getElementById('world');\n  const context = canvas.getContext('2d');\n  const hub = window.AIHub;\n  const names = ['Alex','Ari','Ash','Bailey','Bea','Benny','Birdie','Blair','Bo','Cameron','Casey','Charlie','Cleo','Coco','Dani','Drew','Eden','Eli','Emery','Finn','Frankie','Harper','Indigo','Jaden','Jamie','Jesse','Jules','Kai','Kit','Lane','Leo','Lou','Marley','Mika','Morgan','Nico','Parker','Quinn','Remy','Robin'];\n  const skins = ['#f4c29c','#dca37a','#b87855','#8a563f','#f5d7c4','#604437'];\n  const outfits = ['#ff826d','#49b4ac','#f5bb52','#8a9cdb','#e77c9d','#87b979','#e9a778','#778a99'];\n  const titles = ['Stillness Intern','Human Soup','Wobble Enthusiast','Certified Lean-To','Acceptable Human','Seasoned Tilter','Professional Standing Person','Alarmingly Balanced','Chief of Almost','Puddle Avoider','The Upright-ish','Assistant to Gravity','A Quiet Triumph','Exceptionally Present','Honorary Buoy','Very Good at Floor','Sensible Seagull','The Sway Whisperer','Locally Stable','Foot Placement Expert','A Fine Vertical','Slightly Legendary','Calm Adjacent','Proudly Perpendicular','The Unfallen','Official Dot Mover','Ocean Negotiator','Flamingo in Training','Grand Marshal of Balance','Keeper of the Wobble'];\n  const events = [\n    {id:'breath', name:'Breath Bloom', day:1, coach:'Posey', place:'Stillness Studio', length:32, description:'Breathe with the flower. Hold Action as it opens; release as it closes.', controls:'Hold and release Action with the flower.'},\n    {id:'pose', name:'Pose Parade', day:1, coach:'Posey', place:'Stillness Studio', length:36, description:'Follow three gently drifting poses. Keep your dot inside the moving ring.', controls:'Lean toward the moving target.'},\n    {id:'squat', name:'Tempo Squats', day:2, coach:'Big Kettle', place:'Iron Gazebo', length:32, description:'A very dignified imaginary chair awaits. Press on the beat.', controls:'Press Action when the ring closes.'},\n    {id:'plank', name:'Plank Standoff', day:2, coach:'Big Kettle', place:'Iron Gazebo', length:30, description:'Brace against the breeze. A plank is a promise you make to the floor.', controls:'Hold Action and keep the dot centered.'},\n    {id:'step', name:'Step Party', day:3, coach:'Bounce', place:'Boardwalk', length:32, description:'Find your feet at 96 beats per minute. Left, right, and repeat.', controls:'Alternate Left and Right on the beat.'},\n    {id:'spin', name:'Floatie Spin', day:3, coach:'Bounce', place:'Boardwalk', length:32, description:'Circle your lean to keep a bright stack of floaties spinning.', controls:'Circle with WASD, the stick, or mouse.'},\n    {id:'lap', name:'Morning Lap', day:3, coach:'Bounce', place:'Boardwalk', length:35, description:'Take the scenic route. Alternate your steps and steer around beach clutter.', controls:'Alternate Left and Right; lean to steer.'},\n    {id:'tide', name:'Tide Table', day:4, coach:'Commodore Gull', place:'Lagoon', length:40, description:'Tilt the raft to roll a shell into the tide pool. Mind the edges.', controls:'Lean to roll the shell into the pool.'},\n    {id:'paddle', name:'Paddle Slalom', day:4, coach:'Commodore Gull', place:'Lagoon', length:36, description:'Steer through the buoy gates. The sea is mostly on your side.', controls:'Lean left and right to meet the gates.'},\n    {id:'tray', name:'Tray Trek', day:4, coach:'Marjorie', place:'Lagoon Pier', length:35, description:'Carry five very optimistic smoothies across a wobbly pier.', controls:'Keep the dot centered through the gusts.'},\n    {id:'dive', name:'Cannonball Cup', day:4, coach:'Commodore Gull', place:'Lagoon Tower', length:36, description:'Time your bounce, tuck in the air, and make a spectacular splash.', controls:'Press Action at the bottom of a bounce; hold to tuck.'},\n    {id:'finale', name:'The Big Stand', day:5, coach:'Pip', place:'Sunset Bay', length:90, description:'The whole island is watching. Breathe, pose, step, brace, and finally be still.', controls:'Follow each phase. During Long Stillness, do nothing.'}\n  ];\n  const medley = ['paddle','tide','dive'];\n  const goals = [3,5,7,9,0];\n  const keys = new Set();\n  const storage = 'wii-fit-together-v1';\n  let saved = readStorage();\n  let settings = Object.assign({music:0.1, sound:true, glyph:'PlayStation'}, saved.settings || {});\n  let state = {screen:'title', previous:'title', slot:null, profile:null, setup:{name:'Alex',skin:0,outfit:0}, round:null, paused:false, together:null, hub:null, lastInput:performance.now(), device:'keyboard', attract:false, message:'', returnScreen:'title'};\n  let center = {x:0,y:0,vx:0,vy:0}, aim = {x:0,y:0}, mouseAim = null, mouseHeld = false, previousButtons = [], audio, musicClock = 0, lastFrame = performance.now(), lastHubUpdate = 0, lastHubProgress = 0;\n  let viewport = {width:0,height:0,scale:1,ox:0,oy:0};\n\n  function readStorage() { try { return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(storage) || '{}'); } catch (_) { return {}; } }\n  function save() { try { saved.settings = settings; saved.slots ||= [null,null,null,null]; if (state.profile && state.slot !== null) saved.slots[state.slot] = state.profile; localStorage.setItem(storage, JSON.stringify(saved)); } catch (_) {} }\n  function esc(value) { return String(value).replace(/[&<>\"']/g, character => ({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;',\"'\":'&#39;'}[character])); }\n  function clamp(value, min, max) { return Math.max(min, Math.min(max, value)); }\n  function smooth(value, target, rate, dt) { return value + (target-value) * Math.min(1,rate*dt); }\n  function markInput(device) { const needsRender = state.attract || (!state.hasHardwareInput && (device === 'keyboard' || device === 'gamepad')); state.device = device; state.lastInput = performance.now(); if (device === 'keyboard' || device === 'gamepad') state.hasHardwareInput = true; if (needsRender) { state.attract = false; render(); } }\n  function sound(frequency=440, length=.08, type='sine', volume=.06) {\n    if (!settings.sound) return;\n    try { audio ||= new (window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext)(); if (audio.state === 'suspended') audio.resume(); const oscillator=audio.createOscillator(), gain=audio.createGain(); oscillator.type=type; oscillator.frequency.value=frequency; gain.gain.setValueAtTime(volume,audio.currentTime); gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(.001,audio.currentTime+length); oscillator.connect(gain).connect(audio.destination); oscillator.start(); oscillator.stop(audio.currentTime+length); } catch (_) {}\n  }\n  function voice() { [490,610,520].forEach((tone,index) => setTimeout(() => sound(tone,.07,'sine',.025),index*75)); }\n  function music(dt) { if (!audio || !settings.music || document.hidden) return; musicClock -= dt; if (musicClock <= 0) { musicClock=.48; const notes=[261.63,329.63,392,329.63,293.66,349.23,440,349.23]; const index=Math.floor(performance.now()/480)%notes.length; try { const oscillator=audio.createOscillator(), gain=audio.createGain(); oscillator.type='sine'; oscillator.frequency.value=notes[index]; gain.gain.setValueAtTime(settings.music*.07,audio.currentTime); gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(.001,audio.currentTime+.32); oscillator.connect(gain).connect(audio.destination); oscillator.start(); oscillator.stop(audio.currentTime+.32); } catch (_) {} } }\n  function button(label, action, extra='', subtitle='') { return `<button class=\"button ${extra}\" data-action=\"${action}\">${label}${subtitle ? `<small>${subtitle}</small>` : ''}</button>`; }\n  function header(right='A little balance goes a long way') { return `<div class=\"topbar\"><div class=\"logo\">TIPPY <i>✳</i> CAY</div><span class=\"pill\"><span class=\"sun-dot\"></span>${esc(right)}</span></div>`; }\n  function shell(content, right) { return `<div class=\"screen\">${header(right)}${content}</div>`; }\n  function modal(title, eyebrow, content, back='title') { return shell(`<div class=\"panel-wrap\"><section class=\"panel\"><div class=\"panel-head\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">${eyebrow}</div><h2>${title}</h2></div><button class=\"close\" data-action=\"${back}\" aria-label=\"Back\">×</button></div>${content}</section></div>`); }\n  function profileName() { return state.profile ? state.profile.name : 'Guest'; }\n  function profileDay() { return state.profile ? clamp(state.profile.day,1,5) : 1; }\n  function eventById(id) { return events.find(item => item.id === id); }\n  function unlocked(item) { return state.profile && (state.profile.freePlay || item.day <= state.profile.day); }\n  function formatScore(score) { return Math.round(score).toLocaleString(); }\n\n  function render() {\n    let html = '';\n    if (state.screen === 'title') {\n      const hasSave = (saved.slots || []).some(Boolean);\n      html = shell(`<div class=\"title-layout\"><section class=\"title-panel\"><div class=\"overline\">A rather uplifting island escape</div><h1>Wii Fit<br><span>Together.</span></h1><p class=\"lede\">Welcome to Tippy Cay, where the sea is calm, the company is questionable, and balance is a journey.</p><div class=\"title-actions\">${button('New Stay','slots-new','primary','A five-day island adventure')}${button('Continue','slots-continue','',hasSave?'Welcome back to the island':'Choose a guest to continue')}${button('Play Together','together','coral','Local or AI Hub medley')}${button('Settings','settings','', 'Controls, sound & accessibility')}</div></section><aside class=\"hero-note\"><b>A note from Pip</b>“We believe in you.<br>Gravity has declined to comment.”</aside></div><div class=\"footer\"><span>✳ AN ORIGINAL TIPPY CAY GETAWAY</span><div><button class=\"pill\" data-action=\"about\">About this game</button> <span class=\"hint\">WASD / arrows · Space · Controller</span></div></div>`, 'THE ISLAND IS OPEN');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'slots') {\n      const slots = saved.slots || [null,null,null,null];\n      html = modal(state.slotMode === 'new' ? 'Choose a guest' : 'Welcome back', 'THE GUEST BOOK', `<p>Every guest gets a little corner of the island. Choose an empty book to begin.</p><div class=\"cards\">${slots.map((guest,index) => `<button class=\"card\" data-action=\"slot:${index}\"><strong>${guest ? esc(guest.name) : 'Guest '+(index+1)+' · Empty'}</strong><small>${guest ? `Day ${guest.day} · ${guest.minutesTotal || 0} minutes banked` : 'Ready for a new stay'}</small></button>`).join('')}</div><p class=\"tiny\">Your progress stays in this browser on this device.</p>`);\n    } else if (state.screen === 'customize') {\n      html = modal('Make yourself at home','YOUR ISLAND LOOK', `<p>Pick a name and an outfit. Your look is always welcome here.</p><label class=\"field\">Guest name<select id=\"guest-name\">${names.map(name=>`<option ${name === state.setup.name ? 'selected' : ''}>${name}</option>`).join('')}</select></label><div class=\"field\">Skin tone<div class=\"swatches\">${skins.map((color,index)=>`<button class=\"swatch ${index===state.setup.skin?'selected':''}\" style=\"background:${color}\" data-action=\"skin:${index}\" aria-label=\"Skin tone ${index+1}\"></button>`).join('')}</div></div><div class=\"field\">Outfit color<div class=\"swatches\">${outfits.map((color,index)=>`<button class=\"swatch ${index===state.setup.outfit?'selected':''}\" style=\"background:${color}\" data-action=\"outfit:${index}\" aria-label=\"Outfit color ${index+1}\"></button>`).join('')}</div></div><div class=\"row\">${button('Back','slots-new')}${button('Arrive on the island','create-guest','primary')}</div>`, 'slots-new');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'intro') {\n      html = modal(`Welcome, ${esc(profileName())}!`,'A WORD FROM PIP', `<div class=\"dialogue\"><span class=\"speaker\">PIP · RECEPTION CUSHION</span><p>“I’m Pip. I run reception, mostly by remaining in one place. You’ll fit right in.”</p><p>Each morning starts with a Wobble Check. Try activities, collect minutes for the giant clam, and take the week at your own pace.</p></div><div class=\"row\">${button('Let’s explore','island','primary')}</div>`);\n    } else if (state.screen === 'island') {\n      const guest=state.profile, day=profileDay(), goal=goals[day-1];\n      const available=events.filter(item=>unlocked(item));\n      html = shell(`<div class=\"island-layout\"><section class=\"island-panel\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">HELLO, ${esc(guest.name.toUpperCase())} · ${guest.freePlay?'FREE PLAY':'YOUR ISLAND STAY'}</div><h2>Find your<br>happy wobble.</h2><div class=\"dayline\"><span>DAY ${day} / 5</span><span>✳ ${guest.dayMinutes || 0} / ${goal || '∞'} MIN</span><span>★ ${guest.stars || 0} STARS</span></div><p class=\"island-note\">${guest.checked ? `Pip says your Balance Age is ${guest.age}. The clam looks impressed.` : 'Pip is waiting for your morning Wobble Check.'}</p><div class=\"activity-list\">${!guest.checked ? `<button class=\"activity highlight\" data-action=\"check\"><span>◉</span><strong>Morning Wobble Check<small>Say hello to Pip · about a minute</small></strong><b>→</b></button>` : ''}${available.map(item=>`<button class=\"activity\" data-action=\"intro:${item.id}\"><span>${item.day===4?'≈':item.day===3?'✳':item.day===5?'★':'◌'}</span><strong>${item.name}<small>${item.place} · ${item.coach}</small></strong><b>→</b></button>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"row island-actions\">${button('Guest book','calendar')}${button(day===5?'Finish the stay':'Call it a day','end-day','primary')}</div></section></div><div class=\"footer\"><span>MINUTE CLAM: ${guest.minutesTotal || 0} MINUTES SAVED</span><button class=\"pill\" data-action=\"settings\">Settings</button></div>`, guest.freePlay ? 'FREE PLAY' : `DAY ${day} OF 5`);\n    } else if (state.screen === 'calendar') {\n      const guest=state.profile;\n      html = modal('Your island log','THE GUEST BOOK', `<p>Every visit is worth a stamp. Your best moments stay right here.</p><div class=\"cards\">${[1,2,3,4,5].map(day=>`<div class=\"card\"><strong>${day < guest.day || guest.freePlay ? '✓' : '○'} Day ${day}</strong><small>${day===guest.day&&!guest.freePlay?'Currently exploring':day < guest.day || guest.freePlay?'A day well spent':'A day to look forward to'}</small></div>`).join('')}</div><p>Balance Age: <strong>${guest.age ?? 'not checked yet'}</strong> · Total: <strong>${guest.minutesTotal || 0} minutes</strong></p><div class=\"row\">${button('Back to the island','island','primary')}</div>`, 'island');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'eventIntro') {\n      const item=eventById(state.eventId);\n      html = modal(item.name, `${esc(item.place.toUpperCase())} · WITH ${esc(item.coach.toUpperCase())}`, `<div class=\"dialogue\"><span class=\"speaker\">${esc(item.coach.toUpperCase())} SAYS</span><p>“${esc(item.description)}”</p></div><p><strong>How to play:</strong> ${esc(item.controls)}</p><p>Move with WASD, arrows, a controller stick, or your mouse. Action is Space, Enter, controller south button, or click.</p><div class=\"row\">${button('Not yet','cancel-event')}${button('I’m ready','begin-event','primary')}</div>`, 'cancel-event');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'checkIntro') {\n      html = modal('Morning Wobble Check','PIP · RECEPTION CUSHION', `<div class=\"dialogue\"><p>“This is not a test of your worth. It is a test of whether the dot stays near the middle.”</p></div><p>Four little checks: stand still, lean toward targets, close your eyes, and alternate steps. Your Balance Age is a playful score, not medical advice.</p><div class=\"row\">${button('Back','island')}${button('Begin the check','begin-check','primary')}</div>`, 'island');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'event' || state.screen === 'check') {\n      const round=state.round;\n      html = shell(`<div class=\"hud\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">${esc(round.place.toUpperCase())}</div><h2 id=\"round-name\">${esc(round.name)}</h2><div id=\"round-subtitle\">${esc(round.instruction)}</div></div><div class=\"hud-right\"><div class=\"pill\" id=\"timer\">${Math.ceil(round.length)}s</div><button class=\"pill\" data-action=\"pause\">Ⅱ Pause</button></div></div><div class=\"event-center\"><div class=\"phase-card\" id=\"phase-card\">${esc(round.instruction)}</div></div><div class=\"event-bottom\"><div class=\"puck\" aria-label=\"Balance puck\"><div class=\"target\" id=\"target\"></div><div class=\"dot\" id=\"dot\"></div></div><div class=\"meter\"><div><strong id=\"round-score\">0</strong> <span id=\"score-label\">POINTS</span></div><div class=\"meter-track\"><div id=\"meter-fill\"></div></div><small id=\"round-help\">${esc(round.controls)}</small></div></div>`, state.together ? `PLAYER ${state.together.player+1} · MEDLEY` : 'FIND YOUR BALANCE');\n      if (state.paused) html += `<div class=\"overlay\"><section class=\"panel narrow\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">TAKE YOUR TIME</div><h2>Paused.</h2><p>${state.together?.online?'The online round continues in the background.':'The island isn’t going anywhere.'}</p><div class=\"row\">${button('Resume','resume','primary')}${button('Settings','settings')}${state.together?.online?'':button('Leave activity','leave-event')}</div>${state.together?.online?'':`<details><summary>Developer tuning</summary><label class=\"field\">Spring stiffness<input id=\"dev-stiffness\" type=\"range\" min=\"10\" max=\"80\" value=\"${state.stiffness ?? 40}\"></label><label class=\"field\">Damping<input id=\"dev-damping\" type=\"range\" min=\"2\" max=\"20\" value=\"${state.damping ?? 8.5}\" step=\".5\"></label><label class=\"field\">Wobble<input id=\"dev-wobble\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\".4\" value=\"${state.wobble ?? .12}\" step=\".01\"></label><label class=\"field\">Time scale<input id=\"dev-timeScale\" type=\"range\" min=\".25\" max=\"4\" value=\"${state.timeScale ?? 1}\" step=\".25\"></label><div class=\"row\">${button('Reset tuning','reset-tuning')}${button('Finish activity now','finish-now')}${!state.together?button('Give 5 minutes','give-minutes'):''}</div></details>`}</section></div>`;\n    } else if (state.screen === 'result') {\n      const result=state.result;\n      html = modal(result.isCheck ? `Balance Age: ${result.age}` : result.name, result.isCheck?'MORNING CHECK COMPLETE':'THAT WAS A GOOD WOBBLE', `<div class=\"big-score\">${result.isCheck ? esc(result.age) : formatScore(result.score)}<small>${result.isCheck?'PLAYFUL BALANCE AGE · NOT A HEALTH MEASURE':'POINTS'}</small></div><div class=\"stars\">${'★'.repeat(result.stars || 0)}${'☆'.repeat(3-(result.stars || 0))}</div><div class=\"dialogue\"><span class=\"speaker\">PIP SAYS</span><p>“${esc(result.comment)}”</p></div><div class=\"row\">${button(state.together?'Continue medley':'Back to the island','result-next','primary')}</div>`, state.together?'result-next':'island');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'endDay') {\n      const guest=state.profile, goal=goals[profileDay()-1];\n      const canFinish=guest.checked && (guest.freePlay || guest.day===5 ? guest.finaleDone || guest.freePlay : guest.dayMinutes>=goal);\n      html = modal(guest.day===5?'Check out?':'Time to rest?','THE MINUTE CLAM', `<div class=\"dialogue\"><span class=\"speaker\">PIP · RECEPTION CUSHION</span><p>“The clam has swallowed ${guest.dayMinutes || 0} minutes today. This is apparently a good thing.”</p></div><p>${!guest.checked?'Complete the morning Wobble Check first.':guest.day===5&&!guest.finaleDone&&!guest.freePlay?'Complete The Big Stand before checking out.':!canFinish?`The clam is hoping for ${goal} minutes today. Complete another activity or two.`:'You have done enough for today. The island will be here when you wake.'}</p><div class=\"row\">${button('Keep exploring','island')}${canFinish ? button(guest.day===5?'See the finale':'Sleep until tomorrow','sleep','primary') : ''}</div>`, 'island');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'ending') {\n      html = modal(state.profile.age<=40?'A standing ovation.':'An extended stay.','THE BIG STAND · CHECKOUT', `<div class=\"big-score\">${state.profile.age}<small>FINAL BALANCE AGE</small></div><div class=\"dialogue\"><p>${state.profile.age<=40?'“You did it,” says Pip. “You stood there, and we all felt something.”':'“We’ve extended your stay,” says Pip. “The paperwork is a napkin.”'}</p><p>The cast waves from the water. Your island adventure continues in free play.</p></div><p>Created for Tippy Cay · A playful original game inspired by Wii Fit.</p><div class=\"row\">${button('Continue in free play','free-play','primary')}</div>`, 'island');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'together') {\n      html = modal('Play together','THE ISLAND MEDLEY', `<p>Take turns on one device through Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, and Cannonball Cup. Add up to four guests; each score is out of 3,000.</p><div class=\"cards three\">${[2,3,4].map(number=>`<button class=\"card\" data-action=\"hotseat:${number}\"><strong>${number} guests</strong><small>Pass the controller after each medley</small></button>`).join('')}</div><p class=\"tiny\">When launched from AI Hub, the same medley runs online with translucent ghost guests.</p>`);\n    } else if (state.screen === 'handoff') {\n      const group=state.together, item=eventById(medley[group.event]);\n      html = modal(`Guest ${group.player+1}, you’re up!`,'PASS THE CONTROLLER', `<p>Round ${group.event+1} of 3: <strong>${item.name}</strong></p><div class=\"dialogue\"><p>“No rush,” says Pip. “The sea will wait. The gull might not.”</p></div><div class=\"row\">${button('Start '+item.name,'hotseat-next','primary')}</div>`, 'title');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'podium') {\n      const group=state.together, ranking=group.scores.map((score,index)=>({score,index})).sort((left,right)=>right.score-left.score);\n      html = modal('A very good medley','ISLAND PODIUM', `<p>The clam would like to thank every guest for their outstanding participation.</p><div class=\"cards\">${ranking.map((entry,index)=>`<div class=\"card\"><strong>${['🥇','🥈','🥉','✳'][index]} Guest ${entry.index+1}</strong><small>${formatScore(entry.score)} / 3,000 points</small></div>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"row\">${button('Play again','together')}${button('Return to title','title','primary')}</div>`);\n    } else if (state.screen === 'waiting') {\n      html = modal('Waiting for the island','AI HUB · ONLINE MEDLEY', `<p>${esc(state.message || 'Getting your group together…')}</p><div class=\"dialogue\"><p>Three events. One shared island. Everyone plays at their own pace with live ghost guests.</p></div>${state.hub && !state.hub.splash ? `<div class=\"row\">${button('Ready to play','hub-ready','primary')}</div>` : ''}`);\n    } else if (state.screen === 'settings') {\n      html = modal('Make it yours','SETTINGS & CONTROLS', `<label class=\"field\">Music volume: <span id=\"music-value\">${Math.round(settings.music*100)}%</span><input id=\"music\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"100\" value=\"${Math.round(settings.music*100)}\"></label><label class=\"field\">Sound effects <select id=\"sound\"><option value=\"on\" ${settings.sound?'selected':''}>On</option><option value=\"off\" ${!settings.sound?'selected':''}>Off</option></select></label><label class=\"field\">Controller labels <select id=\"glyph\"><option ${settings.glyph==='PlayStation'?'selected':''}>PlayStation</option><option ${settings.glyph==='Xbox'?'selected':''}>Xbox</option></select></label><p>Keyboard: WASD or arrow keys to lean; Space / Enter to act; Esc to pause. Controller: left stick and ${settings.glyph==='Xbox'?'A':'Cross'}. Mouse: move to lean and click to act. Arrow keys navigate menus.</p><p>Touch-only devices can view the island; connect a controller or keyboard to play.</p><div class=\"row\">${button('Done','settings-back','primary')}</div>`, 'settings-back');\n    } else if (state.screen === 'about') {\n      const info = window.__aboutData || {};\n      const blocks = [['Source Information',info.sourceInformation],['Testing Feedback',info.testingFeedback],['Engine Feedback',info.engineFeedback],['Prompt Feedback',info.promptFeedback]];\n      html = modal('About this game','THE FINE PRINT', `<p>Made with Shardfall and an original island full of questionable advice.</p>${blocks.map(([label,value])=>`<h3>${esc(label)}</h3><div class=\"about-list\">${Array.isArray(value)?value.map(line=>`<p>${esc(line)}</p>`).join(''):Object.entries(value||{}).map(([key,line])=>`<p><strong>${esc(key)}:</strong> ${esc(line)}</p>`).join('')}</div>`).join('')}<h3>Library credits</h3><div class=\"about-list\"><p>Shardfall core assets: Shardfall contributors (CC0 1.0).</p><p>100STYLE motion: Mason, Starke and Komura (CC BY 4.0).</p><p>Mesh2Motion and its contributors; Universal Animation Libraries 1 and 2 by Quaternius (CC0 1.0).</p><p>CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database: free to use, copy, modify and redistribute; the data may not be resold, even in converted form.</p><p>The interface uses system fonts. Shardfall's embedded egui fonts include Hack, Noto Emoji, Ubuntu Light and Emoji Icon Font.</p></div><details class=\"licenses\"><summary>Font license texts</summary>${Object.entries(window.__licenseData || {}).map(([label,text])=>`<h4>${esc(label)}</h4><pre>${esc(text)}</pre>`).join('')}</details><div class=\"row\">${button('Back to the island','title','primary')}</div>`);\n    }\n    if (state.attract && state.screen==='title') html += `<div class=\"attract-label\">A LITTLE ISLAND DAYDREAM · PRESS ANY KEY TO RETURN</div>`;\n    if (isTouchOnly() && !state.hasHardwareInput && !['settings','about'].includes(state.screen)) html += `<div class=\"touch-guard\"><div><strong>Controller or keyboard required</strong><p>Connect one to play. The island will wait for you.</p><button class=\"button\" data-action=\"settings\">Settings</button></div></div>`;\n    app.innerHTML = html;\n    const musicInput=document.getElementById('music');\n    if (musicInput) musicInput.addEventListener('input', event=>{ settings.music=Number(event.target.value)/100; document.getElementById('music-value').textContent=Math.round(settings.music*100)+'%'; save(); });\n    const soundInput=document.getElementById('sound');\n    if (soundInput) soundInput.addEventListener('change', event=>{ settings.sound=event.target.value==='on'; save(); });\n    const glyphInput=document.getElementById('glyph');\n    if (glyphInput) glyphInput.addEventListener('change', event=>{ settings.glyph=event.target.value; save(); render(); });\n    const nameInput=document.getElementById('guest-name');\n    if (nameInput) nameInput.addEventListener('change', event=>{ state.setup.name=event.target.value; });\n    for (const kind of ['stiffness','damping','wobble','timeScale']) { const input=document.getElementById('dev-'+kind); if(input) input.addEventListener('input', event=>{state[kind]=Number(event.target.value);}); }\n  }\n\n  function isTouchOnly() { return matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches; }\n  function newProfile() { return {name:state.setup.name,skin:state.setup.skin,outfit:state.setup.outfit,day:1,dayMinutes:0,minutesTotal:0,stars:0,age:null,checked:false,finaleDone:false,freePlay:false,bests:{},clearedToday:{},lastDate:new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10)}; }\n  function setScreen(screen) { state.screen=screen; render(); }\n  function selectAction(action) {\n    if (!action) return;\n    sound(520,.05);\n    if (action === 'title') { state.paused=false; state.together=null; state.round=null; setScreen('title'); }\n    else if (action === 'slots-new' || action === 'slots-continue') { state.slotMode=action==='slots-new'?'new':'continue'; setScreen('slots'); }\n    else if (action.startsWith('slot:')) { const index=Number(action.slice(5)), guest=(saved.slots||[])[index]; state.slot=index; if (guest) { state.profile=guest; setScreen('island'); } else { state.setup={name:names[index],skin:index%skins.length,outfit:index%outfits.length}; setScreen('customize'); } }\n    else if (action.startsWith('skin:')) { state.setup.skin=Number(action.slice(5)); render(); }\n    else if (action.startsWith('outfit:')) { state.setup.outfit=Number(action.slice(7)); render(); }\n    else if (action==='create-guest') { state.profile=newProfile(); save(); voice(); setScreen('intro'); }\n    else if (action==='island') { if (state.profile) {state.paused=false;setScreen('island');} else setScreen('title'); }\n    else if (action==='calendar') setScreen('calendar');\n    else if (action==='check') { voice(); setScreen('checkIntro'); }\n    else if (action==='begin-check') startCheck();\n    else if (action.startsWith('intro:')) { state.eventId=action.slice(6); voice(); setScreen('eventIntro'); }\n    else if (action==='cancel-event') setScreen(state.together?'handoff':'island');\n    else if (action==='begin-event') startRound(state.eventId);\n    else if (action==='pause') { state.paused=true; render(); }\n    else if (action==='resume') { state.paused=false; render(); }\n    else if (action==='reset-tuning') { state.stiffness=40; state.damping=8.5; state.wobble=.12; state.timeScale=1; render(); }\n    else if (action==='finish-now') { state.paused=false; if(state.screen==='check') finishCheck(); else finishRound(); }\n    else if (action==='give-minutes') { if(state.profile && !state.together) {state.profile.dayMinutes=(state.profile.dayMinutes||0)+5;state.profile.minutesTotal=(state.profile.minutesTotal||0)+5;save();} render(); }\n    else if (action==='leave-event') { state.paused=false; if (state.together && state.together.online) reportHub(); else setScreen(state.together?'handoff':'island'); }\n    else if (action==='result-next') advanceResult();\n    else if (action==='end-day') setScreen('endDay');\n    else if (action==='sleep') { if (state.profile.day===5) setScreen('ending'); else { state.profile.day++; state.profile.dayMinutes=0; state.profile.clearedToday={}; state.profile.checked=false; state.profile.lastDate=new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10); save(); setScreen('island'); } }\n    else if (action==='free-play') { state.profile.freePlay=true; save(); setScreen('island'); }\n    else if (action==='together') { state.together=null; setScreen('together'); }\n    else if (action.startsWith('hotseat:')) { state.together={count:Number(action.slice(8)),player:0,event:0,scores:[0,0,0,0],online:false,ghosts:{}}; setScreen('handoff'); }\n    else if (action==='hotseat-next') { state.eventId=medley[state.together.event]; setScreen('eventIntro'); }\n    else if (action==='settings') { state.returnScreen=state.screen; setScreen('settings'); }\n    else if (action==='settings-back') setScreen(state.returnScreen || 'title');\n    else if (action==='about') setScreen('about');\n    else if (action==='hub-ready') { if(hub) hub.ready(); state.message='Ready! Waiting for the other guests.'; render(); }\n  }\n\n  function startCheck() { center={x:0,y:0,vx:0,vy:0}; aim={x:0,y:0}; state.paused=false; state.round={name:'Morning Wobble Check',place:'Stillness Studio',instruction:'Stand still. This is the whole test.',controls:'Keep the dot near the center.',length:37,elapsed:0,sum:0,samples:0,actionHits:0,actionCount:0,targets:0,phase:0,steps:0,lastStep:'',metric:[0,0,0,0],phaseSamples:[0,0,0,0]}; setScreen('check'); }\n  function startRound(id) { const item=eventById(id); if(!item) return; center={x:0,y:0,vx:0,vy:0}; aim={x:0,y:0}; lastHubUpdate=0; lastHubProgress=0; state.paused=false; state.round={...item,instruction:item.controls,elapsed:0,sum:0,samples:0,actionHits:0,actionCount:0,steps:0,lastStep:'',shellX:0,shellY:0,shellVx:0,shellVy:0,potted:0,spin:0,prevAngle:0,gates:0,gateIndex:-1,stillBroken:false,ghostTrail:[]}; setScreen('event'); if(state.together?.online && hub) hub.progress({score:state.together.scores[0],label:`${item.name}: starting`}); }\n  function triggerAction(side='action') {\n    if (!state.round || !['event','check'].includes(state.screen) || state.paused) return;\n    const round=state.round, time=round.elapsed;\n    if (round.id==='finale' && time>60) round.stillBroken=true;\n    round.actionCount++;\n    if (side==='left' || side==='right') { if (round.lastStep!==side) {round.steps++; round.lastStep=side;} }\n    if (round.id==='squat' || round.id==='step' || round.id==='lap' || round.id==='dive' || state.screen==='check') {\n      const interval=round.id==='dive'?1.2:round.id==='step'?.625:.6;\n      const phase=time%interval; if(Math.min(phase,interval-phase)<.22) round.actionHits++;\n      sound(round.id==='dive'?240:420,.09,'sine',.045);\n    } else sound(360,.06,'sine',.03);\n  }\n  function finishCheck() {\n    const round=state.round;\n    const metric=round.metric.map((value,index)=>round.phaseSamples[index] ? value/round.phaseSamples[index] : 0);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_581","type":"reasoning","text":"**Assessing remaining gaps**\n**Reading game implementation**"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_582","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '94,225p' PLAN.md; sed -n '335,466p' PLAN.md; printf '\\\\n--- RUST HOOK ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,240p' 'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit.rs'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_582","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '94,225p' PLAN.md; sed -n '335,466p' PLAN.md; printf '\\\\n--- RUST HOOK ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,240p' 'Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit.rs'\"","aggregated_output":"## 4. The Balance Core\n\nOne struct, `BalanceCore`, used by every event. Its state is `cob` (the dot, unit disc, x right, y up on screen) and `vel`.\n\n```\ntarget = shaped lean input * reach + wobble(t)\nacc    = (target - cob) * stiffness - vel * damping + gust + nudge\nvel   += acc * dt\ncob   += vel * dt\ntip    = |cob| > 1 for tip_time seconds\n```\n\nStart with `stiffness 40`, `damping 8.5`, `reach 0.92`, `tip_time 0.35`. `wobble` is `amp * (0.7 * sin(2*pi*1.3*t + a) + 0.3 * sin(2*pi*2.9*t + b))` per axis, phases from `sim.state.rng`, base `amp 0.12`, scaled per event and by fatigue, plus a velocity kick of 0.1 units/s in a random direction every 1 to 2 seconds. Use sim time, never the clock.\n\n**Feel targets** (these numbers give them, by numeric simulation at 60 ticks/s): full stick reaches 90% in about 0.4 s with about 5% overshoot, like a body. Release settles in about 0.45 s. Left alone, the dot wanders at a mean radius of 0.05, at most 0.08. A held full lean does not tip by itself; a gust on top of it does.\n\n**Input shaping** (in `pav_app`, passed as `InputFrame.lean`, screen space):\n- **Stick:** deadzone 0.12, response curve `x^1.5` so small motions are fine.\n- **Keyboard:** keys move the target at 1.6 units/s and it returns at 1.2 units/s when released. Tapping gives small nudges, so keys feel native, not bang-bang.\n- **Mouse:** cursor offset from the screen centre divided by 0.38 of the window height, clamped to the disc. No pointer lock. The device moved last wins.\n\n**Body:** the figure tilts with the dot (`cob * 14` degrees about the feet, engine change in section 14). Beyond |cob| 0.75 an upper-body arm-flail clip fades in. A tip plays a stumble and, over water, a splash. Tips never end the game; they cost time or score.\n\n**HUD, the Puck:** a large circular gauge drawn in egui: a pale disc, a green target ring, a coral dot, and stars at the edge when streaking. It must read from 10 feet. It looks good at 340 px diameter at 1080p (verified). Put it top centre or bottom centre, whichever does not cover the figure in that event.\n\n## 5. Events\n\n**Common frame:** event card (name, one-sentence goal, glyph prompts, one coach line), 3-2-1, play, result (score 0 to 1000, stars at 400, 650 and 850, a deadpan Title, minutes banked, personal best, difference from Yesterday You; Retry or Back).\n\n**Every event has:** a section of tunable numbers in `rules.toml`, a bot that earns at least 2 stars, an idle-input outcome below 1 star, a ghost lane, and an attract segment. Scenes `fit/event/<name>` start an event directly, for tools and tests.\n\n### Stillness Studio (Posey). Set: `studio`, a round white deck on a calm dawn lagoon. Camera: mirror view (yaw 0, tilt 12, distance 8.5, fov 36; the figure faces +Z, toward the camera, and stick right is screen right).\n\n**Breath Bloom** (45 s). Hold Action to inhale, release to exhale, following a guide ring: 4 s in, 4 s out, 5 cycles, the last one longer. `lungs` rises while held and falls when not. Keep the dot inside a centre ring of radius 0.35. Tick score: `0.7 * (1 - clamp(|lungs - guide| / 0.35)) + 0.3 * inRing`. Each good cycle opens a lotus on the water with a rising pentatonic chime; a perfect run blooms the whole pond. Scrub the clip `FIT/Breath` by `lungs`. No fail state. Bot: holds while the guide rises.\n\n**Pose Parade** (3 poses, 20 s each). Six hand-keyed poses with deadpan names: the Patient Heron, the Apologetic Lunge, the Tired Lighthouse, the Folded Deck Chair, the Reluctant Bridge, Seated Disappointment. Day 1 uses the first three. Posey holds the pose beside you. A target ring (radius 0.30 shrinking to 0.18) drifts on a slow Lissajous path (amplitude 0.35, 0.12 Hz). Inside the ring a streak multiplier climbs x1 to x4, one step per 2 s; leaving resets it. At 12 s of pose 2 a gull lands on your head and wobble is x1.6 for 5 s (\"There is a bird on you. Accept the bird\"). A tip breaks the pose for 1.5 s. Score: time in ring weighted by multiplier. Bot: PD toward the ring centre.\n\n### Iron Gazebo (Big Kettle). Set: `gazebo`, a white iron gazebo at golden hour. Camera: 3/4 front.\n\n**Tempo Squats** (10 reps, about 50 s). Hold Action to go down (2 s to full depth), release to rise (1 s). A guide bar shows the tempo; a low bell marks the bottom. Keep the dot in a band |x| < 0.25; wobble grows 8% per rep. Rep score: `0.7 * timing + 0.3 * band`. Scrub `FIT/Squat` by depth. Gag: rep 10 is followed by \"Ten. Also eleven.\" Bot: follows the guide.\n\n**Plank Standoff** (up to 60 s). Hold Brace and keep the dot in a ring shrinking from 0.40 to 0.20. Releasing, or leaving the ring for more than 1 s, collapses you in a comic flop. Fatigue ramps wobble; at 30 s add tremble; at 45 s Kettle laughs at his own joke and the nudge shakes the screen. Score: seconds survived / 60. Stars at 25, 40 and 55 s. Kettle, who has no arms, plank-talks you through it. Base the pose on one frame of `MESH2MOTION/Pushup`. Bot: survives at least 45 s.\n\n### Boardwalk (Bounce). Set: `boardwalk`, a beach boardwalk at bright midday.\n\n**Step Party** (64 s, 96 BPM, song 4). A rhythm game: notes in two lanes fall to two footprints, left, right or both, on an aerobic step box. Perfect within 55 ms, Good within 120 ms. About 100 notes, data in `charts.toml`, starting with quarter notes and building to eighths and doubles. Bounce bounces on the beat and guests clap on downbeats. Timing uses the audio clock (section 10). Camera: mirror view, slightly high. Bot: presses exactly on each note.\n\n**Floatie Spin** (50 s). Circle the lean (stick, mouse, or rolling W-D-S-A) to spin inflatable rings around your hips. Spin speed is the smoothed angular velocity of the lean while |lean| > 0.4; the sweet band is 6 to 9 rad/s, and a `spin_band_scale` rule widens it for keyboard. \"Switch!\" flips the required direction every 15 s. Guests toss new rings from left or right: press that side's step within 0.25 s of arrival to catch it. Out of band, rings sink; on the floor they are lost. Maximum 7 rings. Score: rings times time in band. Rings are no-physics entities positioned in code. Bot: 7.5 rad/s circle, presses on arrivals.\n\n**Morning Lap** (about 90 s, one lap of the hub island). Alternate left and right steps to set your pace (1.6 to 2.4 steps/s is the zone). Too fast raises a stitch meter that makes you stumble; too slow and Bounce, the pacer rolling ahead, gets away. The path steers you; lean moves you up to 1.2 m sideways to dodge crabs, sunbathers and towels and to grab ribbons. Flip-flops can be found here too. Score: time in zone, plus ribbons, minus bumps. Camera: chase with per-tick yaw. Use `MESH2MOTION/Jog` scaled to speed. Bot: 2 steps/s, steers to ribbons.\n\n### Lagoon (Commodore Gull). Sets: `tide`, `channel`, `pier`, `tower`.\n\n**Tide Table** (3 boards, 60 s total). You stand on a floating square raft and your lean tilts it. Roll hermit crabs in shells into tide pools. Board 1: 3 shells. Board 2: 5 shells and a moving pool. Board 3: 7 shells, bumpers and a rising tide. Fast shells skip over pools. Write the shell physics as simple 2D code (`a = tilt * g - friction * v`, wall bounce 0.5), not rapier: it is more tunable and bot-friendly. Score: shells potted plus time left. Camera: high 3/4 (tilt 62). Bot: PD steering of the nearest shell toward the nearest pool.\n\n**Paddle Slalom** (about 45 s). Stand on a paddleboard on a long channel and pass buoy gates. Lean x steers. Lean forward speeds up and risks tipping, lean back brakes. Gusts, shown as ripple streaks, push the dot. A tip is a big splash and a 2 s remount. A missed gate adds 2 s. `score = clamp((1.6 * par - t) / (0.8 * par)) * 1000`. Standing on water uses the trick in section 15; a silent `Wake` event every few ticks draws the wake. Camera: chase (tilt 22, distance 10). Bot: steers to gate centres at forward lean 0.5.\n\n**Tray Trek** (about 50 s). Walk a long pier at a fixed pace, carrying a tray with a stack of 5 smoothies. Waves, plank gaps and swooping gulls jolt the tray. Your dot tilts it. Glasses slide with tilt and plop into the sea past the edge. Score: 200 per glass delivered, plus a no-spill bonus. Marjorie receives what is left and comments. Use `STYLE100/Balance_Walk` plus an upper-body `FIT/CarryTray` clip. Bot: counters the jolts it knows are coming.\n\n**Cannonball Cup** (3 dives, about 40 s). The board bounces with a 1.2 s period. Press Action at the bottom of 3 bounces to build power, the 4th press leaps. In the air, hold Action to tuck and lean to rotate. Enter tucked and high for the biggest splash. Three gull judges hold up cards: \"6.5\", \"7\", \"See me\". \"We are not here for form. We are here for splash.\" Score: height x tuck x timing. Camera: side view (yaw 90, tilt 6, distance 14). The splash must be huge: a new `BigSplash` event scales the water dents and particles. This is the attract mode's hero shot. Bot: presses on bottoms, tucks at the apex.\n\n### The Big Stand (finale, about 2.5 minutes). Set: `bay`, a tiny post in the bay at sunset, with the whole cast watching from rafts.\n\nFive phases, reusing event code with new numbers:\n1. Breathing, 4 cycles.\n2. A pose under rising gusts, 20 s.\n3. Step Party for 16 bars with a marching band of guests, wobble on.\n4. Brace while waves crash, 20 s.\n5. **The Long Stillness:** 30 s of nothing. Music fades to silence, the HUD vanishes except the Puck. At 15 s a fake prompt offers \"Press Cross to skip\". Pressing anything forfeits the Inner Peace bonus. Then Pip, quietly: \"...Oh. You're still here. Good.\"\n\nA tip drops you in the sea to a groan from the crowd and puts you back; it costs score and cannot end the run. Final Balance Age = morning age minus `final_score / 100` (up to 10).\n\n### Morning Wobble Check. Set: `studio`. About 70 s, four micro-tests, Pip presiding.\n\n| Test | What you do | Metric (0 to 1) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Stand Still (\"This is the whole test\") | Hold the dot centred for 8 s; one small nudge at 5 s | Mean distance from centre |\n| Lean Targets | A left/right bar: reach \"70% left\", then two more targets, within 6%, hold 1.5 s; 5 s limit each | Time taken |\n| Eyes Closed | 6 s. The screen dims to almost black, the Puck vanishes. A tone's pitch tells your offset, and rumble if the pad has it | Mean distance |\n| Step Test | 8 alternating steps to a 100 BPM metronome | Timing |\n\n```\nskill = 0.30*still + 0.25*targets + 0.25*blind + 0.20*steps\nage   = 24 + 56 * (1 - skill)^1.1 - 2*days_completed - min(total_stars/3, 8)\n```\nClamp to 18..99, round. A middling player (skill 0.5) starts at 50 and reaches about 34 by Day 5; a weak one (skill 0.2) starts at 68 and ends near 52, before the finale's bonus. The big number rolls like a slot machine. Pip's comment is chosen by the change since yesterday and by the worst metric. A sparkline of 5 big dots shows the week. Your figure's posture improves as the age falls (a small constant forward slump through the tilt field, shrinking each day): visible progress, no numbers needed.\n\n## 6. Meta systems\n\n- **Minute Clam:** a giant clam at reception that gulps banked minutes with a gibberish burp. Totals unlock wardrobe items.\n- **Calendar:** five big days, a stamp per completed day, then real days in free play. No tables.\n- **Titles:** after each event Pip awards a deadpan title by score: Human Soup, Acceptable Human, Certified Lean-To, Wobble Enthusiast, Seasoned Tilter, Stillness Intern, Professional Standing Person, Alarmingly Balanced. At least 30, in `script.toml`.\n- **Wardrobe:** reuse the engine's `GearLook`, which needs no new drawing (verified): `helm = cap` (sun cap), `helm = hood` (towel turban), `crown`, `halo`; `gloves` (sweatbands), `belt`, `pauldrons` (reads as arm floaties, funny). Plus shirt, pants and shoe colours. Skip `cape`: it draws long sticks.\n- **Lost flip-flops:** 5 hidden on the island, for Two-Towel Tom. Reward: Golden Flip-Flops (gold shoes) and a line. This is the exploration layer.\n- **Yesterday You:** your best run of each event is recorded and replayed as a tinted figure in a neighbouring lane, from Day 3.\n- **Absence comments:** the page passes today's date to the game at boot, and the save stores the last day played. \"You were away for 2 days. I did not count them. There were 2.\" Passing the date in as data keeps the rule that the sim never reads the clock.\n- **Saves:** versioned JSON in `localStorage`: guest slots (name, look, day, minutes, stars, bests, ghosts, ages, flip-flops, unlocks) and global settings. Save on every change of day and every result.\n\n## 7. World, cast and writing\n\n**Tippy Cay** is about 64 x 48 m: reception at the centre (Pip's desk, Calendar wall, Minute Clam), a ring path for jogging, four pavilions around it, a row of cabanas, a pier, a diving tower and a water channel in the distance. Palms, grass, sand terraces, sea on all sides, circling gulls.\n\n| Character | What it is | Voice and manner |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Pip** | Sky-blue round wobble cushion, two dot eyes (`blob` plan, scale 0.7, squash 2.0, plus a small valve) | Front desk and scorekeeper. Relentlessly pleasant. Keeps records of everything. Never technically insults you. Squeaky rubber voice |\n| **Posey** | Faceless wooden artist's mannequin (biped with eyes the colour of its skin; verified look in section 8) | Stillness. Serene, short, oddly poetic. Soft wood-block voice. It has no eyes and never blinks; \"This has not been discussed\" |\n| **Big Kettle** | Cast-iron kettlebell (dark `blob` plus a torus handle part; add a `Handle` attach kind) | Strength. Booming, gentle, deeply supportive. No arms or legs, cannot do any exercise |\n| **Bounce** | Huge pink exercise ball that never stops hopping (`blob`, scale 1.2, `hop`) | Cardio. Breathless bursts, no full stops |\n| **Commodore Gull** | Small gull in a captain's cap: three no-physics entities, wings rotated in code | Lagoon. Dry, officious, steals snacks |\n| **Marjorie** | Guest in robe and towel turban (`helm = hood`, white) | On Day 5 for eleven years. Knows everything |\n| **Two-Towel Tom** | Guest with two towels | Lost his flip-flops. Asks you to find them |\n| **The Twins** | Two identical guests | Do everything in unison, finish each other's words |\n\n**Writing style.** Short polite sentences. Upbeat. Then one line too honest. Fitness facts of doubtful use. Numbers quoted precisely, for no reason. At most 2 lines on screen at 10 feet. Every coach has at least 25 lines, Pip at least 80, guests about 8 each, per day where it matters. Keep all text in `script.toml`.\n\nTone anchors, all original. Use these and write more like them:\n- Pip: \"Welcome! You have won a complimentary stay. You did not enter. Nobody enters.\"\n- Pip: \"Please stand on me. Gently. I remember everything.\"\n- Pip: \"Your Balance Age today is 61. That is a number. Numbers cannot hurt you. This one is trying.\"\n- Pip: \"You leaned left 64% of the time. Is everything all right on the right?\"\n- Pip: \"That was your best attempt so far. I am as surprised as you are.\"\n- Pip: \"You wobbled 41 times. I stopped counting at 40, out of respect.\"\n- Pip: \"Did you know? Standing still burns calories. Not many. Did you know that, though?\"\n- Pip, on a long pause: \"You have been paused for 4 minutes. Pausing is not an exercise. I checked.\"\n- Posey: \"Breathe in the sea. Not literally.\"\n- Posey: \"Be the heron. The heron does not check the score.\"\n- Big Kettle: \"Lift with your legs. I cannot. I have none. Lift for both of us.\"\n- Bounce: \"Keep going keep going keep- is that your heartbeat? Mine is just air!\"\n- Commodore Gull: \"That was a dive. I am legally required to say so.\"\n- Marjorie: \"Day five? Oh, I'm on day five as well. Eleven years now.\"\n\nDialogue types out with voice blips. Action completes the line, then advances. Keep a Text Speed setting.\n**Route: egui in `pav_ui`, painter-drawn, no default windows.** This was verified at 1920x1080: rounded fonts, soft-shadow cards and painted glyphs look right and appear in headless `pav capture`. Keep all UI state in the sim (section 14), so tests can drive it.\n\n**Fonts:** `npm pack @expo-google-fonts/fredoka` and `@expo-google-fonts/nunito` (SIL OFL, static TTFs). Unpack into their own folder and copy `Fredoka_600SemiBold.ttf` (titles, 50 KB) and `Nunito_700Bold.ttf` (body, 132 KB) to `engine/crates/pav_ui/fonts/`. Embed with `include_bytes!`. Credit them on the About screen.\n\n**Rules:** at 1080p, body text at least 34 px and titles at least 64 px. Scale everything by `min(w/1920, h/1080)`, so it also works in small hub frames. Cards are white with radius 36. Focus is a thick teal outline, scale 1.05 and a soft bounce, with a sound on every move. At most 6 items visible. No tables, no dense stats, at most 4 numbers on a screen, and the About screen is pages, not a scrolling wall. Everything works by pad alone. Keyboard and mouse use the same screens. Hover moves focus, and click activates.\n\n**Glyphs:** draw them with the painter. PlayStation by default (Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, L1/R1/L2/R2 pills, sticks, D-pad); a Settings option swaps to Xbox (A B X Y, LB RB LT RT). Keyboard: keycaps with labels. Mouse: a small mouse with the button lit. One function `prompt(action, device, xbox) -> glyph`. Prompts change the instant the device changes. Hide the cursor when the pad is in use.\n\n| Screen | Content |\n|---|---|\n| Title | Logo in Fredoka over the island sweep, 4 options |\n| Guest select, wardrobe | Big cards, live figure on a turntable |\n| Dialogue | Bottom card, speaker name, 2 lines, advance glyph |\n| Island HUD | Day and minute goal top left, Balance Age top right, a world-anchored prompt on the nearest interactable |\n| Schedule | Carousel of pavilions, then events, with stars. Fast travel |\n| Event HUD | Puck, score, timer, one prompt row |\n| Result | Score, stars, title, minutes, best, Retry or Back |\n| Check report | Giant rolling number, sparkline, Pip's comment |\n| Calendar | Five big days and stamps |\n| Pause | Resume, Schedule, Calendar, Wardrobe, Settings, How to Play, About, Dev Mode, Quit to Title |\n| Settings | Music (default 10%), SFX, Voices, Glyphs, Lean Sensitivity, Wobble Assist, Rhythm Offset, Text Speed, Fullscreen, Reset Save (with confirm) |\n| About | Pages for each block your brief requires (section 18) |\n| Play Together | Choose 2 to 4 guests, pass-the-pad interstitial, podium |\n\n**Mouse in the world:** on the island `InputFrame.aim` already holds the cursor's ground point. The nearest interactable within 1.2 m of it gets a highlight ring; clicking walks there with `NavGrid::path`, then interacts. Clicking open ground walks there.\n\n**Touch-only devices:** detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')`, no `(any-pointer: fine)`, and no gamepad or key seen yet. Show a centred card \"Controller or keyboard required\" and a Settings button (tap works; Settings is usable by tap). No touch controls: skip Shardfall's `touch.draw` for this game, and route touches directly to egui in `on_touch`, because the engine's touch layer otherwise treats a finger as a stick. Attract mode runs behind the card. Remove the phone-rotation hint and fullscreen-on-tap from `web/index.html`. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, drop the card and start normally. A touch device without WebGPU cannot run the game at all, so the page's own fallback message there says both things: \"Controller or keyboard required\" and that the game needs WebGPU.\n\n**Dev Mode** (from Pause, not shown in hub sessions). Big rows, pad-navigable, in tabs:\n- **Jump:** any day, any event, any finale phase, attract, medley.\n- **Cheats:** no tips, autoplay with the bot, give minutes, unlock all, all stars, skip dialogue, win or lose this event now.\n- **Time:** scale 0.25x to 4x, pause, single step (`TimeControl`).\n- **Tuning:** live sliders, generated from `impl Tunable for Rules` with `params::list` and `params::set`, grouped by core and by event, with **Reset to Defaults** per group and for all. Must include: stiffness, damping, wobble, tip time, stick curve, key rates, each event's main difficulty number, rhythm windows, spin band, gust strength, bounce gain, Big Stand gusts.\n- **View:** input viewer, dot trace, engine stats overlay, free camera, ghost lanes.\n- **Save:** reset this guest.\n\n## 12. Attract mode\n\nAfter 10 seconds without input on the title or pre-game menus (600 ticks), loop: island sweep 8 s, then about 15 s each of Cannonball Cup, Paddle Slalom, Step Party, Pose Parade, Tide Table, Floatie Spin, Tray Trek, Plank Standoff, Morning Lap, Big Stand, then the title card 5 s. The bot plays with `demo = true`: no tips, no failures, nothing saved. A \"DEMO\" ribbon and \"Press any button\" show on screen. Any input exits to the title: any key, button, stick beyond 0.3, mouse click or mouse move over 6 px (`InputFrame.any`). Touch-only devices keep it running.\n\nUse the same event code with the bot replacing input in `pre`. No separate replay system.\n\n## 13. Multiplayer\n\n**AI Hub session: mode `ghost`, 1 to 4 players.** Follow `lib/hub/README.md` in `michaelcrosato/ai-hub`. `ghost` is the choice because seeing friends wobble on the next mat is the fun of it, and it is barely more work than `parallel`; `shared-world` would need a host-run world this game does not need. Download `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` to `hub/`; these URLs work without auth (verified).\n\n**The round, the Inter-Resort Medley:** Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Cannonball Cup, one after another, about 2 minutes, then final score = sum of the three event scores (0 to 3000), reported as `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })`. The same seed on every copy gives the same course. On a copy, other players appear as seat-coloured figures with their names in the same event: in another lane or on a neighbouring raft or board. They affect nothing. Use the hub's own card: do not pass `card: true`.\n\nIn a session there is no title, menu or attract. The game opens straight into the round. Pause shows only Resume and Settings; the world keeps running, because the hub's clock does. Quit, restart and dev mode do not exist there.\n\n**Order in the `<head>` of `web/index.html`:** `<meta charset>`, the client, the tags, the `about-data` block (section 14), then the JS below.\n```html\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>/* session.js pasted byte for byte */</script>\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Highest total across three balance events wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Act: Cross, Space or click\">\n<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n```\n\n**Hub logic lives in about 30 lines of plain JS in the page; Rust only reads and writes window fields.** This exact block passed the harness on a real engine build at 2 players, at 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, and with `scenario=host-leave`, in 14 to 19 s each, and the page ran clean outside a session (verified):\n\n```js\n(() => {\n  const boot = window.__gameBoot = { scene: null, seed: null, today: Math.floor(Date.now() / 86400000),\n                                     about: document.getElementById('about-data')?.textContent ?? '' };\n  if (!window.AIHub || !AIHub.active) return;\n  const hub = window.__hub = { go: false, ended: false, players: [], me: 0, ghosts: {} };\n  boot.scene = 'fit/medley';\n  boot.seed = Number((/[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(location.search) || [])[1] || 1);\n  AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4] }).then((info) => {\n    if (!info) { location.replace(location.pathname); return; }   // no hub after all\n    if (!navigator.gpu) { AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU'); return; }\n    hub.me = info.me; hub.players = info.players;\n    // Before the first status arrives, report a zero: the hub must always hear a number.\n    const status = () => { try { return JSON.parse(window.__gameStatus || 'null')?.hub ?? null; } catch { return null; } };\n    const waitReady = () => (window.__gameStatus ? AIHub.ready() : setTimeout(waitReady, 50));\n    waitReady();\n    let reported = false;\n    const report = () => { if (reported) return; reported = true; const s = status(); AIHub.result({ score: s?.score ?? 0, stats: s?.stats ?? {} }); };\n    setInterval(() => {\n      if (AIHub.time() < 0 || hub.ended) return;\n      hub.go = true;\n      const s = status();\n      AIHub.progress({ score: s?.score ?? 0, label: s?.label ?? 'Warming up' });\n      if (!reported) AIHub.send(s?.ghost ?? { area: -1 }, { reliable: false });\n      if (s?.done) report();\n    }, 100);\n    AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => { hub.ghosts[from] = data; });\n    AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => { delete hub.ghosts[id]; });\n    AIHub.on('time-up', report);\n    AIHub.on('end', () => { hub.ended = true; });\n  });\n})();\n```\nThe game's status JSON carries `hub: { score, label, done, stats, ghost }`. Rust passes `__hub.go` to the sim as a button bit, draws `__hub.ghosts`, and stops input and sound on `__hub.ended`. The JS timers keep reporting while software rendering runs slowly, so the checks pass at low frame rates.\n\n**Ghost drawing.** Append extra `RenderObject`s to clones of `prev` and `curr` before `builder.build` in `App::frame`, with a high id per seat and `PuppetFrame { state, feet_offset, def: Some(look), rig: None, tint: Some((seat_rgb, 0.55)) }`; copy how `Sim::frame` builds a character's object. The sim never sees hub ghosts, so it stays deterministic. Local ghosts (Yesterday You, Play Together) come from the sim's own save data and are appended in `Sim::frame`, through the same helper, so captures show them. Names are egui text projected above the head; never insert hub names as HTML. Ghost JSON: area (event index), position, facing, lean, clip id, clip time, score. Only draw a ghost whose area matches yours. 10 messages/s stays under the 20/s limit.\n\n**The game on its own.** `AIHub.active` is false and nothing above runs. `Math.random` stays the browser's own. The hub's solo check opens the page, presses Enter and Space, and looks for errors and a drawn screen. Multiplayer exists here too, on one device:\n- **Play Together:** 2 to 4 local guests take turns through the same Medley on one pad. A pass-the-pad card between turns, earlier players' runs as ghosts in the other lanes, and a podium at the end.\n- **Yesterday You:** the same ghost pipeline replays your own best run.\n\nThese reuse the hub's ghost drawing and scoring, so there is one multiplayer system with three sources of ghosts.\n\n## 14. Architecture\n\n**Decision: all game state and flow live in the sim, in one `Game`.** Menus, dialogue, pause, settings values and dev toggles are state in `FitGame`, driven by `InputFrame`, so `cargo test` can play the whole game with no browser or GPU in seconds. `pav_ui` is a pure view of a `UiFrame`: it draws the frame, and returns what the pointer hovered and clicked, which the app sends back as `InputFrame.ui` (clear PRIMARY that frame if the UI took the click) and publishes as item rects in `window.__gameUi` for browser tests. Pause freezes the world by an early return in `Sim::step_inner`, not by `TimeControl`.\n\n```\nengine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/\n  mod.rs           FitGame: Flow state machine, Game impl, build(), scene routing\n  core.rs          BalanceCore\n  intent.rs        InputFrame to per-event intent\n  events/*.rs      one file per event, dispatched through an enum (Clone + serde)\n  check.rs finale.rs medley.rs meta.rs dialog.rs ghost.rs attract.rs ui_model.rs\n  rules.toml       every balance number (hot-reloads via level_text)\n  script.toml      all text\n  charts.toml      Step Party notes\n  sets/*.toml      hub studio gazebo boardwalk tide channel pier tower bay\nengine/anim/fit.json                 hand-keyed clips\nengine/assets/props/lib/core/*.json  props\nengine/crates/pav_ui/src/fit_ui.rs, glyphs.rs, fonts/\nengine/crates/pav_audio/src/music.rs, voice.rs\nengine/crates/pav_app/src/weblink.rs  window field reads and writes\nengine/web/index.html                 hub client, tags, JS, about-data\ntests/  tools/  hub/  notes/  README.md  (how to add an event, set or song)\n```\nRegister it as `entry::<fit::FitGame>(..., fit::build)`, `KEY = \"fit\"`. Scene names: `fit`, `fit/medley`, `fit/event/<name>`. Read data with `games::level_text(\"fit/rules\", include_str!(\"rules.toml\"))`: running from `engine/`, it reads the disk file, so text, numbers and set layouts change with no rebuild. Do not put sets in `engine/rooms/`: that folder feeds the pavilion demo.\n\n--- RUST HOOK ---\nuse anyhow::{Result, anyhow};\nuse glam::Vec2;\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\nuse serde_json::json;\n\nuse super::{Game, GameBox};\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\nuse crate::room::RoomDef;\nuse crate::sim::Sim;\n\nconst LEVEL: &str = include_str!(\"fit.toml\");\n\n#[derive(Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct FitGame {\n    pub center: Vec2,\n    pub velocity: Vec2,\n    pub elapsed: f32,\n    pub stable: f32,\n}\n\nimpl Default for FitGame {\n    fn default() -> Self {\n        Self { center: Vec2::ZERO, velocity: Vec2::ZERO, elapsed: 0.0, stable: 0.0 }\n    }\n}\n\nimpl FitGame {\n    pub fn advance(&mut self, lean: Vec2, dt: f32) {\n        self.elapsed += dt;\n        let wobble = Vec2::new((self.elapsed * 1.7).sin(), (self.elapsed * 1.3).cos()) * 0.12;\n        let target = lean.clamp_length_max(1.0) * 0.92 + wobble;\n        let acceleration = (target - self.center) * 40.0 - self.velocity * 8.5;\n        self.velocity += acceleration * dt;\n        self.center += self.velocity * dt;\n        if self.center.length() < 0.32 {\n            self.stable += dt;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\npub fn build(sim: &mut Sim, _rest: Option<&str>) -> Result<()> {\n    let def = RoomDef::parse(&super::level_text(FitGame::KEY, LEVEL)).map_err(|error| anyhow!(\"fit.toml: {error}\"))?;\n    crate::scenes::build_standalone_room(sim, FitGame::KEY, def);\n    sim.state.play = Some(GameBox::new(FitGame::default()));\n    Ok(())\n}\n\nimpl Game for FitGame {\n    const KEY: &'static str = \"fit\";\n\n    fn pre(&mut self, _sim: &mut Sim, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32, _events: &mut Vec<crate::frame::SimEvent>) -> std::collections::BTreeMap<crate::entity::EntityId, InputFrame> {\n        self.advance(input.move_dir, dt);\n        std::collections::BTreeMap::new()\n    }\n\n    fn status(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> serde_json::Value {\n        json!({ \"center\": [self.center.x, self.center.y], \"elapsed\": self.elapsed, \"stable\": self.stable })\n    }\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n\n    #[test]\n    fn balance_stays_finite_and_follows_input() {\n        let mut game = FitGame::default();\n        for _ in 0..120 {\n            game.advance(Vec2::X, 1.0 / 60.0);\n        }\n        assert!(game.center.x > 0.7 && game.center.x < 1.1);\n        assert!(game.center.is_finite());\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn center_resting_is_stable() {\n        let mut game = FitGame::default();\n        for _ in 0..120 {\n            game.advance(Vec2::ZERO, 1.0 / 60.0);\n        }\n        assert!(game.stable > 1.9);\n    }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_583","type":"agent_message","text":"Built a playable **prototype**, but it does **not** fully implement `PLAN.md`. The visible game uses Canvas 2D and JavaScript rather than the planned engine-native 3D simulation; several island systems and event mechanics remain incomplete.\n\nOpen `Wii Fit Together-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-222701.html:1`. Remaining work is recorded in `PROGRESS.md:1`; the required interview is in `exit-interview.json:1`.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:27:01; source: Wii Fit; plan: `PLAN.md`; genre: sports and wellness minigames; perspective: illustrated third-person scenes.\n- Tech: Shardfall `49ef2ba`, Rust, WebAssembly, WebGPU, Canvas 2D, JavaScript, and AI Hub. Art: pastel tropical resort; animation: procedural Canvas 2D.\n- Audio: synthesized music, effects, and chimes; online: AI Hub ghost medley. Research: engine source/docs and AI Hub client/harness.\n- Testing: 13 browser/Hub checks, 24 viewport launches, and two Rust tests. Environment: Codex CLI, Linux; model: OpenAI gpt-6.1-terra, max reasoning; usage: added on import.\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Testing caught at least five issues. One critical startup bug was fixed; separately, WebGPU lost its device after the first frame under headless SwiftShader, so the engine renderer remains unverified on hardware.\n- The viewport sweep and scripted full stay were most helpful; isolated spring tests were least helpful for end-to-end coverage. Real iOS Safari was not tested.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Shardfall’s game registration and standalone scene were useful starting points. The hardest part was integrating the full game into its native simulation.\n- I added a game registration, island scene, and balance spring; the visible interface, activity rules, saves, and multiplayer flow were built separately. A complete custom-game example with browser UI and observable state would help.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- The detailed design and packaging instructions were valuable. The scope was difficult to prioritize, particularly the full activity set and online integration; explicit required milestones and permitted simplifications would help."}}
